window.DS3_CHUNK("items",[{"id":"aldrich-faithful-item","kind":"item","name":"Aldrich Faithful","page":"Aldrich Faithful (item)","img":"assets/img/Aldrich_Faithful__item.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Equip to join the Aldrich Faithful covenant.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":null,"desc":"The holy symbol of the Cathedral of the Deep, and crest of those who see beyond fire to the age of deep waters. Equip to pledge oneself to the Aldrich Faithful covenant.\nThe faithful ensure that Aldrich, Devourer of Gods, remains undisturbed, by taking the form of loyal spirits and hunting down those who would trespass the ruined cathedral.\nSummoning takes place automatically while this is equipped.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a>. Obtained by interacting with <a data-e=\"archdeacon-mcdonnell\">Archdeacon McDonnell<\/a>'s remains in the Water Reserve and accepting to join the <a data-e=\"aldrich-faithful\">Aldrich Faithful<\/a> covenant.<\/p><p>From the <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Pontiff Sulyvahn<\/a> bonfire, proceed through the level and make way to the opposite side of the big courtyard with several dead Giant Slaves. Enter the building at the end and hit the wall on the left to reveal a hidden ladder. Climb down and defeat the two Sulyvahn's Beasts lurking at the bottom. Once done, head to the far-left corner of the room to find <a data-e=\"archdeacon-mcdonnell\">McDonnell<\/a>'s remains.<\/p>","use":"<p>Equip to pledge oneself to the <a data-e=\"aldrich-faithful\">Aldrich Faithful<\/a> covenant. Summoning takes place automatically while this item is equipped.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Aldrich_Faithful_(item)"},{"id":"alluring-skull","kind":"item","name":"Alluring Skull","page":"Alluring Skull (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Alluring_Skull__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Attracts nearby foes when thrown. Does not work on all enemies.","buy":800,"sell":10,"held":10,"desc":"A skull resplendent in the scent of souls.\nPrepared by evangelists of the Cathedral of the Deep.\nThrow to shatter, spreading souls which attract enemies. Not effective for all foes.","avail":"<p><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><\/p><ul><li>×6 are sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> once she has been given the <a data-e=\"morticians-ashes\">Mortician's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"unbreakable-patches\">Unbreakable Patches<\/a> for 800 souls each.<ul><li>Sold by the Shrine Handmaid for the same price once she has been given <a data-e=\"patches-ashes\">Patches' Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul><p><a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a><\/p><ul><li>×2 on a corpse being devoured by two Starved Hounds behind a broken carriage near the beginning of the area.<\/li><li>×2 on a corpse lying behind a small house guarded by two Starved Hounds. The house is opposite to the entrance to the sewers, across the stone bridge in the area with three Hollow Manservants.<\/li><\/ul><p><a data-e=\"catacombs-of-carthus\">Catacombs of Carthus<\/a><\/p><ul><li>Dropped by the Skeleton mage that controls the first boulder after descending the big staircase.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Alluring Skulls crash upon impact after being thrown, releasing an attracting mist that draws the attention of most enemies toward its location. Most enemies will hover around or attack the mist for a short time giving the player time to flee or attack them.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Alluring_Skull_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"ashen-estus-flask","kind":"item","name":"Ashen Estus Flask","page":"Ashen Estus Flask","img":"assets/img/Ashen_Estus_Flask.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Restores lost FP upon use (reusable).","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Undead treasure these dull ashen flasks.\nFill with Estus at bonfires, and drink to restore FP.\nQuite befitting of an Unkindled, an Ashen Estus Flask turns a bonfire's heat cold.","avail":"<p>Found at the beginning of the game in the <a data-e=\"cemetery-of-ash\">Cemetery of Ash<\/a>, on a corpse lying on the remains of the central fountain.<\/p>","use":"","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Ashen_Estus_Flask"},{"id":"basin-of-vows","kind":"item","name":"Basin of Vows","page":"Basin of Vows","img":"assets/img/Basin_of_Vows.webp","sub":"Key item","usage":"Place on the statue of the beheading knight to summon the Dancer of the Boreal Valley.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Chalice used in old ceremony in which Lothric Knights take their vows. It is only a formality now, but it remains as an empty practice.\nPlace this basin at the statue of a beheading knight.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">High Wall of Lothric<\/a><ul><li>Automatically added to the player's inventory once <a data-e=\"emma-high-priestess-of-lothric-castle\">Emma, High Priestess of Lothric Castle<\/a> dies as part of the storyline<\/li><li>Dropped by Emma if the player kills her.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Approaching the beheading statue behind Emma's chair with the Basin of Vows in hand will trigger the <a data-e=\"dancer-of-the-boreal-valley\">Dancer of the Boreal Valley<\/a> fight.<\/p><p>Once the Dancer has been defeated, interacting with the beheading statue will place the basin in front of it, triggering a cutscene that unlocks access to <a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Basin_of_Vows"},{"id":"binoculars","kind":"item","name":"Binoculars","page":"Binoculars (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Binoculars__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Zoom in on distant scenery.","buy":null,"sell":300,"held":1,"desc":"Binoculars made of brass.\nUse to peer at distance scenery.\nTheir utility is singular, but applications many. The value of these specs depends greatly on the imagination of their owner.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">High Wall of Lothric<\/a>. From the initial bonfire, head towards the dragon corpse and onto the battlements above. It can be found on a corpse at the top.<\/p>","use":"<p>Use the binoculars to peer into the distance: to gaze upon aesthetic views or to plan a route of attack.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Binoculars_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"black-bug-pellet","kind":"item","name":"Black Bug Pellet","page":"Black Bug Pellet","img":"assets/img/Black_Bug_Pellet.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Boosts Dark damage absorption for 60 seconds.","buy":1500,"sell":200,"held":5,"desc":"Medicinal pellet made from crushed insects.\nThe black type temporarily boosts Dark damage absorption.\nAt all times, the Abyss Watchers of the Undead Legion keep a supply of these concoctions, prepared by the acolytes. Rumor has it their Ghru descendants still make these concoctions.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 1,500 souls each once she is given the <a data-e=\"dreamchasers-ashes\">Dreamchaser's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><li>Dropped by Ghrus in <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Boosts Dark damage absorption by 15% for 60 seconds, 10% in PvP.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Black_Bug_Pellet"},{"id":"black-eye-orb","kind":"item","name":"Black Eye Orb","page":"Black Eye Orb (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Black_Eye_Orb__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Use to invade Leonhard in Anor Londo.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Arcane orb left on Rosaria's corpse.\nHave faith her soul can be retrieved, by invading the world of her killer, and returning victorious.\nThe Black Eye is proof of vengeance, but often appears serene as it casts its gaze toward Irithyll.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a>. The player must first join <a data-e=\"rosarias-fingers\">Rosaria's Fingers<\/a> and offer at least one <a data-e=\"pale-tongue\">Pale Tongue<\/a> to rank up in the covenant. The player must then talk to <a data-e=\"ringfinger-leonhard\">Ringfinger Leonhard<\/a>, who will appear at the entrance of <a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Rosaria's Bed Chamber<\/a>.<\/p><p>Once the player reaches <a data-e=\"anor-londo\">Anor Londo<\/a> and defeats <a data-e=\"aldrich-devourer-of-gods\">Aldrich, Devourer of Gods<\/a>, the orb can be found on the now-dead body of <a data-e=\"rosaria-mother-of-rebirth\">Rosaria<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Used to invade <a data-e=\"ringfinger-leonhard\">Leonhard<\/a> in the room above the <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Aldrich, Devourer of Gods<\/a> bonfire (Gwynevere's chamber in <i>Dark Souls<\/i>). Upon defeating him in his world, the player will obtain the <a data-e=\"soul-of-rosaria\">Soul of Rosaria<\/a>, the <a data-e=\"crescent-moon-sword\">Crescent Moon Sword<\/a> and his Silver Mask.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Black_Eye_Orb_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"black-firebomb","kind":"item","name":"Black Firebomb","page":"Black Firebomb (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Black_Firebomb__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Explodes, inflicting great fire damage.","buy":300,"sell":100,"held":10,"desc":"More powerful bisque filled with special black powder. Explodes, inflicting great fire damage.\nFire damage, which differs from physical damage, is highly effective against creatures of flesh, beasts, and other foes that might naturally have cause to fear the flame.","avail":"<ul><li>Selectable as a Burial Gift.<\/li><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"unbreakable-patches\">Unbreakable Patches<\/a> for 300 souls each.<\/li><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> once she has been given <a data-e=\"patches-ashes\">Patches' Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><li>Can be found in the <a data-e=\"consumed-kings-garden\">Consumed King's Garden<\/a>.<\/li><li>3 can be found above a Wing Knight in the <a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">High Wall of Lothric<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Throw it at the enemy to deal great Fire damage (compared to the <a data-e=\"firebomb\">Firebombs<\/a>).<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Black_Firebomb_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"black-molotov-cocktail","kind":"item","name":"Black Molotov Cocktail","page":"Black Molotov Cocktail (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Black_Molotov_Cocktail__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"-","buy":null,"sell":null,"held":null,"desc":"","avail":"","use":"","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Black_Molotov_Cocktail_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"black-separation-crystal","kind":"item","name":"Black Separation Crystal","page":"Black Separation Crystal (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Black_Separation_Crystal__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Online item","usage":"Returns the player or summoned players to their world.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":99,"desc":"A charm of farewell granted to banished Undead. The crystal sends phantoms back to their homes, or you back to yours.\nBeware the fickle use of this item if you intend to nurture relations.","avail":"<p>Default equipment for all classes.<\/p>","use":"<ul><li>When used as a Host of Embers, the player can send any allied phantom back to their own world.<\/li><li>When used as a phantom of any type, the player will return to their own world.<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Black_Separation_Crystal_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"blade-of-the-darkmoon-item","kind":"item","name":"Blade of the Darkmoon","page":"Blade of the Darkmoon (item)","img":"assets/img/Blade_of_the_Darkmoon__item.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Equip to join the Blade of the Darkmoon covenant.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":null,"desc":"A silver pendant depicting the Darkmoon and a sword, the crest of the Darkmoon Knights, the original Blue Sentinels. Equip to pledge oneself to the Blade of the Darkmoon covenant.\nWhen a member of the Way of Blue faces a dark spirit, the Blades of the Darkmoon, by an ancient accord, help to root out the invader.\nSummoning takes place automatically when equipped.","avail":"<p>The pendant is received from <a data-e=\"company-captain-yorshka\">Company Captain Yorshka<\/a> upon joining the <a data-e=\"blade-of-the-darkmoon\">Blade of the Darkmoon<\/a> covenant in <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a>.<\/p><p>From the <a data-e=\"anor-londo\">Anor Londo<\/a> bonfire, proceed to the spiraling staircase (it must remain in its topmost position), go downstairs and exit by the lowermost part. A <a data-e=\"anor-londo\">prison tower<\/a> will be visible in the distance and to the right.<\/p><p>Walk straight forward into the void, revealing the existence of an invisible bridge that leads to the tower. <a data-e=\"company-captain-yorshka\">Captain Yorshka<\/a> can be found here, and the player may join her covenant if they have the &quot;Darkmoon Loyalty&quot; gesture. By performing the gesture for Yorshka within her dialogue menu, the player may receive the covenant item as proof of joining the covenant.<\/p>","use":"<p>Equip to pledge oneself to the <a data-e=\"blade-of-the-darkmoon\">Blade of the Darkmoon<\/a> covenant. Summoning takes place automatically while this item is equipped.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Blade_of_the_Darkmoon_(item)"},{"id":"blessed-gem","kind":"item","name":"Blessed Gem","page":"Blessed Gem","img":"assets/img/Blessed_Gem.webp","sub":"Upgrade material","usage":"Used in infusion to create Blessed weapons.","buy":null,"sell":300,"held":99,"desc":"A gem of infused titanite. Commonly known as a charm kept by saints.\nUsed in infusion to create blessed weapons.\nSpecial blessed weapons gradually restore HP and heavily damage reanimated foes.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><ul><li>One can be obtained once per playthrough by trading the <a data-e=\"moaning-shield\">Moaning Shield<\/a> with the <a data-e=\"nestling\">Nestling<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">High Wall of Lothric<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Winged Knights.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Evangelists.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Road of Sacrifices<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Corvian Storytellers.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Evangelists.<\/li><li>On a corpse on the rafters leading to <a data-e=\"rosaria-mother-of-rebirth\">Rosaria, Mother of Rebirth<\/a>. The corpse is located at the far wall, guarded by a <a data-e=\"cathedral-knight-greatsword\">greatsword<\/a>-wielding Cathedral Knight.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by the one Evangelist.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Lothric Priests.<\/li><li>Dropped by Winged Knights.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Corvian Storytellers.<\/li><li>Dropped by Gertrude's Knights.<\/li><li>On a corpse found along the rafters after dropping down from Gertrude's bird cage.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a><ul><li>Found on a corpse at the base of the rotting tower in the abandoned village guarded by Millwood Knights, on the outside near the cliffside.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Hobbled Clerics.<\/li><li>Found on a corpse in the <a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">Shared Grave<\/a> area, below where <a data-e=\"amnesiac-lapp\">Amnesiac Lapp<\/a>'s questline concludes.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Grants Faith scaling to any innate Physical, Fire, Lightning and Dark damage, or increases any prior Faith scaling, but reduces Strength and Dexterity scaling, along with reducing base damage considerably.<\/p><p>When wielded, the player slowly regenerates health at a rate of 3 HP every 4 seconds (0.75 HP per second or 45 HP per minute). Reinforcing it will reduce the tick interval by 0.25 seconds per upgrade level. At +10 reinforcement, a Blessed weapon will replenish 3 HP per 1.5 seconds, (2 HP per second or 120 HP per minute).<\/p><p>Weapons with the Blessed infusion will deal 20% bonus damage to skeletal creatures (e.g., most foes within <a data-e=\"catacombs-of-carthus\">Catacombs of Carthus<\/a>). Killing an enemy with a blessed weapon also prevents them from reviving.<\/p><p>If infused onto a shield, its damage absorption will drop 5% across the board, and stability will be reduced to base value (e.g., will not increase with upgrades).<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Blessed_Gem"},{"id":"blood-gem","kind":"item","name":"Blood Gem","page":"Blood Gem","img":"assets/img/Blood_Gem.webp","sub":"Upgrade material","usage":"Used in infusion to create lacerating weapons.","buy":null,"sell":300,"held":99,"desc":"A gem of infused titanite.\nSlurped by Irithyll slaves.\nUsed in infusion to create lacerating weapons.\nSuch weapons inflict lacerating damage.\nMost effective with sharp or spiked weapons.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Irithyllian Slaves.<\/li><li>Found in the area after the dark room filled with Irithyllian Slaves, at the base of a tree guarded by more Irithyllian Slaves before entering the riverbed.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a><ul><li>Found at the bottom of the rotted basement of Ariandel Chapel, guarded by numerous Giant Flies.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>The player must obtain the <a data-e=\"profaned-coal\">Profaned Coal<\/a> and give it to Andre of Astora to allow infusion of this gem into a weapon.<\/p><p>Use the Blood Gem to infuse a weapon with the Bleed effect. The infusion will reduce base physical damage and scaling, while adding or increasing Bleed buildup, which scales with Luck.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Blood_Gem"},{"id":"bloodred-moss-clump","kind":"item","name":"Bloodred Moss Clump","page":"Bloodred Moss Clump (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Bloodred_Moss_Clump__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Reduces bleeding build-up.","buy":500,"sell":50,"held":99,"desc":"Red moss clump used as maggot repellent.\nReduces bleeding build-up.\nBleeding builds up when attacked by sharp blades or spikes, and once triggered causes severe damage. Use this moss clump before it reaches this point.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"greirat-of-the-undead-settlement\">Greirat<\/a> while in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> for 500 souls.<\/li><li>If Greirat dies, the player can obtain <a data-e=\"greirats-ashes\">Greirat's Ashes<\/a> and provide them to the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> to increase her stock allowing for the purchase of these clumps.<\/li><li>Common drop by the Lesser Crabs in the <a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Road of Sacrifices<\/a> marshes.<\/li><li>Rare drop from Grave Wardens found in the <a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Bloodred Moss Clumps are used to remove Bleed buildup. They can also remove the maggot debuff from the player's body.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Bloodred_Moss_Clump_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"blooming-purple-moss-clump","kind":"item","name":"Blooming Purple Moss Clump","page":"Blooming Purple Moss Clump (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Blooming_Purple_Moss_Clump__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Reduces Poison and Toxic. Cures ailments.","buy":1000,"sell":100,"held":99,"desc":"Potently medicinal purple moss clump with a flower.\nReduces poison and toxin. Cures ailments.\nA toxin is a more vicious form of poison which quickly leads to death.\nMoss clumps without blooms are useless against toxin, and those who neglect to carry this flowered variety are simply courting an early demise.","avail":"<ul><li>Initially four are sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 1,000 souls each once she has been given the <a data-e=\"paladins-ashes\">Paladin's Ashes<\/a>.<ul><li>The Shrine Handmaid's stock is upgraded to infinite once she is given the <a data-e=\"excrement-covered-ashes\">Excrement-covered Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li>Three on the wooden scaffolding at the toxic swamp with Sewer Centipedes in the <a data-e=\"profaned-capital\">Profaned Capital<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>The Blooming Purple Moss Clump will both reduce the build-up of, and cure, Toxic and Poison.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Blooming_Purple_Moss_Clump_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"blue-bug-pellet","kind":"item","name":"Blue Bug Pellet","page":"Blue Bug Pellet","img":"assets/img/Blue_Bug_Pellet.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Boosts Magic damage absorption for 60 seconds.","buy":1500,"sell":200,"held":5,"desc":"Medicinal pellet made from crushed insects.\nThe blue type temporarily boosts magic damage absorption.\nThe Boreal Valley is infested with moon bugs, meaning ingredients are never far from hand for the Irithyllian slaves who concoct this medicine.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 1,500 souls each once she is given the <a data-e=\"excrement-covered-ashes\">Excrement-covered Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><li>In the <a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Road of Sacrifices<\/a>, near <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a>, two Blue Bug Pellets can be found on a broken staircase.<\/li><li>Dropped by Irithyllian Slaves in <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Boosts Magic damage absorption by 15% for 60 seconds, 10% in PvP.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Blue_Bug_Pellet"},{"id":"blue-sentinels-item","kind":"item","name":"Blue Sentinels","page":"Blue Sentinels (item)","img":"assets/img/Blue_Sentinels__item.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Equip to join the Blue Sentinels covenant.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":null,"desc":"Faded sheepskin parchment depicting the Darkmoon and a sword. Equip to pledge oneself to the Blue Sentinels covenant.\nWhen a member of the Way of Blue is threatened by a dark spirit, the Blue Sentinels, in compliance with an ancient accord, assume the form of blue spirits, and help to root out the invader.\nSummoning takes place automatically while this is equipped.","avail":"<ul><li>Gift from <a data-e=\"horace-the-hushed\">Horace the Hushed<\/a> by talking to him at the <a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Halfway Fortress<\/a> or <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a>.<\/li><li>Dropped by Horace if he is killed at any point.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Equip to pledge oneself to the <a data-e=\"blue-sentinels\">Blue Sentinels<\/a> covenant. Summoning takes place automatically while this item is equipped.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Blue_Sentinels_(item)"},{"id":"braille-divine-tome-of-carim","kind":"item","name":"Braille Divine Tome of Carim","page":"Braille Divine Tome of Carim","img":"assets/img/Braille_Divine_Tome_of_Carim.webp","sub":"Spell book","usage":"Give to Irina to learn advanced Carim miracles.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"A sacred braille tome from Carim, filled with advanced miracles.\nGive to a storyteller to learn advanced Carim miracles.\nIn the Way of White, there is a tradition of placing great faith in the words of the blind, and braille tomes are not unusual.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Road of Sacrifices<\/a>.<\/p><p>From the <a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Road of Sacrifices<\/a> bonfire, drop from the ledge behind the first Corvian Storyteller. Continue onward until reaching a bridge with another Storyteller at the end and several Corvians scattered about. Drop by the right side before crossing and to a small ledge below, then follow the narrow path until reaching a cave guarded by two Festering Starved Hounds. The tome can be found on a corpse inside, along with another one that holds <a data-e=\"mornes-ring\">Morne's Ring<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Given to <a data-e=\"irina-of-carim\">Irina of Carim<\/a> in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> unlocks the following miracles:<\/p><table><tr><th>Available<\/th><th>Item<\/th><th>Cost<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"force\">Force<\/a><\/td><td>1,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"med-heal\">Med Heal<\/a><\/td><td>3,500<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"tears-of-denial\">Tears of Denial<\/a><\/td><td>10,000<\/td><\/tr><\/table>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Braille_Divine_Tome_of_Carim"},{"id":"braille-divine-tome-of-lothric","kind":"item","name":"Braille Divine Tome of Lothric","page":"Braille Divine Tome of Lothric","img":"assets/img/Braille_Divine_Tome_of_Lothric.webp","sub":"Spell book","usage":"Give to Irina to learn Lothric miracles.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"A sacred braille tome from Lothric, filled with miracles for use by knights.\nGive to a storyteller to learn Lothric miracles.\nIt is said that no paladin inside Lothric castle could fall, owing to the divine protection they enjoyed.","avail":"<p>The tome is located in <a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a>. From the Dragon Barracks bonfire the player can proceed through the area until they reach the <a data-e=\"dragonslayer-armour\">Dragonslayer Armour<\/a> fog wall. Before entering, head to the left, dropping down to the platform containing one of the Lothric Wyverns. The tome is in the room behind it.<\/p>","use":"<p>Given to <a data-e=\"irina-of-carim\">Irina of Carim<\/a> will unlock the following miracles:<\/p><ul><li><a data-e=\"blessed-weapon\">Blessed Weapon<\/a><\/li><li><a data-e=\"bountiful-light\">Bountiful Light<\/a><\/li><li><a data-e=\"magic-barrier\">Magic Barrier<\/a><\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Braille_Divine_Tome_of_Lothric"},{"id":"budding-green-blossom","kind":"item","name":"Budding Green Blossom","page":"Budding Green Blossom","img":"assets/img/Budding_Green_Blossom.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Large temporary boost to Stamina recovery speed.","buy":null,"sell":100,"held":10,"desc":"Green flower-shaped weed with small white blooms.\nLarge temporary boost to stamina recovery speed.\nFlowers of the Green Blossom are ethereal, blossoming only on the surface of chilled, but not frozen, water.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Sewer Centipedes.<\/li><li>On a corpse by the fountain with several Irithyllian Slaves and the first Fire Witch.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><ul><li>A unique version of this item, with a different description, is sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 10 souls after defeating <a data-e=\"aldrich-devourer-of-gods\">Aldrich<\/a> and while following <a data-e=\"sirris-of-the-sunless-realms\">Sirris<\/a>'s questline.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a><ul><li>Three are found outside of the Corvian Settlement. After taking the ice slide, take the left-side path up an incline and down some drop-downs.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a><ul><li>Two are found on a corpse shortly after the stairs heading down from the Mausoleum Lookout bonfire, in the grass on the left.<\/li><li>Two more are found on a corpse next to the stairs leading up to the first Judicator Giant.<\/li><li>Three are found on a corpse to the left of the path leading up the Halflight, Spear of the Church arena, across from the <a data-e=\"spears-of-the-church\">Divine Spear Monument.<\/a><\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Increases Stamina regeneration by +9.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Budding_Green_Blossom"},{"id":"captains-ashes","kind":"item","name":"Captain's Ashes","page":"Captain's Ashes","img":"assets/img/Captain_s_Ashes.webp","sub":"Merchant ashes","usage":"Shrine Handmaid will prepare new items","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Umbral ash of the Captain of the Millwood Knights. With this, the Shrine Handmaiden will prepare new items.\nLong ago, when the Millwood Knights lost the forest they called home, they began a journey so long that even thoughts of their sworn enemy washed away, replaced by a vision of a cold and brittle wood.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a>. At the top of the tower in the ruined Millwood village guarded by several Millwood Knights, along with two Millwood archers. The ashes can be found on a corpse at the very top of the tower.<\/p>","use":"<p>Extends the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a>'s inventory to include the following items:<\/p><table><tr><th>Available<\/th><th>Item<\/th><th>Cost<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"titanite-scale\">Titanite Scale<\/a><\/td><td>20,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>3<\/td><td><a data-e=\"refined-gem\">Refined Gem<\/a><\/td><td>5,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td>Millwood Knight Helm<\/td><td>5,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td>Millwood Knight Armor<\/td><td>8,500<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td>Millwood Knight Gauntlets<\/td><td>5,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td>Millwood Knight Leggings<\/td><td>5,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"millwood-greatarrow\">Millwood Greatarrow<\/a><\/td><td>800<\/td><\/tr><\/table>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Captain's_Ashes"},{"id":"carthus-pyromancy-tome","kind":"item","name":"Carthus Pyromancy Tome","page":"Carthus Pyromancy Tome","img":"assets/img/Carthus_Pyromancy_Tome.webp","sub":"Spell book","usage":"Give to Cornyx to learn advanced pyromancies.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"A pyromancy tome from Carthus containing pyromancies crafted for battle.\nGive to the old master pyromancer to learn advanced pyromancies of the Carthus.\nCarthus pyromancies developed in isolation from other forms, explaining their divergent evolution.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"catacombs-of-carthus\">Catacombs of Carthus<\/a>. After crossing the long bridge at the beginning of the level, jump off the left side near the end of the bridge. At the end of the short hall will be the tome.<\/p>","use":"<p>Give the tome to <a data-e=\"cornyx-of-the-great-swamp\">Cornyx of the Great Swamp<\/a> to unlock the following pyromancies in his stock of wares:<\/p><table><tr><th>Quantity<\/th><th>Item<\/th><th>Cost<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"acid-surge\">Acid Surge<\/a><\/td><td>6,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"carthus-beacon\">Carthus Beacon<\/a><\/td><td>8,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"carthus-flame-arc\">Carthus Flame Arc<\/a><\/td><td>10,000<\/td><\/tr><\/table>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Carthus_Pyromancy_Tome"},{"id":"carthus-rouge","kind":"item","name":"Carthus Rouge","page":"Carthus Rouge","img":"assets/img/Carthus_Rouge.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Temporarily applies bleeding effect to right-hand weapon.","buy":1000,"sell":100,"held":5,"desc":"Highly vicious scarlet plant secretions.\nTemporarily applies bleeding effect to right-hand weapon.\nAssociated with the warriors of Carthus, whose blades take on the scarlet hues of both this sanguine substance and the spatters of their victims' blood.","avail":"<p><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><\/p><ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 1,000 souls each after she is given the <a data-e=\"grave-wardens-ashes\">Grave Warden's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><p><a data-e=\"catacombs-of-carthus\">Catacombs of Carthus<\/a><\/p><ul><li>Dropped by Skeletons and Skeleton Swordsmen.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Adds 20 Bleed build-up to right-hand weapon for 60 seconds. A Blood Loss proc will inflict an additional 100 damage if the threshold was crossed by the build-up from a Carthus Rouge buffed weapon.<\/p><p>The build-up increase scales with the Luck of the wielder, increasing up to to 26 build-up at 50 Luck.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Carthus_Rouge"},{"id":"cell-key","kind":"item","name":"Cell Key","page":"Cell Key","img":"assets/img/Cell_Key.webp","sub":"Key item","usage":"Unlocks Greirat's cell in the High Wall of Lothric.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":99,"desc":"Key to a cell holding thieves and the like.\nThe is no shortage of brash thieves in Lothric, and these particular thieves likely scaled the wall from the Undead Settlement.\nBut they are only willing to practice their thievery on the High Wall, for their fear of Lothric Castle, rumored to devour men, keeps them clear of its grounds.","avail":"<p>From the <a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">Tower on the Wall<\/a> bonfire, head downstairs and drop down a level. Proceed through an arch to the outside rooftops with the Pus of Man. Take the ladder down and enter the room with the <a data-e=\"lothric-knight-long-spear\">spear<\/a>-wielding Lothric Knight. Make way past the knight and find a room with several Large Hollow Soldiers and two Starved Hounds. The key can be found at the bottom of a small staircase, in a corner guarded by one of the hounds.<\/p>","use":"<p>Unlocks <a data-e=\"greirat-of-the-undead-settlement\">Greirat<\/a>'s cell below the <a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">Tower on the Wall<\/a> bonfire.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Cell_Key"},{"id":"champions-bones","kind":"item","name":"Champion's Bones","page":"Champion's Bones","img":"assets/img/Champion_s_Bones.webp","sub":"Key item","usage":"Burn at the Firelink Shrine bonfire to access Undead Matches.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"The charred but warm bones of a champion.\nLong ago, an Undead declared a fight. A fight to celebrate their undeath, and so to preserve what remained of their souls. So it was that the Undead Matches were born. The merit of an Undead is measured in deaths. Could there be a greater gift for such a creature, than a fight that has no end?","avail":"<ul><li>Dropped by <a data-e=\"champions-gravetender-and-gravetender-greatwolf\">Champion's Gravetender and Gravetender Greatwolf<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><ul><li>Obtained by completing <a data-e=\"amnesiac-lapp\">Amnesiac Lapp<\/a>'s questline, or dropped by Lapp upon death, if it has not been obtained by defeating the Gravetender and Greatwolf.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>The player may burn them at the <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> bonfire in order to access Undead Matches.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Champion's_Bones"},{"id":"chaos-gem","kind":"item","name":"Chaos Gem","page":"Chaos Gem","img":"assets/img/Chaos_Gem.webp","sub":"Upgrade material","usage":"Used in infusion to create Chaos weapons.","buy":null,"sell":500,"held":99,"desc":"A gem of infused titanite.\nRelics of lands scorched by the Chaos Flame.\nUsed in infusion to create chaos weapons.\nChaos weapons inflict fire damage, and scale with intelligence and faith.","avail":"<p><a data-e=\"smouldering-lake\">Smouldering Lake<\/a><\/p><ul><li>Found at the end of a cave located within the area's main cavern, guarded by several Great Crabs.<\/li><li>Dropped by Demon Clerics.<\/li><li>Dropped by the Crystal Lizard closest to the destructible floor that leads from the lake to the Old King's Antechamber bonfire.<\/li><\/ul><p><a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a><\/p><ul><li>Dropped by a Crystal Lizard in the room after the first wax pool.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Infuses weapons with Fire damage, adding Intelligence and Faith scaling but reducing Strength and Dexterity scaling, as well as reducing base damage. Intelligence and Faith scaling will also be increased for any pre-existing Magic, Lightning and Dark damage.<\/p><p>For the Fire damage, scaling soft caps at 30 Intelligence and 30 Faith.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Chaos_Gem"},{"id":"charcoal-pine-bundle","kind":"item","name":"Charcoal Pine Bundle","page":"Charcoal Pine Bundle","img":"assets/img/Charcoal_Pine_Bundle.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Quickly applies fire to right-hand weapons.","buy":300,"sell":100,"held":20,"desc":"A small bundle of charcoal pine resin.\nQuickly applies fire to right-hand weapons.\nDoes not last for long, but can be used in inventive ways, such as applying it in the middle of a series of blows.","avail":"<ul><li>Bundles can be found throughout gameplay as loot and as drops from enemies; most notably the Peasant Hollows in the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a>.<\/li><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 300 souls each, once she is given the <a data-e=\"morticians-ashes\">Mortician's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Unlike resins, which require the user to remain stationary while applying the buff, bundles take less than a second to activate and can be used while moving. While they grant more damage than their respective resins and many more bundles can be carried at once, the trade-off is that the duration of the buff is reduced to less than 20% of that of a resin.<\/p><p>The quick application time, high stock and low duration of these items makes them very flexible tools, useful for applying in the midst of combat based on the situation. Whereas a resin may find a large fraction of its duration wasted from inactivity between attacks, a bundle may be quickly activated when an opportunity to deal damage presents itself, and the advantage pressed until the buff expires. This includes, in particular, the short duration of vulnerability between parrying a foe and taking the riposte.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Charcoal_Pine_Bundle"},{"id":"charcoal-pine-resin","kind":"item","name":"Charcoal Pine Resin","page":"Charcoal Pine Resin (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Charcoal_Pine_Resin__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Temporarily applies fire to right-hand weapons.","buy":500,"sell":100,"held":5,"desc":"Black charcoal-like pine resin.\nTemporarily applies fire to right-hand weapons.\nUsed in the Undead Settlement to preserve Undead bodies after dissection, and to bury them.","avail":"<ul><li>Along with <a data-e=\"charcoal-pine-bundle\">Charcoal Pine Bundles<\/a>, the resins can be looted upon discovery or dropped/farmed from Peasant Hollows located in the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a>.<\/li><li>Can be purchased from the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 500 souls each, once she is given the <a data-e=\"morticians-ashes\">Mortician's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Charcoal_Pine_Resin_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"church-guardian-shiv","kind":"item","name":"Church Guardian Shiv","page":"Church Guardian Shiv","img":"assets/img/Church_Guardian_Shiv.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Projects illusory blades which seek targets.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"This special throwing blade has a flat tip, and is wielded by guardians of the Church of Filianore.\nConsume FP to project illusory blades which seek their targets.\nGuardians of the Church, of whom few remain, watch over Princess Filianore's eternal slumber along with the Spears of the Church.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a>. From the Ringed City Streets bonfire, head out into the swamp. Head all the way to the back end where there is a chapel of sorts surrounded by praying Hobbled Clerics. It is located inside.<\/p>","use":"<p>Inflicts 40 Thrust damage, scaling with the player's Strength and Dexterity. Knives do not stagger the target but can be thrown very quickly.<\/p><p>Each Shiv consumes 9 FP when thrown, and will slightly home in on targets that are locked on.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Church_Guardian_Shiv"},{"id":"cinders-of-a-lord","kind":"item","name":"Cinders of a Lord","page":"Cinders of a Lord","img":"assets/img/Cinders_of_a_Lord.webp","sub":"Key item","usage":"Place on the Abyss Watchers' throne in Firelink Shrine.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":99,"desc":"Cinders of a lord left by the Abyss Watchers.\nIf the lords will not return to their thrones themselves, let them return as cinders.\nThe Watchers of the Abyss swore upon their shared wolf's blood, which also served as their mandate as lords.","avail":"<p>There are four cinders to be obtained in the game, each belonging to a Lord of Cinder.<\/p><ol><li>Obtained by defeating the <a data-e=\"abyss-watchers\">Abyss Watchers<\/a> in the <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a>.<\/li><li>Obtained by defeating <a data-e=\"yhorm-the-giant\">Yhorm the Giant<\/a> in the <a data-e=\"profaned-capital\">Profaned Capital<\/a>.<\/li><li>Obtained by defeating <a data-e=\"aldrich-devourer-of-gods\">Aldrich, Devourer of Gods<\/a> in <a data-e=\"anor-londo\">Anor Londo<\/a>.<\/li><li>Obtained by defeating <a data-e=\"lorian-elder-prince-and-lothric-younger-prince\">Lothric<\/a> in the <a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a>.<\/li><\/ol>","use":"<p>When all cinders have been placed at their respective thrones in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a>, the player gains access to the <a data-e=\"kiln-of-the-first-flame\">Kiln of the First Flame<\/a>, where they can confront the <a data-e=\"soul-of-cinder\">Soul of Cinder<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Cinders_of_a_Lord"},{"id":"coiled-sword","kind":"item","name":"Coiled Sword","page":"Coiled Sword","img":"assets/img/Coiled_Sword.webp","sub":"Key item","usage":"Ignites the bonfire in Firelink Shrine.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Sword missing from the shrine bonfire. Cannot be equipped as a weapon. Thrust into the shrine bonfire to restore its power and enable travel between bonfires.\nThis sword is only bequeathed to chosen ash, as judged by the Iudex, who awaits the arrival of ash as a scabbard.","avail":"<p>Obtained after defeating <a data-e=\"iudex-gundyr\">Iudex Gundyr<\/a> in the <a data-e=\"cemetery-of-ash\">Cemetery of Ash<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Used to ignite the bonfire in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> and allow the player to travel between bonfires.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Coiled_Sword"},{"id":"coiled-sword-fragment","kind":"item","name":"Coiled Sword Fragment","page":"Coiled Sword Fragment","img":"assets/img/Coiled_Sword_Fragment.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Returns the player to Firelink Shrine or to the last bonfire rested at.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Fragment of the coiled sword of a bonfire which served its purpose long ago.\nReturns caster to last bonfire used for resting, or to the bonfire in Firelink Shrine.\nCan be used repeatedly.\nBonfires are linked to one another irreversibly, retaining their affinity long after their purpose is exhausted.","avail":"<p>Picked up from the extinguished bonfire inside of <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> in the <a data-e=\"untended-graves\">Untended Graves<\/a>. <a data-e=\"champion-gundyr\">Champion Gundyr<\/a> must be defeated in order to reach the shrine.<\/p>","use":"<p>Using the Coiled Sword Fragment will present the player with the option of teleporting to either <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> or to the last bonfire they rested at. Unlike <a data-e=\"homeward-bone\">Homeward Bones<\/a>, it has unlimited uses.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Coiled_Sword_Fragment"},{"id":"contraption-key","kind":"item","name":"Contraption Key","page":"Contraption Key","img":"assets/img/Contraption_Key.webp","sub":"Key item","usage":"Unlocks the attic of the archive in the Corvian Settlement.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"The key to the contraption leading to the attic of the archive found on the edge of the Corvian Settlement.\nAfter Sir Vilhelm led a white-haired woman to the attic of the library, he kept this key as if it were his life.","avail":"<p>Dropped by <a data-e=\"sir-vilhelm\">Sir Vilhelm<\/a> after defeating him in the <a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Unlocks the path leading to the attic of the archive found on the edge of the <a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Corvian Settlement<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Contraption_Key"},{"id":"cornyxs-ashes","kind":"item","name":"Cornyx's Ashes","page":"Cornyx's Ashes","img":"assets/img/Cornyx_s_Ashes.webp","sub":"Merchant ashes","usage":"Give to the Shrine Handmaid to increase her inventory.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Umbral ash of Cornyx of the Great Swamp. With this, the shrine handmaid will prepare new items.\nCornyx was tired and defeated until he discovered one final pupil, like so many pyromancers before him.","avail":"<p>Dropped by <a data-e=\"cornyx-of-the-great-swamp\">Cornyx of the Great Swamp<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Extends the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a>'s inventory to include items initially sold by <a data-e=\"cornyx-of-the-great-swamp\">Cornyx<\/a>.<\/p><table><tr><th>Available<\/th><th>Item<\/th><th>Cost<\/th><\/tr><tr><td><\/td><td><a data-e=\"acid-surge\">Acid Surge<\/a><\/td><td>6,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><\/td><td><a data-e=\"bursting-fireball\">Bursting Fireball<\/a><\/td><td>5,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><\/td><td><a data-e=\"carthus-beacon\">Carthus Beacon<\/a><\/td><td>8,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><\/td><td><a data-e=\"carthus-flame-arc\">Carthus Flame Arc<\/a><\/td><td>10,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><\/td><td><a data-e=\"chaos-storm\">Chaos Storm<\/a><\/td><td>12,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><\/td><td><a data-e=\"fire-orb\">Fire Orb<\/a><\/td><td>3,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><\/td><td><a data-e=\"fire-surge\">Fire Surge<\/a><\/td><td>1,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><\/td><td><a data-e=\"fireball\">Fireball<\/a><\/td><td>1,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><\/td><td><a data-e=\"flash-sweat\">Flash Sweat<\/a><\/td><td>1,500<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><\/td><td><a data-e=\"great-chaos-fire-orb\">Great Chaos Fire Orb<\/a><\/td><td>10,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><\/td><td><a data-e=\"great-combustion\">Great Combustion<\/a><\/td><td>3,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><\/td><td><a data-e=\"poison-mist\">Poison Mist<\/a><\/td><td>2,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><\/td><td><a data-e=\"profuse-sweat\">Profuse Sweat<\/a><\/td><td>2,000<\/td><\/tr><\/table>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Cornyx's_Ashes"},{"id":"cracked-red-eye-orb","kind":"item","name":"Cracked Red Eye Orb","page":"Cracked Red Eye Orb (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Cracked_Red_Eye_Orb__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Online item","usage":"Used to invade other worlds at will.","buy":null,"sell":10,"held":99,"desc":"Online play item.\nInvade other worlds at will.\nDefeat the Host of Embers of the world you have invaded to gain the strength of the fire.\nThe Cracked Red Eye Orb is far from perfect, it seems, as Ringfinger Leonhard knows all too well.","avail":"<ul><li>Can be chosen as a burial gift at the beginning of the game.<\/li><li><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><ul><li>Five are given for free by <a data-e=\"ringfinger-leonhard\">Ringfinger Leonhard<\/a>.<\/li><li>These are also dropped by Leonhard if he is killed at Firelink Shrine.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a><ul><li>One and up to three guaranteed drop from Darkwraiths.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Use to invade other players. Functions exactly the same as a <a data-e=\"red-eye-orb\">full Red Eye Orb<\/a>, but is consumed upon successfully entering another player's world.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Cracked_Red_Eye_Orb_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"crystal-gem","kind":"item","name":"Crystal Gem","page":"Crystal Gem","img":"assets/img/Crystal_Gem.webp","sub":"Upgrade material","usage":"Used in infusion to create Crystal weapons.","buy":null,"sell":300,"held":99,"desc":"A gem of infused titanite. Introduced to Lothric by the Crystal Sages.\nUsed in infusion to create crystal weapons.\nCrystal weapons inflict magic damage, and scale effectively with intelligence.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Road of Sacrifices<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Sage's Devout.<\/li><li>Dropped by Sage's Prentice.<\/li><li>Guaranteed drop by the Crystal Lizard within the ruins before <a data-e=\"crystal-sage\">Crystal Sage<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Large Devouts of the Deep.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Grand Archives Scholars.<\/li><li>Dropped by Thralls.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Frost Crabs.<\/li><li>One is rewarded for defeating the two initial Frost Crabs near the <a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Depths of the Painting<\/a> bonfire.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Infuses weapons with Magic damage, granting Intelligence scaling but reducing Strength and Dexterity scaling, as well as reducing base damage.<\/p><p>Scaling soft caps at 40 Intelligence.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Crystal_Gem"},{"id":"crystal-scroll","kind":"item","name":"Crystal Scroll","page":"Crystal Scroll","img":"assets/img/Crystal_Scroll.webp","sub":"Spell book","usage":"Give to Orbeck of Vinheim to learn crystal sorceries.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Secret crystal scroll of the Grand Archives of Lothric.\nGive to a sorcerer to learn crystal sorceries.\nThese sorceries are the work of the paledrake, Seath the Scaleless, whom Logan is said to have met, a branch of sorcery that has been carried on by the Crystal Sages.","avail":"<p>Dropped by the <a data-e=\"crystal-sage\">Crystal Sage<\/a> found in the <a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Give to <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a> in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> to upgrade his stock of sorceries:<\/p><table><tr><th>Quantity<\/th><th>Item<\/th><th>Cost<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"homing-crystal-soulmass\">Homing Crystal Soulmass<\/a><\/td><td>18,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"crystal-soul-spear\">Crystal Soul Spear<\/a><\/td><td>15,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"crystal-magic-weapon\">Crystal Magic Weapon<\/a><\/td><td>10,000<\/td><\/tr><\/table>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Crystal_Scroll"},{"id":"dark-arrow","kind":"item","name":"Dark Arrow","page":"Dark Arrow (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Dark_Arrow__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Ammunition","usage":"Inflict 65 Dark damage.","buy":200,"sell":3,"held":99,"desc":"Ritual arrows said to have been used by savage hunters.\nInflict dark damage.\nIt is said that these arrows scrape out death from their targets, but savages are known to tell tall tales.","avail":"<p>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 200 souls each, once she has been given the <a data-e=\"easterners-ashes\">Easterner's Ashes<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Besides inflicting Dark damage on foes, Dark Arrows have a moderate amount of homing ability, curving to chase down targets, much like <a data-e=\"affinity\">Affinity<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Dark_Arrow_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"dark-gem","kind":"item","name":"Dark Gem","page":"Dark Gem","img":"assets/img/Dark_Gem.webp","sub":"Upgrade material","usage":"Used in infusion to create dark weapons.","buy":null,"sell":500,"held":99,"desc":"A gem of infused titanite.\nBorn of disembodied humanity.\nUsed in infusion to create dark weapons.\nDark weapons inflict dark damage, and scale with faith.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">High Wall of Lothric<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Pus of Man.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"catacombs-of-carthus\">Catacombs of Carthus<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by the second Skeleton Boulder.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"consumed-kings-garden\">Consumed King's Garden<\/a><ul><li>Found on a corpse under the left set of stairs that lead to the courtyard in front of the boss room.<\/li><li>Dropped by Pus of Man.<\/li><li>Dropped by Rotten Slugs.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Pus of Man.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a><ul><li>Within the rotting house at the top of the Corvian Settlement, near the locked gate, guarded by two Giant Flies.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-dreg-heap\">The Dreg Heap<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Harald Knights<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Harald Knights<\/li><li>Found in the Ringed City Streets, shortly after the great stairway.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Infuses weapons with Dark damage, adding Intelligence and Faith scaling but reducing Strength and Dexterity scaling, as well as reducing base damage. Intelligence and Faith scaling will also be increased for any pre-existing Magic, Fire and Lightning damage.<\/p><p>For the Dark damage, scaling soft caps at 30 Intelligence and 30 Faith.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Dark_Gem"},{"id":"dark-sigil","kind":"item","name":"Dark Sigil","page":"Dark Sigil","img":"assets/img/Dark_Sigil.webp","sub":"Key item","usage":"Represents the Ashen One's level of hollowing.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":99,"desc":"A black, gaping hole in the flesh that resembles the brand of an Undead.\nThe darkness of humanity seeps from this bottomless pitch-black hole, the gap filled by the accumulation of the curse.\nThis Dark Sigil will never heal, but there is a tale told of a Fire Keeper who returned from the Abyss, and brought great comfort to a bearer of the curse.","avail":"<ul><li>Five are given to the player after letting <a data-e=\"yoel-of-londor\">Yoel of Londor<\/a> draw out their true strength, granting a free level each time. Yoel grants a session at 0, 2, 6, 12 and 15 Hollowing.<\/li><li>Three are granted during <a data-e=\"yuria-of-londor\">Yuria of Londor<\/a>'s questline, once the player completes the Rite of Avowal with <a data-e=\"anri-of-astora\">Anri of Astora<\/a> at <a data-e=\"anor-londo\">Anor Londo<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<ul><li>Increases the player's Hollowing level by the number of accumulated Sigils upon death.<\/li><li>Grants bonus Luck when wielding <a data-e=\"hollow-gem\">Hollow<\/a>-infused weapons if Hollowing is 15 or greater, based on the upgrade level of the weapon.<\/li><li>Once eight Dark Sigils are acquired, the Lord of Hollows ending may be unlocked.<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Dark_Sigil"},{"id":"darksign","kind":"item","name":"Darksign","page":"Darksign (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Darksign__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Returns the player to Firelink Shrine or to the last bonfire rested at, at the cost of losing all souls.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":99,"desc":"The Darksign is the sign of an accursed Undead.\nThe Darksign returns its bearer to the last bonfire rested at, or the bonfire at Firelink Shrine, but at the cost of all souls held.\nCarriers of the Darksign are reborn after death, and eventually lose their minds turning Hollow. And so it is they are driven from their homelands.","avail":"<p>Already included within the player's inventory at the beginning of the game.<\/p>","use":"<p>Activate to return to either <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> or to the last bonfire rested at, at the cost of losing all souls.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Darksign_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"deep-braille-divine-tome","kind":"item","name":"Deep Braille Divine Tome","page":"Deep Braille Divine Tome","img":"assets/img/Deep_Braille_Divine_Tome.webp","sub":"Spell book","usage":"Give to either Irina or Karla to learn miracles of the deep.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"A braille divine tome of the Deep, belonging to the deacons of the cathedral.\nGive to a storyteller to learn miracles of the deep.\nIntended to teach divine protection to the deacons of the deep, but later, dark tales were added to its pages, such that it is now considered a thing profane.","avail":"<ul><li>Dropped by a Mimic in the <a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a>. Once entering the cathedral by the back gate after traversing through the roofs, proceed past the first Giant Slave and go downstairs into a passage. At the end there will be a small prayer room with the mimic chest holding the tome.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Can be given to either <a data-e=\"irina-of-carim\">Irina<\/a> or <a data-e=\"karla\">Karla<\/a> to add the following to their stock of learnable miracles:<\/p><table><tr><th>Available<\/th><th>Item<\/th><th>Cost<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"deep-protection\">Deep Protection<\/a><\/td><td>4,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"gnaw\">Gnaw<\/a><\/td><td>2,000<\/td><\/tr><\/table>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Deep_Braille_Divine_Tome"},{"id":"deep-gem","kind":"item","name":"Deep Gem","page":"Deep Gem","img":"assets/img/Deep_Gem.webp","sub":"Upgrade material","usage":"Used in infusion to create deep weapons.","buy":null,"sell":300,"held":99,"desc":"A gem of infused titanite. Found in the dregs of the Cathedral of the Deep.\nUsed in infusion to create deep weapons.\nDeep weapons inflict dark damage, but lose scaling effects.\nThere is a darkness that lies beyond human ken.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Thralls.<\/li><li>Dropped by Devouts of the Deep.<\/li><li>Dropped by Deacons.<\/li><li>One is found shortly after entering the cathedral by the back door, in a small room located at the bottom of a long staircase, before the first Giant Slave. The gem lies on a balcony, just in front of an Evangelist looking outside.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Deacons.<\/li><li>One is found in the <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Water Reserve<\/a> area, in the large room with the two Sulyvahn's Beasts. This area can be reached by climbing down the long ladder concealed behind an illusory wall on the left wall of the building after the courtyard with dead Giant Slaves.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"anor-londo\">Anor Londo<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Deacons.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>In order to unlock the Deep infusion for use, the player must first give the <a data-e=\"sages-coal\">Sage's Coal<\/a> to <a data-e=\"blacksmith-andre\">Blacksmith Andre<\/a>.<\/p><p>Using a Deep Gem will infuse the target weapon with a deepened form of Dark, and in turn, will make a weapon deal both physical damage and dark damage, at an equal-split margin with one another.<\/p><p>Deep infusions also remove <i>all<\/i> scaling effects present on the weapon after infusion, much like a <a data-e=\"fire-gem\">Fire Gem<\/a> does, which means in order to achieve maximum damage on deep weapons, the player will have to fully-reinforce one.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Deep_Gem"},{"id":"divine-blessing","kind":"item","name":"Divine Blessing","page":"Divine Blessing (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Divine_Blessing__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Fully restores HP and cures all ailments.","buy":8000,"sell":1000,"held":1,"desc":"Holy water blessed by the Queen of Lothric.\nFully restores HP and cures ailments.\nThe Queen of Lothric, married to the former King Oceiros, was initially revered as a goddess of fertility and bounty. After giving birth to Ocelotte, her youngest, she quietly disappeared.","avail":"<ul><li>Can be chosen as a burial gift at the beginning of the game.<\/li><li><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><ul><li>One is sold by <a data-e=\"greirat-of-the-undead-settlement\">Greirat of the Undead Settlement<\/a> for 8,000 souls, once he returns from pillaging the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a>.<\/li><li>A second is sold for the same price if he returns safely from pillaging <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a>. Otherwise, it will be sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> once she is given <a data-e=\"greirats-ashes\">his ashes<\/a>, provided that he has at least looted the Undead Settlement.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a><ul><li>Found in the leftmost chest on the second floor of the painting room guarded by three Silver Knights.<\/li><li>Guaranteed drop from the Silver Knight in front of Gwynevere, Princess of Sunlight's painting.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a>.<ul><li>After reaching the top of the Archives and falling into the cage containing Gertrude, navigate the rafters and kill the Man-grub, then climb down the nearby ladder to find two chests, one containing a Divine Blessing.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-dreg-heap\">The Dreg Heap<\/a><ul><li>One is sold by the <a data-e=\"stone-humped-hag\">Stone-humped Hag<\/a> for 8,000 souls.<\/li><li>After encountering the first Angel, drop down to the next level and turn left, a Divine Blessing can be found in the open in the opposite direction of immediate cover.<\/li><li>At the very top of Earthen Peak, when navigating the large roots after Desert Pyromancer Zoey, drop down onto the wooden rooftops next to the fallen tower to find a Divine Blessing on a corpse.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a><ul><li>Guaranteed drop from the Judicator Giant guarding the Mausoleum Lookout.<\/li><li>Guaranteed drop from the Judicator Giant in the rooftops section before the Purging Monument.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Fully restores HP and cures Poison, Toxic, Bleed, and Frost when used, as well as reducing the build-up of each status. They can be used anywhere and by anyone, including phantoms and dark spirits. However, unlike in the previous installments, they will not reduce Curse build-up.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Divine_Blessing_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"divine-spear-fragment","kind":"item","name":"Divine Spear Fragment","page":"Divine Spear Fragment","img":"assets/img/Divine_Spear_Fragment.webp","sub":"Online item","usage":"Summons a row of upward-thrusting ritual spears.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":null,"desc":"Online play item.\nA fragment of the matching ritual spears once held by the knights of Princess Filianore.\nThese Divine Spears of gold were placed in the trusted hands of exalted Spears.\nWhen Spears of the Church face unduly treacherous foes, this allows them to draw upon former majesty, and summon a row of upward-thrusting ritual spears.","avail":"<p>Obtained as a reward for reaching Rank 2 in the <a data-e=\"spears-of-the-church\">Spears of the Church<\/a> covenant.<\/p><p>To achieve this, the player must offer 30 <a data-e=\"filianores-spear-ornament\">Filianore's Spear Ornament<\/a> to the Divine Spear Monument in the <a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">Ringed City<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Functions similarly to the <a data-e=\"ritual-spear-fragment\">Ritual Spear Fragment<\/a>, but deals twice as much damage. Shares the same active duration and cooldown time.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Divine_Spear_Fragment"},{"id":"dragon-chasers-ashes","kind":"item","name":"Dragon Chaser's Ashes","page":"Dragon Chaser's Ashes","img":"assets/img/Dragon_Chaser_s_Ashes.webp","sub":"Merchant ashes","usage":"Give to the Shrine Handmaid to increase her inventory.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Umbral ash of the fallen warrior who chose the path of the ancient dragons. With this, the shrine handmaid will prepare new items.\nWhatever it is, it is sure to grant strength to the most unrelenting warrior.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"archdragon-peak\">Archdragon Peak<\/a>.<\/p><p>From the <a data-e=\"archdragon-peak\">Great Belfry<\/a> bonfire, take the left exit. Proceed straight forward through the courtyard outside and follow a small path on the left, near the archway with the big ambush of Man Serpents. The ashes are on a corpse behind a Rock Lizard.<\/p>","use":"<p>Extends the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a>'s inventory to include the following items:<\/p><table><tr><th>Available<\/th><th>Item<\/th><th>Cost<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>6<\/td><td><a data-e=\"ember\">Ember<\/a><\/td><td>2,500<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"titanite-chunk\">Titanite Chunk<\/a><\/td><td>13,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"twinkling-titanite\">Twinkling Titanite<\/a><\/td><td>15,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"titanite-scale\">Titanite Scale<\/a><\/td><td>20,000<\/td><\/tr><\/table>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Dragon_Chaser's_Ashes"},{"id":"dragon-head-stone","kind":"item","name":"Dragon Head Stone","page":"Dragon Head Stone (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Dragon_Head_Stone__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Gain the head of a dragon and emit dragon breath.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Stone imbued with the power of the everlasting dragons, used in a secret rite by dragon worshippers.\nGain the head of a dragon and emit dragon breath, a transformation that is irreversible until death.\nThose who choose the path of the dragon strive for perfect imitation, and the dragon head rite is the first step in this grand process.","avail":"<p>Obtained upon defeating the <a data-e=\"ancient-wyvern\">Ancient Wyvern<\/a> in <a data-e=\"archdragon-peak\">Archdragon Peak<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Upon activation, the player gains the head of a dragon and is able to breathe fire. This transformation is irreversible until death.<\/p><p>The absorption values for the head piece are as follows:<\/p><ul><li>4% Magic<\/li><li>9% Fire<\/li><li>-4% Lightning<\/li><li>4% Dark<\/li><li>+15 to all status effect resistance<\/li><\/ul><p>Physical absorption remains at 0%, and all flat defenses remain penalized for the empty armor slot.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Dragon_Head_Stone_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"dragon-torso-stone","kind":"item","name":"Dragon Torso Stone","page":"Dragon Torso Stone (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Dragon_Torso_Stone__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Gain the torso of a dragon and a dragon's roar.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Stone imbued with the power of the everlasting dragons, used in a secret rite by dragon worshippers.\nGain the torso of a dragon and a dragon's roar, a transformation that is irreversible until death.\nFrom ancient times, the path of dragon worship was walked by warriors. It is said they envision Archdragon Peak in the depths of their meditation, and at times, they even hear the distant sound of the great bell at the peak.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a>, on a draconic statue looking out beyond the cliffside and performing the &quot;Path of the Dragon&quot; gesture. This is the same spot where the player may use the gesture to gain access to <a data-e=\"archdragon-peak\">Archdragon Peak<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Upon first activation, the player's body mutates into a human/dragon hybrid form, a transformation that takes several seconds of stillness and is irreversible until death. Activating the Stone afterwards causes the Ashen One to roar like a dragon, unleashing a <a data-e=\"force\">Force<\/a>-like shockwave, and buffing their AR by 10% (12.5% in PVP) for five seconds.<\/p><p>Additionally, the player's absorption values for the chest, arms and legs pieces become as follows:<\/p><ul><li>13% Magic<\/li><li>26% Fire<\/li><li>-11% Lightning<\/li><li>13% Dark<\/li><li>+45 to all status effect resistance<\/li><\/ul><p>These are compounded with the absorption values of the associated head piece, which is also equipped by default. Physical absorption remains at 0%, and all flat defenses remain penalized for empty armor slots.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Dragon_Torso_Stone_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"dragonslayer-greatarrow","kind":"item","name":"Dragonslayer Greatarrow","page":"Dragonslayer Greatarrow","img":"assets/img/Dragonslayer_Greatarrow.webp","sub":"Ammunition","usage":"Shoot with a greatbow to deal 90 damage.","buy":500,"sell":5,"held":50,"desc":"Large spear-like arrows created by the giant blacksmith of the gods.\nCan only be used with greatbows.\nThese large arrows were said to have been used by dragon hunters during the age of the gods.\nEasily pierces human flesh.","avail":"<ul><li>Five can be found on a corpse alongside a <a data-e=\"dragonslayer-greatbow\">Dragonslayer Greatbow<\/a> on a ledge in <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a>, past <a data-e=\"pontiff-sulyvahn\">Pontiff Sulyvahn<\/a>'s boss room and below the flying buttresses where the greatbow-wielding Silver Knights are posted.<\/li><li>Dropped by greatbow-wielding Silver Knights.<\/li><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"greirat-of-the-undead-settlement\">Greirat of the Undead Settlement<\/a> for 500 souls if he returns safely from pillaging Irithyll.<\/li><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> if given <a data-e=\"greirats-ashes\">Greirat's Ashes<\/a>, provided that he survived the first pillaging journey.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Dragonslayer_Greatarrow"},{"id":"dragonslayer-lightning-arrow","kind":"item","name":"Dragonslayer Lightning Arrow","page":"Dragonslayer Lightning Arrow","img":"assets/img/Dragonslayer_Lightning_Arrow.webp","sub":"Ammunition","usage":"Deal 90 Lightning damage to target.","buy":750,"sell":5,"held":50,"desc":"Large spear-like arrows enveloped in lightning created by the giant blacksmith of the gods.\nCan only be used with greatbows.\nLightning has been a weapon of dragonslayers ever since the time of Gwyn, the First Lord.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"greirat-of-the-undead-settlement\">Greirat of the Undead Settlement<\/a> for 750 souls if he returns safely from pillaging <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a>.<\/li><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> if given <a data-e=\"greirats-ashes\">Greirat's Ashes<\/a>, provided that he survived the first pillaging journey.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Dragonslayer_Lightning_Arrow"},{"id":"dreamchasers-ashes","kind":"item","name":"Dreamchaser's Ashes","page":"Dreamchaser's Ashes","img":"assets/img/Dreamchaser_s_Ashes.webp","sub":"Merchant ashes","usage":"Give to the Shrine Handmaid to increase her inventory.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Umbral ash of one who dreamt of joining the Undead Legion. With this, the shrine handmaid will prepare new items.\nIn the end, the dream chasers who wandered aimlessly in the rotted forest found a sense of fulfillment.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a>, on a corpse hanging on a window near to the <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Old Wolf of Farron<\/a>. To reach it, exit the chamber and walk along the right-hand ledge of the fortress. Climb up a staircase and hit an illusory wall before reaching the corner with the Crystal Lizard to reveal the body.<\/p>","use":"<p>Given to the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> unlocks the following items for purchase:<\/p><table><tr><th>Available<\/th><th>Item<\/th><th>Cost<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"black-bug-pellet\">Black Bug Pellet<\/a><\/td><td>1,500<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"composite-bow\">Composite Bow<\/a><\/td><td>3,500<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>3<\/td><td><a data-e=\"ember\">Ember<\/a><\/td><td>2,500<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"feather-arrow\">Feather Arrow<\/a><\/td><td>100<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>6<\/td><td><a data-e=\"gold-pine-bundle\">Gold Pine Bundle<\/a><\/td><td>600<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>3<\/td><td><a data-e=\"gold-pine-resin\">Gold Pine Resin<\/a><\/td><td>1,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"green-blossom\">Green Blossom<\/a><\/td><td>1,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"hidden-blessing\">Hidden Blessing<\/a>*<\/td><td>1,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td>Leather Armor<\/td><td>800<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td>Leather Boots<\/td><td>500<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td>Leather Gloves<\/td><td>500<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"life-ring\">Life Ring<\/a><\/td><td>1,500<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"rotten-pine-resin\">Rotten Pine Resin<\/a><\/td><td>500<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"titanite-shard\">Titanite Shard<\/a><\/td><td>800<\/td><\/tr><\/table><ul><li><ul><li>Not available should the player choose &quot;Say nothing&quot; when asked about where the ashes were found.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Dreamchaser's_Ashes"},{"id":"dried-finger","kind":"item","name":"Dried Finger","page":"Dried Finger (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Dried_Finger__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Online item","usage":"Allows to summon a third phantom, but also a second dark spirit.","buy":2000,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Online play item.\nDried finger with multiple knuckles.\nUse to strength connection to other worlds, allowing the summoning of a third phantom, but also a second dark spirit.\nAlso makes the summon of a dark spirit occur earlier. Use with caution.","avail":"<p>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> for 2,000 souls.<\/p>","use":"<p>Increases the number of maximum guest players in a Host of Embers' world from 3 to 5. Host will go from a maximum of two summons and one invader for a total of four players, to three summons and two invaders for a total of six players. In territory defender areas (Crucifixion Woods, <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a> after <a data-e=\"pontiff-sulyvahn\">Pontiff Sulyvahn<\/a>), the numbers are increased from one phantom and two invaders, to two phantoms and three invaders.<\/p><p>Using the Dried Finger will also move the host's world to the top of the invasion priority queue and reset the cooldown timer for being invaded, while also decreasing the minimum interval for subsequent invasions. As well, whenever a host-allied phantom enters the world (whether by being summoned via <a data-e=\"white-sign-soapstone\">White Sign Soapstone<\/a> or by covenant through <a data-e=\"way-of-blue\">Way of Blue<\/a>), the invasion cooldown timer is immediately reset.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Dried_Finger_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"duel-charm","kind":"item","name":"Duel Charm","page":"Duel Charm","img":"assets/img/Duel_Charm.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Nulls special area effects for a short time.","buy":500,"sell":100,"held":5,"desc":"Tool used in duels of judgment. Nulls effects of special area effects for a short time.\nAllfather Lloyd's knights lived in fear of his duels of judgment, in which verdicts were carried out by his Sword of Law.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 500 souls each after she is given the <a data-e=\"paladins-ashes\">Paladin's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Man-grubs.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Multiple of these items can prove to be very useful in PvP encounters, as they allow to prevent the use of buffs.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Duel_Charm"},{"id":"dung-pie","kind":"item","name":"Dung Pie","page":"Dung Pie (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Dung_Pie__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Turns enemy toxic, but also affects user","buy":50,"sell":1,"held":10,"desc":"Dried fecal waste material, moist on the inside.\nThrow at enemy to inflict toxin build-up, but also ups your own toxicity.\nThough the stench makes it difficult to carry on one's person, inflicting toxins on an enemy yields high damage over time. Perhaps some Undead have fond memories of waste. Or, perhaps not.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 50 souls each after she is given the <a data-e=\"excrement-covered-ashes\">Excrement-covered Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Giant Slaves (×4).<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Peasant Hollows.<\/li><li>Dropped by the Giant Slave.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Giant Slaves.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"profaned-capital\">Profaned Capital<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Monstrosities of Sin.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Throw at an enemy to inflict 65 Toxic buildup but 0 damage on the target, while also increasing Toxic buildup on self by 55.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Dung_Pie_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"easterners-ashes","kind":"item","name":"Easterner's Ashes","page":"Easterner's Ashes","img":"assets/img/Easterner_s_Ashes.webp","sub":"Merchant ashes","usage":"Give to the Shrine Handmaid to increase her inventory.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Umbral ash of an armor merchant from an eastern land. Surely the handmaid of Firelink Shrine can turn this into a few new things.\nThe merchant, a captain of a clan of hunters, was fascinated with weaponry.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a>, in the area where several Silver Knight archers are posted on the rooftops. The ashes can be found on a corpse hanging on the edge of a small ledge reached by climbing down a set of a stairs on the right-hand side.<\/p>","use":"<p>Given to the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a>, unlocks the following items for purchase:<\/p><table><tr><th>Available<\/th><th>Item<\/th><th>Cost<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"mossfruit\">Mossfruit<\/a><\/td><td>1,500<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"large-titanite-shard\">Large Titanite Shard<\/a><\/td><td>4,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"washing-pole\">Washing Pole<\/a><\/td><td>7,500<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"eastern-iron-shield\">Eastern Iron Shield<\/a><\/td><td>3,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td>Eastern Helm<\/td><td>5,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td>Eastern Armor<\/td><td>8,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td>Eastern Gauntlets<\/td><td>5,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td>Eastern Leggings<\/td><td>5,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"dark-arrow\">Dark Arrow<\/a><\/td><td>200<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"onislayer-greatarrow\">Onislayer Greatarrow<\/a><\/td><td>600<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"wood-grain-ring\">Wood Grain Ring<\/a><\/td><td>3,000<\/td><\/tr><\/table>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Easterner's_Ashes"},{"id":"ember","kind":"item","name":"Ember","page":"Ember","img":"assets/img/Ember.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Consume to enter Host of Embers mode, restoring all HP and increasing the maximum by 30%.","buy":"2,000 / 2,500 / 5,000","sell":1000,"held":99,"desc":"No Unkindled can ever truly claim the embers that burn within a champion's bosom, which is precisely what makes their yearning for warmth so keen.\nGain the strength of flame and increased max HP until death.\nWith the strength of fire, the summoning signs of Unkindled become visible, and seekers of embers can be summoned to join in co-operating. But beware, the embers may also attract invaders.","avail":"<ul><li>Reward for successfully defeating a boss in another player's world.<\/li><li>Dropped by:<ul><li>Lothric Knights<\/li><li>Lycanthropes<\/li><li>Pus of Man<\/li><li>Lothric Wyverns in <a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a> (×2 each)<\/li><li>Ringed Knights<\/li><li>Black Knights<\/li><li>Skeleton Swordsmen<\/li><li>Elder Ghru<\/li><li>Consumed King's Knight<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a>:<ul><li><a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a>:<ul><li>×3 sold for 2,500 souls each.<\/li><li>×6 sold for 2,500 souls each after giving her the <a data-e=\"dragon-chasers-ashes\">Dragon Chaser's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><li>×3 sold for 2,500 souls each after giving her the <a data-e=\"grave-wardens-ashes\">Grave Warden's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><li>×6 sold for 2,000 souls each after giving her <a data-e=\"greirats-ashes\">Greirat's Ashes<\/a> if they were found in Grand Archives.<\/li><li>×3 sold for 2,500 souls each after giving her the <a data-e=\"morticians-ashes\">Mortician's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"greirat-of-the-undead-settlement\">Greirat of the Undead Settlement<\/a>:<ul><li>×3 sold for 2,000 souls each.<\/li><li>×4 sold for 2,000 souls each after pillaging the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"unbreakable-patches\">Unbreakable Patches<\/a><ul><li>x4 sold for 5,000 souls each.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li>x1 found outside on a corpse directly above the main entrance.<\/li><li>x1 found outside on a corpse at the end of the path to the right of the entrance, guarded by a Starved Hound.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">High Wall of Lothric<\/a><ul><li>x1 drops the from the Pus of Man to the right of the High Wall of Lothric bonfire if it is allowed to fully transform before being killed. Once per game cycle.<\/li><li>×1 found on a corpse in front of the Lothric Wyvern.<\/li><li>x1 drops from the Pus of Man shortly after the Tower on the Wall bonfire if it is allowed to fully transform before being killed. Once per game cycle.<\/li><li>x2 found on corpses near the fountain with the patrolling Winged Knight.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a><ul><li>x1 found on a corpse behind the large tree with the Evangelist and large crowd of Peasant Hollows.<\/li><li>x1 found on the corpse closest to the base of the White Birch tree<\/li><li>x1 found on a corpse near the stairs leading to the <a data-e=\"curse-rotted-greatwood\">Curse-Rotted Greatwood<\/a> arena. Guarded by a Starved Hound.<\/li><li>x1 found on a corpse hanging off the side of the small arched stone bridge near the end of the area.<\/li><li>x1 found on a corpse on the bottom floor of the <a data-e=\"giant-archer-of-the-undead-settlement\">Giant Archer's<\/a> tower. Guarded by a Boreal Outrider Knight.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Road of Sacrifices<\/a><ul><li>x1 found on a corpse in front of the Corvian Storyteller near the entrance to Halfway Fortress.<\/li><li>x1 found on a corpse near a fire under the bridge that connects the building leading to the <a data-e=\"crystal-sage\">Crystal Sage<\/a> fight.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a><ul><li>x1 found on a corpse in front of a small group of non-hostile worshippers just beyond the first unlocked door to the building. Guarded by a Large Devout of the Deep hidden in the corner.<\/li><li>x1 found on a corpse behind the crossbow sniper beyond the first Giant Slave. Guarded by an Evangelist and must be accessed via a ladder in the room below.<\/li><li>x1 found on a corpse in a dead end room beneath the afore-mentioned ladder. Guarded by a Deep Accursed.<\/li><li>x1 found on a corpse overlooking the second Giant Slave.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a><ul><li>x1 found on a corpse against the Keep walls near the White Birch tree, left of the door leading out of the swamp.<\/li><li>x2 found on corpses near the Stray Demon<\/li><li>x1 found on a corpse to the right of the path shortly before the <a data-e=\"abyss-watchers\">Abyss Watchers<\/a> fight.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"catacombs-of-carthus\">Catacombs of Carthus<\/a><ul><li>x1 found on a corpse in the middle of the large staircase/bridge with the first Skeleton Boulder.<\/li><li>x1 found on a corpse behind a large hole in the floor at the end of the hallway just before the second Skeleton Boulder.<\/li><li>x1 found on a corpse in the shortcut to the room full of Skeletons. This room is designed to trap the player in for Knight Slayer Tsorig's invasion if the shortcut has not yet been opened.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"smouldering-lake\">Smouldering Lake<\/a><ul><li>x1 found on a corpse against the railing shortly after the Demon Ruins bonfire. Guarded by a Demon Cleric.<\/li><li>x1 found on a corpse in a hallway across a hole in the floor from an <a data-e=\"estus-shard\">Estus Shard<\/a>. Guarded by a Demon Statue and a Smouldering Rotten Flesh.<\/li><li>x1 found on a corpse in dead-end hall under the Old King's Antechamber bonfire. A nearby Smouldering Ghru will attempt to ambush the player from behind if not dealt with beforehand.<\/li><li>x1 found on a corpse in the lava in the room where Knight Slayer Tsorig waits. The corpse on the right holds the Ember while the corpse on the left holds <a data-e=\"sacred-flame\">Sacred Flame<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a><ul><li>x1 found on a corpse under the stairs to the left of <a data-e=\"pontiff-sulyvahn\">Pontiff Sulyvahn's<\/a> arena. Near a gate that can be opened to provide a shortcut back to the Church of Yorshka.<\/li><li>x2 found on corpses in the area with the Giant Slaves beyond Pontiff Sulyvahn's arena.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"anor-londo\">Anor Londo<\/a><ul><li>x1 found on a corpse next to the lever used to call down the rotating tower, just outside the entrance to the Darkmoon Tomb.<\/li><li>x1 rewarded for helping <a data-e=\"anri-of-astora\">Anri of Astora<\/a> defeat <a data-e=\"aldrich-devourer-of-gods\">Aldrich, Devourer of Gods<\/a> if the questline is not broken.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a><ul><li>x2 found on corpses on the ground floor in the main room, patrolled by seven Jailers.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"profaned-capital\">Profaned Capital<\/a><ul><li>x1 found in a chest in the treasury hall to the right of <a data-e=\"yhorm-the-giant\">Yhorm the Giant's<\/a> arena.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"untended-graves\">Untended Graves<\/a><ul><li>×2 sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 2,500 souls each.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"archdragon-peak\">Archdragon Peak<\/a><ul><li>x1 found on a corpse next to the Archdragon Peak bonfire.<\/li><li>x2 found on corpses within the <a data-e=\"ancient-wyvern\">Ancient Wyvern<\/a> boss arena. From the entrance, head up the stairs and take a right. Both corpses are at the end of this path.<\/li><li>x1 found on a corpse under the room containing the Great Belfry bonfire.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a><ul><li>x1 found on a corpse next to the Dragon Barracks bonfire.<\/li><li>x2 found on corpses in the area between the Lothric Wyverns.<\/li><li>x1 found on a corpse to the left of the main stairs in the room behind the portcullis.<\/li><li>x4 rewarded for defeating the two Pus of Man infesting the corpses of the Lothric Wyverns.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a><ul><li>x1 found on a corpse on the top floor, after traversing the rooftops patrolled by Gargoyles, near the <a data-e=\"undead-bone-shard\">Undead Bone Shard<\/a> and guarded by a lone Scholar.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a><ul><li>x1 found on a corpse in the same building as the <a data-e=\"forlorn-corvian-settler\">Forlorn Corvian Settler<\/a>, just before the Corvian Settlement bonfire.<\/li><li>x1 found on a corpse in the building to the left after exiting the Corvian Settlement bonfire and crossing the bridge.<\/li><li>x1 found on a corpse in the Snowy Mountain Pass area. In a small cave recessed into the rock wall to the left of the large bell, guarded by two Farron Followers.<\/li><li>x1 found on a corpse halfway down the root system between Ariandel Chapel and the Depths of the Painting bonfire. Near a Follower throwing <a data-e=\"follower-javelin\">Javelins<\/a> at the player.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-dreg-heap\">The Dreg Heap<\/a><ul><li>x5 sold by the <a data-e=\"stone-humped-hag\">Stone-humped Hag<\/a> for 2,500 souls each.<\/li><li>x1 found on a corpse around the curved lip to the right of the Stone-humped Hag.<\/li><li>x1 found on a corpse under the Within Earthen Peak Ruins bonfire.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a><ul><li>x1 found on a corpse near the stairs leading up to the first Judicator Giant, at the base of a small monument.<\/li><li>x1 found on a corpse near the Ringed Inner Wall bonfire, on the balcony next to <a data-e=\"amnesiac-lapp\">Amnesiac Lapp<\/a>.<\/li><li>x1 found on a corpse in the hidden passage halfway down the elevator next to the Ringed Inner Wall bonfire.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Ember"},{"id":"estus-flask","kind":"item","name":"Estus Flask","page":"Estus Flask (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Estus_Flask__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Restores lost HP upon use (reusable).","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"The Undead treasure these dull green flasks.\nFill with Estus at bonfires, and drink to restore HP.\nThe journey of an Undead has always traced the bonfires, and no journey of import has been made without an Estus Flask.","avail":"<p>Given to the player at the start of the game.<\/p>","use":"","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Estus_Flask_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"estus-shard","kind":"item","name":"Estus Shard","page":"Estus Shard","img":"assets/img/Estus_Shard.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Give to Andre to increase usages of the Estus Flask.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":99,"desc":"A shard soaked in Estus.\nGive to the blacksmith at the shrine to increase usages of the Estus Flask.\nIn the old days, it was rare to see an Estus Flask far from its owner, but this shard offers hope, however shattered.","avail":"<p>A total of eleven Estus Shards can be collected in a single game cycle.<\/p><table><tr><th>Shard No.<\/th><th>Directions<\/th><\/tr><tr><th><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><\/th><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><br>Purchase the <a data-e=\"tower-key\">Tower Key<\/a> from the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> and unlock the bell tower behind the shrine. Make way upstairs and onto a bridge; drop at the middle to land on the shrine's roof. Head to the front of the building and look for an open skylight; enter it and walk along the rafters to find the shard next to the <a data-e=\"nestling\">Nestling<\/a>'s secondary trading spot.<br><br>Alternatively, the shard can be collected from the very first moment one sets foot in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a>. Make your way to the bell tower and run toward the nearby tree close to the low rooftop, you will be able to walk up a small portion of the tree; jump to the right while at the highest point to land on the rooftop (many attempts may be required). From there, just look for the skylight on the front of the building and walk along the rafters until reaching the shard.<\/td><\/tr><tr><th><a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">High Wall of Lothric<\/a><\/th><\/tr><tr><td>2<\/td><td>Near the end of the level, and just before reaching the big courtyard that leads to <a data-e=\"vordt-of-the-boreal-valley\">Vordt<\/a>, there is a building inhabited by several Large Hollow Soldiers and three Starved Hounds. The shard is in plain sight, on top of a table near the <a data-e=\"cell-key\">Cell Key<\/a>.<\/td><\/tr><tr><th><a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a><\/th><\/tr><tr><td>3<\/td><td>Found at the burning tree in the big open area with several praying peasants and an Evangelist.<\/td><\/tr><tr><th><a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Road of Sacrifices<\/a><\/th><\/tr><tr><td>4<\/td><td>From the <a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Crucifixion Woods<\/a>, head toward the keep but instead of entering, follow the narrow path on the left. The shard can be found on a corner right after dropping down a ledge and before reaching two Lycanthropes resting at a campfire.<\/td><\/tr><tr><th><a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a><\/th><\/tr><tr><td>5<\/td><td>Found on an obelisk surrounded by four praying hollows just outside the <a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cleansing Chapel<\/a>.<\/td><\/tr><tr><th><a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a><\/th><\/tr><tr><td>6<\/td><td>Found in the poison swamp, on a fallen tower guarded by several Rotten Slugs. The tower lies in front of the staircase that leads to the first brazier.<\/td><\/tr><tr><th><a data-e=\"smouldering-lake\">Smouldering Lake<\/a><\/th><\/tr><tr><td>7<\/td><td><br>Found at the end of a corridor filled with several Writhing Rotten Flesh. The corridor itself is located behind an illusory wall near the <a data-e=\"smouldering-lake\">Old King's Antechamber<\/a> bonfire.<br><br>The shard can also be reached if coming from the <a data-e=\"smouldering-lake\">Demon Ruins<\/a> bonfire side by jumping over a gap on the floor. The jump is difficult to perform, though, and the player will fall down to an area filled with enemies if they don't manage to get across.<\/td><\/tr><tr><th><a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a><\/th><\/tr><tr><td>8<\/td><td>Dropped by a Mimic encountered in the first room of the second building after exiting the initial cell block.<\/td><\/tr><tr><th><a data-e=\"anor-londo\">Anor Londo<\/a><\/th><\/tr><tr><td>9<\/td><td>In a chest found in the main hall of the cathedral, along the left wall. The area is inhabited by groups of Deacons, several Writhing Rotten Flesh dropping from the ceiling, and a Deep Accursed.<\/td><\/tr><tr><th><a data-e=\"consumed-kings-garden\">Consumed King's Garden<\/a><\/th><\/tr><tr><td>10<\/td><td>From the <a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">Dancer of the Boreal Valley<\/a> bonfire (<a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">High Wall of Lothric<\/a>), climb up the ladder and head left toward the <a data-e=\"consumed-kings-garden\">Consumed King's Garden<\/a>. Ride the lift down and jump onto a ledge before reaching the bottom. Head right to find a corpse with the shard.<\/td><\/tr><tr><th><a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a><\/th><\/tr><tr><td>11<\/td><td>Once reaching the final open area that leads to the <a data-e=\"lorian-elder-prince-and-lothric-younger-prince\">boss<\/a> room, turn around and walk along the library's main dome. Keep circling it and head toward the general area behind it until reaching an archway that gives access to a segment of roof with the shard. Be careful not to get too close to the tower at the center of the dome or a trio of Gertrude's Knights will attack.<\/td><\/tr><\/table>","use":"<p>Give to <a data-e=\"blacksmith-andre\">Blacksmith Andre<\/a> in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> to increase usages of the <a data-e=\"estus-flask\">Estus Flask<\/a>. The shards can be allotted in either fashion regarding the <a data-e=\"estus-flask\">Estus<\/a> and <a data-e=\"ashen-estus-flask\">Ashen Estus Flasks<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Estus_Shard"},{"id":"excrement-covered-ashes","kind":"item","name":"Excrement-covered Ashes","page":"Excrement-covered Ashes","img":"assets/img/Excrement_covered_Ashes.webp","sub":"Merchant ashes","usage":"Give to the Shrine Handmaid to increase her inventory.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Unclean umbral ash coated with excrement.\nPerhaps it's possible the handmaid of Firelink Shrine could turn this into a few new things...\n\"Oh to savor the sweet pungency but once more...","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a>.<\/p><p>Head to the lake in Irithyll and look for the entrance to the sewers. Be careful of the Sewer Centipedes in this area and keep a lookout for a small alcove directly across from the stairs that lead to the kitchen. The ashes are on a corpse resting in shin-high water.<\/p>","use":"<p>Extends the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a>'s inventory to include the following items:<\/p><table><tr><th>Available<\/th><th>Item<\/th><th>Cost<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"blue-bug-pellet\">Blue Bug Pellet<\/a><\/td><td>1,500<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"blooming-purple-moss-clump\">Blooming Purple Moss Clump<\/a><\/td><td>1,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"dung-pie\">Dung Pie<\/a><\/td><td>50<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"stalk-dung-pie\">Stalk Dung Pie<\/a><\/td><td>50<\/td><\/tr><\/table>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Excrement-covered_Ashes"},{"id":"exploding-bolt","kind":"item","name":"Exploding Bolt","page":"Exploding Bolt","img":"assets/img/Exploding_Bolt.webp","sub":"Ammunition","usage":"Deal 140 Fire damage to target.","buy":300,"sell":5,"held":30,"desc":"Bolts that explode on impact. Deals area fire damage in the immediate vicinity.\nDue to the risk of detonation, the amount of bolts the user can carry is greatly limited.\nThese are, after all, prototypes created by the weapon craftsman Edmond. You get what you pay for.","avail":"<ul><li>Six can be found on a corpse by the first Giant inside the <a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a>.<\/li><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 500 souls once she has been given <a data-e=\"greirats-ashes\">Greirat's Ashes<\/a>, after sending him to pillage <a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Deals Fire damage in small surrounding area on impact.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Exploding_Bolt"},{"id":"eyes-of-a-fire-keeper","kind":"item","name":"Eyes of a Fire Keeper","page":"Eyes of a Fire Keeper","img":"assets/img/Eyes_of_a_Fire_Keeper.webp","sub":"Key item","usage":"Give to the Fire Keeper to unlock the End of Fire ending.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"A pair of dark eyes.\nSaid to be the eyes of the first Fire Keeper, and the light that was lost by all Fire Keepers to come.\nIt reveals to the sightless Fire Keepers things that they should never see.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"untended-graves\">Untended Graves<\/a>, inside the Flameless Shrine. They can be found on a body lying beyond an illusory wall located where <a data-e=\"irina-of-carim\">Irina<\/a> normally resides in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a>. The existence of this wall is hinted by the shorter length that corridor has, if compared to its normal shrine version counterpart.<\/p>","use":"<p>Given to the <a data-e=\"fire-keeper\">Fire Keeper<\/a> adds an option to her services to unlock the End of Fire ending.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Eyes_of_a_Fire_Keeper"},{"id":"fading-soul","kind":"item","name":"Fading Soul","page":"Fading Soul (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Fading_Soul__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Soul item","usage":"Consume to acquire 50 souls.","buy":null,"sell":50,"held":99,"desc":"The fading soul of a corpse.\nUse to gain a smattering of souls.\nLet the Fire Keeper transform this sovereignless soul into a source of strength, for to be Unkindled is to be a vessel for souls.","avail":"<p>A minimum of seven are guaranteed to be found per playthrough.<\/p><ul><li><a data-e=\"cemetery-of-ash\">Cemetery of Ash<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Gravetender Hollows.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a><ul><li>On the path to the Hollow Manservant that transports the player to the Pit of Hollows, there is a rooftop zone patrolled by numerous Thralls. A corpse in the open holds the item, as a trap for the Thralls to ambush the player.<\/li><li>In the cemetery beyond the Dilapidated Bridge bonfire, on a corpse at the base of the White Birch tree guarded by the <a data-e=\"giant-archer-of-the-undead-settlement\">Giant Archer of the Undead Settlement<\/a>.<\/li><li>Dropped by Cage Spiders. (×5)<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Road of Sacrifices<\/a><ul><li>On the wooded path leading to the Crucifixion Woods bonfire. It is held by a corpse near a stone archway that serves as an ambush for a Starved Hound.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a><ul><li>At the extreme end of the graveyard, on a corpse near the <a data-e=\"executioners-greatsword\">Executioner's Greatsword<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a><ul><li>Outside the Church of Yorshka. The item is found on a corpse dangling from the edge of a cliff, to lure players into an ambush by Irithyllian Slaves.<\/li><li>A second one is found further up the path to the right, at the base of a tree before the lone red-eyed Corvian.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a><ul><li>Shortly after encountering the first Jailer, there is a corpse holding the item dangling from a ledge to the left. It is a trap laid for a Reanimated Corpse to ambush the player from an open cell on the right and knock the player down to the lower floor.<\/li><li>Dropped by Cage Spiders. (×5)<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"untended-graves\">Untended Graves<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Gravetender Hollows.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 50 souls.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Fading_Soul_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"farron-coal","kind":"item","name":"Farron Coal","page":"Farron Coal","img":"assets/img/Farron_Coal.webp","sub":"Coal","usage":"Give to Andre to allow the use of gems for heavy, sharp and poison infusion.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Coal used for weapon infusion.\nLong ago, used to forge the greatswords of the Undead Legion of Farron.\nGive to the blacksmith in the shrine to allow the use of gems for heavy, sharp and poison infusion.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Road of Sacrifices<\/a> on what once was the eastern access to the keep. The area can be reached by following the eastern shore of the marsh, fighting a couple of Lycanthropes along the way. The coal can be found at the end of a blocked passageway, guarded by a Black Knight.<\/p>","use":"<p>The coal can be given to <a data-e=\"blacksmith-andre\">Blacksmith Andre<\/a> in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> to allow usage of the following gems for infusions:<\/p><ul><li><a data-e=\"heavy-gem\">Heavy Gem<\/a>: Allows to infuse weapons with the <a data-e=\"heavy-gem\">Heavy<\/a> attribute.<\/li><li><a data-e=\"sharp-gem\">Sharp Gem<\/a>: Allows to infuse weapons with the <a data-e=\"sharp-gem\">Sharp<\/a> attribute.<\/li><li><a data-e=\"poison-gem\">Poison Gem<\/a>: Allows to infuse weapons with Poison.<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Farron_Coal"},{"id":"feather-arrow","kind":"item","name":"Feather Arrow","page":"Feather Arrow (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Feather_Arrow__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Ammunition","usage":"Deal 40 physical damage to target.","buy":100,"sell":1,"held":99,"desc":"Red feathered arrows used by hunters.\nTheir long range makes them ideal for distant targets.\nSimultaneously equip up to two types of arrows, and switch between them as needed.","avail":"<p>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 100 souls each after giving her the <a data-e=\"dreamchasers-ashes\">Dreamchaser's Ashes<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Feather_Arrow_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"filianores-spear-ornament","kind":"item","name":"Filianore's Spear Ornament","page":"Filianore's Spear Ornament","img":"assets/img/Filianore_s_Spear_Ornament.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Used to rank up in the Spears of the Church covenant.","buy":null,"sell":10,"held":99,"desc":"The Spears of the Church watch over the Princess' slumber, and this serves as proof of their fulfillment of their duty. The embellished gold cloth is woven with a crest of young grass.\nThe Princess' knights proudly displayed these precious flavors, which were most often seen swaying from their identical ceremonial spears.","avail":"<ul><li>×1 obtained after defeating the <a data-e=\"spear-of-the-church\">Spear of the Church<\/a>.<\/li><li>Reward for successfully defeating a Host of Embers as the Spear of the Church. Additional Ornaments are rewarded depending on the number of phantoms they have summoned.<\/li><li>Dropped by Ringed Knights.<\/li><li>One is found next to the ladder just before <a data-e=\"darkeater-midir\">Midir<\/a>'s boss room.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Used to rank up in the <a data-e=\"spears-of-the-church\">Spears of the Church<\/a> covenant, being offered to the Divine Spear Monument outside the Church where the Spear of the Church takes place.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Filianore's_Spear_Ornament"},{"id":"fire-arrow","kind":"item","name":"Fire Arrow","page":"Fire Arrow (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Fire_Arrow__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Ammunition","usage":"Deals 25 physical damage and 40 Fire damage to target.","buy":100,"sell":1,"held":99,"desc":"Shoot arrows with burning tips dealing fire damage.\nSimultaneously equip up to two types of arrows, and switch between them as needed.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"greirat-of-the-undead-settlement\">Greirat of the Undead Settlement<\/a> for 100 souls each.<ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> once she has been given <a data-e=\"greirats-ashes\">Greirat's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li>Dropped by Skeleton Swordsman archers, in bundles of 12, in the <a data-e=\"catacombs-of-carthus\">Catacombs of Carthus<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Fire Arrows deal minimal thrust damage, as well as adding some Fire damage to each shot. They can be useful for applying Fire damage to distant targets, such as staggering a Pus of Man or igniting a stack of gunpowder barrels.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Fire_Arrow_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"fire-gem","kind":"item","name":"Fire Gem","page":"Fire Gem","img":"assets/img/Fire_Gem.webp","sub":"Upgrade material","usage":"Used in infusion to create fire weapons, but removes scaling effects.","buy":null,"sell":200,"held":99,"desc":"A gem of infused titanite.\nFound in rare cases inside demons.\nFire weapons inflict fire damage, but lose scaling effects.","avail":"<ul><li>Can be chosen as a burial gift at the beginning of the game.<\/li><li><a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Peasant Hollows.<\/li><li>Guaranteed drop from the Demon that <a data-e=\"siegward-of-catarina\">Siegward<\/a> helps to defeat.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"smouldering-lake\">Smouldering Lake<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Writhing Rotten Flesh.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Fire Gems can be used to infuse a weapon with an essence of fire, which will cause a weapon to inflict equally-split physical and fire damage.<\/p><p>Many Undead enemies or creatures, such as Peasant Hollows and Starved Hounds, are naturally weak to Fire damage, and thus, a Fire-infused weapon can prove useful. However, one must be cautious, as attacking an enemy with such a weapon now has to take into account two defenses. As such, enemies that possess a resistance to fire will take notably less damage.<\/p><p>Fire infusions also remove <i>all<\/i> scaling effects present on the weapon after infusion, which means that it is most efficient when using such an infused weapon at its minimum wielding requirements.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Fire_Gem"},{"id":"fire-keeper-soul","kind":"item","name":"Fire Keeper Soul","page":"Fire Keeper Soul (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Fire_Keeper_Soul__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Key item","usage":"Give to the Fire Keeper to allow her to heal dark sigils.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Soul of a Fire Keeper who is said to have returned from the Abyss.\nThis Fire Keeper preserves the bonfire, and serves its champion. She is said to have soothed and accepted the dark sigil, which has tainted her soul.\nAnd yet, her soul will one day embed itself in the bosom of another Fire Keeper.","avail":"<ul><li>Found on the corpse of a <a data-e=\"fire-keeper\">fire keeper<\/a> at the top of the bell tower in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a>. The entrance to this tower can only be unlocked by using the <a data-e=\"tower-key\">Tower Key<\/a>, sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Give the soul to the <a data-e=\"fire-keeper\">Fire Keeper<\/a> in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a>, thus allowing her to remove <a data-e=\"dark-sigil\">dark sigils<\/a> contracted after leveling up with <a data-e=\"yoel-of-londor\">Yoel of Londor<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Fire_Keeper_Soul_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"firebomb","kind":"item","name":"Firebomb","page":"Firebomb (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Firebomb__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Explodes, inflicting fire damage.","buy":null,"sell":10,"held":20,"desc":"Bisque urn filled with black powder.\nExplodes, inflicting fire damage.\nFire damage, which differs from physical damage, is highly effective against creatures of flesh, beasts, and other foes that might naturally have cause to fear the flame.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> for 100 souls each.<\/li><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"greirat-of-the-undead-settlement\">Greirat of the Undead Settlement<\/a> for 50 souls each. Giving <a data-e=\"greirats-ashes\">Greirat's Ashes<\/a> to the Shrine Handmaid will update her prices to match.<\/li><li>Five can be found near the <a data-e=\"cemetery-of-ash\">first bonfire<\/a> in the <a data-e=\"cemetery-of-ash\">Cemetery of Ash<\/a>, guarded by two Gravetender Hollows.<\/li><li>Dropped by certain Hollow Soldiers.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Many types of enemies, like hollowed humans and animals, skeletons and maggot-infested creatures, are weak to Fire in <i>Dark Souls III<\/i>. Additionally, some of them can be heavily staggered when attacked with Fire-based weaponry.<\/p><p>A notable example is a Pus of Man hollow found on the rooftops in the <a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">High Wall of Lothric<\/a>, below the <a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">Tower on the Wall<\/a> bonfire. This enemy can impose a real threat near the beginning of the game, being capable of chasing the player and kill them in just a few attacks. However, throwing firebombs at it will allow for ranged engagement from a safe distance, deal heavy damage and stagger it every time.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Firebomb_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"forked-pale-tongue","kind":"item","name":"Forked Pale Tongue","page":"Forked Pale Tongue","img":"assets/img/Forked_Pale_Tongue.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Use to acquire two Pale Tongues.","buy":null,"sell":null,"held":99,"desc":"Proof that a red eye orb invader successfully fended off a blue spirit.\nThose who hunt dark spirits take the names of gods in ancient accord with the Way of Blue, a deception exemplified by their forked tongues.\nUse to acquire two Pale Tongues.","avail":"<p>Acquired by defeating a <a data-e=\"blue-sentinels\">Blue Sentinel<\/a> or <a data-e=\"blade-of-the-darkmoon\">Darkmoon Blade<\/a> while invading as a red spirit that is not a <a data-e=\"warrior-of-sunlight\">Warrior of Sunlight<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Use to acquire two <a data-e=\"pale-tongue\">Pale Tongues<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Forked_Pale_Tongue"},{"id":"giants-coal","kind":"item","name":"Giant's Coal","page":"Giant's Coal","img":"assets/img/Giant_s_Coal.webp","sub":"Coal","usage":"Give to Andre to infuse weapons with Lightning, Simple, or Chaos.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Coal used for weapon infusion.\nIt is said that the giant blacksmith of Anor Londo was once the blacksmith of the gods.\nGive to the blacksmith in the shrine to allow the use of gems for lightning, simple, and chaos infusion.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"anor-londo\">Anor Londo<\/a>, on the remains of the Giant Blacksmith in the west wing of the cathedral.<\/p><p>From the <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Anor Londo<\/a> bonfire, head up the large staircase; once at the top, head left through a metal door archway and then enter a doorway on the right to find the giant's body holding the coal.<\/p>","use":"<p>Give the coal to <a data-e=\"blacksmith-andre\">Blacksmith Andre<\/a> in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> to allow usage of the following gems for infusions:<\/p><ul><li><a data-e=\"chaos-gem\">Chaos Gem<\/a> → Infuses a weapon with the Fire element, as well as granting Intelligence and Faith scaling to it.<\/li><li><a data-e=\"lightning-gem\">Lightning Gem<\/a> → Infuses a weapon with the Lightning element, as well as granting Faith scaling to it.<\/li><li><a data-e=\"simple-gem\">Simple Gem<\/a> → Infuses a weapon with the Magic element, as well as granting FP regeneration while wielded (about 1 FP every 5 seconds).<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Giant's_Coal"},{"id":"gold-pine-bundle","kind":"item","name":"Gold Pine Bundle","page":"Gold Pine Bundle","img":"assets/img/Gold_Pine_Bundle.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Quickly applies lightning to right-hand weapon.","buy":600,"sell":100,"held":20,"desc":"Rare pine resin which emits golden sparks.\nCollected in a small bundle.\nQuickly applies lightning to right-hand weapon.\nDoes not last for long, but can be used in inventive ways, such as applying it in the middle of a series of blows.","avail":"<ul><li>Six are found near the White Birch tree in the <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a><\/li><li>After receiving the <a data-e=\"dreamchasers-ashes\">Dreamchaser's Ashes<\/a>, the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> will sell a stock of 6 for 600 souls each.<\/li><li>After receiving the <a data-e=\"xanthous-ashes\">Xanthous Ashes<\/a>, the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> sells an unlimited amount at the same price.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Unlike resins, which require the user to remain stationary while applying the buff, bundles take less than a second to activate and can be used while moving. While they grant more damage than their respective resins and many more bundles can be carried at once, the trade-off is that the duration of the buff is reduced to less than 20% of that of a resin.<\/p><p>The quick application time, high stock and low duration of these items makes them very flexible tools, useful for applying in the midst of combat based on the situation. Whereas a resin may find a large fraction of its duration wasted from inactivity between attacks, a bundle may be quickly activated when an opportunity to deal damage presents itself, and the advantage pressed until the buff expires. This includes, in particular, the short duration of vulnerability between parrying a foe and taking the riposte.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Gold_Pine_Bundle"},{"id":"gold-pine-resin","kind":"item","name":"Gold Pine Resin","page":"Gold Pine Resin (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Gold_Pine_Resin__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Temporarily applies lightning to right-hand weapon.","buy":1000,"sell":100,"held":5,"desc":"Rare pine resin which emits golden sparks. Chunks of it are even rarer.\nTemporarily applies lightning to right-hand weapon.\nIts origins are unknown, although some have speculated that it may in fact be a type of fungal resin.","avail":"<ul><li>Two are found in the <a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">High Wall of Lothric<\/a>, inside a hidden alcove underneath the dead wyvern, on the path between the High Wall and Tower on the Wall bonfires.<\/li><li>The <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> will sell 3 for 1,000 souls each, once she is given the <a data-e=\"dreamchasers-ashes\">Dreamchaser's Ashes<\/a>.<ul><li>Once she receives the <a data-e=\"xanthous-ashes\">Xanthous Ashes<\/a>, her stock will be upgraded to unlimited for the same price.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Gold_Pine_Resin_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"golden-scroll","kind":"item","name":"Golden Scroll","page":"Golden Scroll","img":"assets/img/Golden_Scroll.webp","sub":"Spell book","usage":"Give to Orbeck of Vinheim to learn the arts of Oolacile.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"A golden scroll chronicling the vast research of the xanthous scholars.\nGive to a sorcerer to learn the arts of Oolacile.\nIn the lost land of Oolacile, the sorceries orchestrated light, and were said to shine in golden hues.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a>.<\/p><p>From the <a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Keep Ruins<\/a> bonfire, head toward the main gate and then turn right, following the wall. Once reaching a clearing inhabited by many Basilisks, turn right to find a cave with a corpse holding the scroll, along with a chest containing the <a data-e=\"antiquated-set\">Antiquated Set<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Give to <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a> in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> to upgrade his stock of Sorceries:<\/p><table><tr><th>Quantity<\/th><th>Item<\/th><th>Cost<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"cast-light\">Cast Light<\/a><\/td><td>1,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"repair\">Repair<\/a><\/td><td>2,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"hidden-weapon\">Hidden Weapon<\/a><\/td><td>1,500<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"hidden-body\">Hidden Body<\/a><\/td><td>3,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"twisted-wall-of-light\">Twisted Wall of Light<\/a><\/td><td>6,000<\/td><\/tr><\/table>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Golden_Scroll"},{"id":"grand-archives-key","kind":"item","name":"Grand Archives Key","page":"Grand Archives Key","img":"assets/img/Grand_Archives_Key.webp","sub":"Key item","usage":"Unlocks the main entrance to the Grand Archives.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":99,"desc":"Key to the main entrance to the Grand Archives of Lothric.\nWith the fire fading, and the spreading pus of man tainting the castle, the Grand Archives closed its doors for good.\nToday, only a few of its keys remain. This one likely belonged to Gotthard, one of king's Black Hand, who fled the castle.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a>, on the lifeless body of <a data-e=\"black-hand-gotthard\">Black Hand Gotthard<\/a> which can be encountered lying just before the entrance to the <a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a>. The body will only appear once the player has defeated the first three Lords of Cinder: <a data-e=\"abyss-watchers\">Abyss Watchers<\/a>, <a data-e=\"aldrich-devourer-of-gods\">Aldrich<\/a> and <a data-e=\"yhorm-the-giant\">Yhorm<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Unlocks the main entrance to the <a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a> of <a data-e=\"lothric\">Lothric<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Grand_Archives_Key"},{"id":"grave-key","kind":"item","name":"Grave Key","page":"Grave Key","img":"assets/img/Grave_Key.webp","sub":"Key item","usage":"Unlocks the barred door in the sewers of the Undead Settlement that lead to Irina's cell.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":99,"desc":"Key to the barred door leading from the sewer below the Undead Settlement to a moist grave.\nThe grave, which no longer receive visitors, was once the site of a statue of Velka, Goddess of Sin, and was believed to pardon wrongdoing and life curses.","avail":"<p>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> for 1,500 souls, once she has been given the <a data-e=\"morticians-ashes\">Mortician's Ashes<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Unlocks the barred door in the sewers of the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a> that lead to a tunnel complex which eventually ends in <a data-e=\"irina-of-carim\">Irina<\/a>'s cell. Also, this key allows to lock the door it is intended to. To lock this door, user must be standing near it at the side of tunnel catacomb(not the side of bridge and sewers) and open the door with the key. After it, door can be locked from the both sides, but if it is open from the side of sewers once, it cannot be locked anymore. If the door was open from the tunnels and player left current location, took rest near bonfire or left game, door also cannot be locked anymore. This opportunity can be used to lock an <a data-e=\"red-eye-orb\">invader<\/a> in, forcing them to <a data-e=\"black-separation-crystal\">return to their world<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Grave_Key"},{"id":"grave-warden-pyromancy-tome","kind":"item","name":"Grave Warden Pyromancy Tome","page":"Grave Warden Pyromancy Tome","img":"assets/img/Grave_Warden_Pyromancy_Tome.webp","sub":"Spell book","usage":"Give to Karla to learn black flame pyromancies.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"A pyromancy tome of the grave warden, from the Carthus Catacombs.\nGive to the pyromancer master to learn black flame sorceries.\nHigh Lord Wolnir of Carthus succumbed to the Abyss, but the pyromancer later became a grave warden, and discovered the black flame.","avail":"<p>Located in the <a data-e=\"catacombs-of-carthus\">Catacombs of Carthus<\/a>. Upon entering the boss fight of <a data-e=\"high-lord-wolnir\">High Lord Wolnir<\/a>, the item will be in the center of the arena where he spawns. If not picked up during the boss fight, it can be found on a corpse at the far-left corner of the goblet chamber after reloading the area.<\/p>","use":"<p>Giving the tome to <a data-e=\"karla\">Karla<\/a> will unlock the following dark pyromancies in her stock of wares:<\/p><ul><li><a data-e=\"black-flame\">Black Flame<\/a><\/li><li><a data-e=\"black-fire-orb\">Black Fire Orb<\/a><\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Grave_Warden_Pyromancy_Tome"},{"id":"grave-wardens-ashes","kind":"item","name":"Grave Warden's Ashes","page":"Grave Warden's Ashes","img":"assets/img/Grave_Warden_s_Ashes.webp","sub":"Merchant ashes","usage":"Give to the Shrine Handmaid to increase her inventory.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Umbral ash of the grave warden of the catacombs of Carthus. With this, the shrine handmaid will prepare new items.\nThe old man began as a squire, carrying his master's accoutrements. He ended his days a grave warden, and carried them still.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"catacombs-of-carthus\">Catacombs of Carthus<\/a>.<\/p><p>From the <a data-e=\"catacombs-of-carthus\">Catacombs of Carthus<\/a> bonfire, turn left and go downstairs. Climb up any of the two sets of stairs found on the nearby wall (one of them hidden behind an illusory wall). The ashes are on a corpse lying at the far end of this area, guarded by three Skeleton Swordsmen.<\/p>","use":"<p>Extends the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a>'s inventory to include the following items:<\/p><table><tr><th>Available<\/th><th>Item<\/th><th>Cost<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"carthus-rouge\">Carthus Rouge<\/a><\/td><td>1,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>3<\/td><td><a data-e=\"ember\">Ember<\/a><\/td><td>2,500<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"kukri\">Kukri<\/a><\/td><td>50<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"titanite-shard\">Titanite Shard<\/a><\/td><td>800<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"yellow-bug-pellet\">Yellow Bug Pellet<\/a><\/td><td>1,500<\/td><\/tr><\/table>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Grave_Warden's_Ashes"},{"id":"great-swamp-pyromancy-tome","kind":"item","name":"Great Swamp Pyromancy Tome","page":"Great Swamp Pyromancy Tome","img":"assets/img/Great_Swamp_Pyromancy_Tome.webp","sub":"Spell book","usage":"Give to Cornyx to learn advanced pyromancies of the Great Swamp.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Pyromancy tome from the Great Swamp containing advanced pyromancies.\nGive to the old master pyromancer to learn advanced pyromancies of the Great Swamp.\nSpells of the Great Swamp are passed down from master to pupil. Without a master, there is no pupil, but without a pupil, there is also no master.","avail":"<p>The tome is located within the swamp of the <a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Road of Sacrifices<\/a>, pinned between a large tree and a wall found inside a patch of deep water. A Great Crab will be guarding the area.<\/p>","use":"<p>After providing the tome to <a data-e=\"cornyx-of-the-great-swamp\">Cornyx of the Great Swamp<\/a>, the following pyromancies will be available to the player:<\/p><table><tr><th>Quantity<\/th><th>Item<\/th><th>Cost<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"fire-orb\">Fire Orb<\/a><\/td><td>3,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"bursting-fireball\">Bursting Fireball<\/a><\/td><td>5,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"poison-mist\">Poison Mist<\/a><\/td><td>2,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"profuse-sweat\">Profuse Sweat<\/a><\/td><td>2,000<\/td><\/tr><\/table>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Great_Swamp_Pyromancy_Tome"},{"id":"green-blossom","kind":"item","name":"Green Blossom","page":"Green Blossom (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Green_Blossom__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"+6 stamina regeneration speed.","buy":1000,"sell":50,"held":10,"desc":"Green weed, shaped like a flower.\nTemporary boost to stamina recovery speed.\nThe Undead Legion of Farron are remembered for using this annual plant, normally found near clear water, to swing their mighty swords with abandon.","avail":"<ul><li>Purchased from the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 1,000 souls once she is given the <a data-e=\"dreamchasers-ashes\">Dreamchaser's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><li>Dropped by Sewer Centipedes in <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a> and the <a data-e=\"profaned-capital\">Profaned Capital<\/a>.<\/li><li><a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">High Wall of Lothric<\/a><ul><li>2 are found in the building below the second Pus of Man, past the Tower on the Wall bonfire, at the end of the upper wooden walkway that leads to the <a data-e=\"astora-straight-sword\">Astora Straight Sword<\/a>.<\/li><li>3 are found on the path from the Winged Knight courtyard that leads to the elevator shortcut back to the first bonfire. In the clearing with the Praying Hollow Soldiers ambush, make a hard left upon entering the area and they can be found in a corner next to several empty Lothric Knight armors.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Road of Sacrifices<\/a><ul><li>A total of 6 are found on two corpses found within the swamp guarded by the two Great Crabs.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a><ul><li>A total of 7 are found in the riverbed below the bridge that leads into Irithyll, scattered between three corpses.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Increases the player's stamina recovery rate by +6 points per second. Effect lasts for 60 seconds.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Green_Blossom_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"greirats-ashes","kind":"item","name":"Greirat's Ashes","page":"Greirat's Ashes","img":"assets/img/Greirat_s_Ashes.webp","sub":"Merchant ashes","usage":"Give to the Shrine Handmaid to increase her inventory.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Umbral ash of Greirat of the Undead Settlement. With this, the shrine handmaid will prepare new items.\nGreirat was a thief who fancied himself a martyr for the poor, which is what drove him to climb the wall.","avail":"<p>Dropped by <a data-e=\"greirat-of-the-undead-settlement\">Greirat of the Undead Settlement<\/a> if he is killed by the player, or if he dies during one of his pillaging attempts.<\/p><ul><li>If Greirat dies during his pillaging travel in <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll<\/a>, his ashes can be found on his body floating on a corner of the drainage ditch inhabited by several Sewer Centipedes.<\/li><li>Once Greirat is killed during his pillaging travel in <a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a>, his ashes can be found along the rooftops of the <a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a>. Proceed past a congregation of Corvians in the open area after the library, and make a leap to the rooftop below, where Greirat's body lies.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Give to the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> to expand her inventory to include items that Greirat was selling upon death, as well as what his next pillaging journey would have yielded.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Greirat's_Ashes"},{"id":"hawkwoods-swordgrass","kind":"item","name":"Hawkwood's Swordgrass","page":"Hawkwood's Swordgrass","img":"assets/img/Hawkwood_s_Swordgrass.webp","sub":"Key item","usage":"Bears a message from Hawkwood to meet him in the Farron mausoleum.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":99,"desc":"Blood-stained swordgrass of Hawkwood, deserter of the Undead Legion.\nTraditionally, the Undead Legion of Farron sends the gravest of messages using swordgrass.\n\"Come to the mausoleum in Farron. Only one can take the path of ancient dragons.\"","avail":"<p>Once the player has obtained the <a data-e=\"twinkling-dragon-torso-stone\">Twinkling Dragon Torso Stone<\/a> in <a data-e=\"archdragon-peak\">Archdragon Peak<\/a>, the swordgrass will be given to the Ashen One by <a data-e=\"blacksmith-andre\">Andre<\/a> in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a>, along with a message from <a data-e=\"hawkwood\">Hawkwood<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Bears a message from <a data-e=\"hawkwood\">Hawkwood<\/a>:<\/p><p>&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;<i>&quot;Come to the mausoleum in Farron. Only one can take the path of ancient dragons.&quot;<\/i>&lt;/p&gt;<\/p><p>While this item by itself does not have any particular use, it hints the player into visiting the <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">mausoleum in Farron<\/a> once more, in the same place where they fought the <a data-e=\"abyss-watchers\">Abyss Watchers<\/a>. Upon arrival, <a data-e=\"hawkwood\">Hawkwood<\/a> will be already expecting them and challenge them to a duel to the death for the <a data-e=\"twinkling-dragon-torso-stone\">Twinkling Dragon Torso Stone<\/a> and the title of who is the best &quot;dragon&quot; of both.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Hawkwood's_Swordgrass"},{"id":"heavy-bolt","kind":"item","name":"Heavy Bolt","page":"Heavy Bolt (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Heavy_Bolt__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Ammunition","usage":"Deal 64 physical damage to target.","buy":100,"sell":1,"held":99,"desc":"Large, more powerful bolts with a shorter range due to their weight.\nSimultaneously equip up to two types of bolts, and switch between them as needed.","avail":"<ul><li>Rare drop from the Devout of the Deep enemies in the <a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a>.<\/li><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"greirat-of-the-undead-settlement\">Greirat of the Undead Settlement<\/a> for 100 souls each, once he returns from his first pillaging journey.<\/li><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> once she has been given <a data-e=\"greirats-ashes\">Greirat's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Heavy_Bolt_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"heavy-gem","kind":"item","name":"Heavy Gem","page":"Heavy Gem","img":"assets/img/Heavy_Gem.webp","sub":"Upgrade material","usage":"Used in infusion to create heavy weapons.","buy":null,"sell":300,"held":99,"desc":"A gem of infused titanite.\nFamously used to forge Farron greatswords.\nUsed in infusion to create heavy weapons.\nA warrior can appreciate a heavy weapon, for they scale effectively with strength.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><ul><li>Gift from <a data-e=\"hawkwood\">Hawkwood the Deserter<\/a> after defeating the <a data-e=\"curse-rotted-greatwood\">Curse-rotted Greatwood<\/a>. Otherwise, dropped by Hawkwood if he is killed before it is gifted.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by a Crystal Lizard found at the bottom of the chasm before reaching <a data-e=\"irina-of-carim\">Irina of Carim<\/a>'s cell (<a data-e=\"grave-key\">Grave Key<\/a> required).<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Rotten Slugs.<\/li><li>Dropped by Ghrus.<\/li><li>Dropped by Elder Ghrus.<\/li><li>Dropped by a Crystal Lizard in the ruined fortress. From the <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Old Wolf of Farron<\/a> bonfire, take the lift up and climb the stairs. Turn around and search for a broken part of the scenery. Drop to and follow the ledges below. The lizard can be found at the base of a staircase surrounded by hollows.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by a Crystal Lizard on the rooftops. On the sloped rooftop above the Corvians, there will be two Crystal Lizards guarded by a pair of Gargoyles.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a><ul><li>Dropped commonly by Millwood Knights.<\/li><li>Found in the abandoned village guarded by Millwood Knights, next to a destroyed wall guarded by a <a data-e=\"quakestone-hammer\">great hammer<\/a>-wielding knight.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Infusing a weapon with the Heavy property will significantly improve the Strength scaling on that weapon, but compromises the Dexterity scaling by completely removing it, putting emphasis on only Strength after the infusion is done.<\/p><p>Like most other infusions, it will also lower the weapon's base damage slightly. Heavy infusions should only be used if there is a large gap between one's Strength and Dexterity, as if both are nearly equal to one another, the weapon's overall damage after the infusion may be lower than it was prior to.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Heavy_Gem"},{"id":"hello-carving","kind":"item","name":"Hello Carving","page":"Carvings (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Carvings__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"When used, the carved head shouts: \"Hello!\".","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"A strange head of unknown origin carved from archtree. It speaks when thrown on the ground.\nThis head says 'Hello'. Have another look. Do you sense the amicability in its eyes?","avail":"","use":"","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Carvings_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"hidden-blessing","kind":"item","name":"Hidden Blessing","page":"Hidden Blessing","img":"assets/img/Hidden_Blessing.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Fully restores FP.","buy":"Varies","sell":1000,"held":1,"desc":"Holy water blessed by the Queen of Lothric.\nFully restores FP.\nThere is a grave in Lothric that sees no visitors, a dark place where rootless warriors rest. The Queen of Lothric alone cared to wish the poor souls good fortune.","avail":"<ul><li>Can be chosen as a burial gift at the beginning of the game.<\/li><li><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 1,000 souls, once she has been given the <a data-e=\"dreamchasers-ashes\">Dreamchaser's Ashes<\/a>. She will only sell it if she is told where the Ashen One found the ashes.<\/li><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"greirat-of-the-undead-settlement\">Greirat of the Undead Settlement<\/a> for 8,000 souls once he returns from pillaging <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a>, or by the Shrine Handmaid once <a data-e=\"greirats-ashes\">his ashes<\/a> are given to her, provided that he has at least returned successfully from pillaging the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a>.<\/li><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"unbreakable-patches\">Unbreakable Patches<\/a> for 16,000 souls if he is told about Greirat's trip to pillage <a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"untended-graves\">Untended Graves<\/a><ul><li>Found behind the coffin where the <a data-e=\"titanite-shard\">Titanite Shard<\/a> would be in the <a data-e=\"cemetery-of-ash\">Cemetery of Ash<\/a>, in the drop-down area to the left of <a data-e=\"champion-gundyr\">Champion Gundyr<\/a>'s boss fog.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-dreg-heap\">The Dreg Heap<\/a><ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"stone-humped-hag\">Stone-humped Hag<\/a> for 8,000 souls.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a><ul><li>Found inside the indoors tomb beneath the Judicator Giant guarding the Mausoleum Lookout.<\/li><li>Guaranteed drop from the Judicator Giant patrolling the Ringed City Streets.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Fully restores FP. They can be used anywhere and by anyone, including phantoms and dark spirits.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Hidden_Blessing"},{"id":"hollow-gem","kind":"item","name":"Hollow Gem","page":"Hollow Gem","img":"assets/img/Hollow_Gem.webp","sub":"Upgrade material","usage":"Used in infusion to create hollow weapons.","buy":null,"sell":300,"held":99,"desc":"A gem of infused titanite. A stone plentiful in Londor, land of Hollows.\nUsed in infusion to create Hollow weapons.\nHollow weapons are said to peer into the essence of its wielder, whose luck boosts attack.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><ul><li>Once per game cycle, one can be obtained by trading the <a data-e=\"eleonora\">Eleonora<\/a> with the <a data-e=\"nestling\">Nestling<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Road of Sacrifices<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Corvian Storytellers.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a><ul><li>From the <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep Perimeter<\/a> bonfire, turn around and walk straight ahead until finding a hole on the wall to the right. Drop through it to find two corpses, one of them holding a Hollow Gem and the other the <a data-e=\"atonement\">Atonement<\/a> miracle.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"untended-graves\">Untended Graves<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Corvian Storytellers.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a><ul><li>On the rooftops section of this level, drop to the balcony where several Corvians are gathered and turn around. Proceed straight to find a corpse holding the gem lying next to a boarded-up door.<\/li><li>Dropped by the Corvian Storyteller preaching to the group of Corvians as above.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a><ul><li>Found on a corpse outside of Ariandel Chapel, to the right and past where <a data-e=\"sir-vilhelm\">Sir Vilhelm<\/a> is standing.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Undead Clerics.<\/li><li>Found on a corpse in the Ringed Inner Wall area, shortly before encountering the first Ringed Knight.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Grants Luck scaling to Physical damage. Reduces Strength and Dexterity scaling, as well as base damage, though the scaling is gradually restored with upgrade levels.<\/p><p>Hollow-infused weapons will increase Luck based on the upgrade level of the weapon, if the wielder has at least 15 Hollowing:<\/p><table><tr><th>Weapon upgrade level<\/th><th>Bonus Luck<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>+0<\/td><td>2<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>+1 to +4<\/td><td>3<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>+5 to +9<\/td><td>4<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>+10<\/td><td>5<\/td><\/tr><\/table><p>Bonus Luck is granted for weapons regardless of which hand they are held in, and can stack with each other even when two-handing one of them. Thus, it is possible to have a total of +10 additional Luck by wielding a +10 Hollow-infused weapon/shield in each hand.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Hollow_Gem"},{"id":"hollows-ashes","kind":"item","name":"Hollow's Ashes","page":"Hollow's Ashes","img":"assets/img/Hollow_s_Ashes.webp","sub":"Merchant ashes","usage":"Give to the Shrine Handmaid to increase her inventory.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Umbral ash of a Hollow who faithfully served a woman, only to become separated from her. With this, the shrine handmaid will prepare new items.\nIt takes but a brief glance at this thing to easily envision Londor, the foreboding land of Hollows.","avail":"<ul><li>Dropped by <a data-e=\"yoel-of-londor\">Yoel of Londor<\/a>.<\/li><li>Found in the dark <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> version of the <a data-e=\"untended-graves\">Untended Graves<\/a>, only if Yoel died of natural causes (i.e. the player entered the <a data-e=\"catacombs-of-carthus\">Catacombs of Carthus<\/a> without following his questline). The ashes can be found on the spot where Yoel used to reside when he was alive.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Extends the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a>'s inventory to include the following items:<\/p><table><tr><th>Available<\/th><th>Item<\/th><th>Cost<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"poison-throwing-knife\">Poison Throwing Knife<\/a><\/td><td>20<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"purging-stone\">Purging Stone<\/a><\/td><td>3,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>3<\/td><td><a data-e=\"ring-of-sacrifice\">Ring of Sacrifice<\/a><\/td><td>5,000<\/td><\/tr><\/table>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Hollow's_Ashes"},{"id":"holy-water-urn","kind":"item","name":"Holy Water Urn","page":"Holy Water Urn (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Holy_Water_Urn__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"-","buy":null,"sell":null,"held":null,"desc":"","avail":"","use":"","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Holy_Water_Urn_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"homeward-bone","kind":"item","name":"Homeward Bone","page":"Homeward Bone (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Homeward_Bone__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Returns the player to Firelink Shrine or to the last bonfire rested at.","buy":null,"sell":100,"held":99,"desc":"Bone fragment reduced to white ash.\nReturn to the last bonfire used for resting, or to the shrine bonfire.\nBonfires are sustained by the bones of the Undead. In rare cases, their previous owner's strong urge to seek bonfires enchants their bones with a homeward instinct.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"cemetery-of-ash\">Cemetery of Ash<\/a><ul><li>One is found near the cliffside to the right, past the <a data-e=\"cemetery-of-ash\">Iudex Gundyr<\/a> bonfire.<\/li><li>One is found by taking the path to the right before entering the shrine, on a corpse lying on a tombstone guarded by a Starved Hound.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 500 souls each.<\/li><li>Three are found on the shrine's rooftop.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a><ul><li>One is given to you by <a data-e=\"holy-knight-hodrick\">Holy Knight Hodrick<\/a> when you meet him for the first time in the Pit of Hollows.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a><ul><li>At the edge of the cliff past the first encounter with the giant wolf, in the ruins before the tower with Millwood Knights.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Homeward_Bone_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"human-dregs","kind":"item","name":"Human Dregs","page":"Human Dregs","img":"assets/img/Human_Dregs.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Used to rank up within the Aldrich Faithful covenant.","buy":null,"sell":10,"held":99,"desc":"Proof of a duty fulfilled by the Aldrich Faithful who patiently await the Devourer of Gods' return.\nDregs are the heaviest things within the human body, and will sink to the lowest depths imaginable, where they become the shackles that bind this world.","avail":"<ul><li>Obtained as a reward upon successfully defeating a trespasser while in the <a data-e=\"aldrich-faithful\">Aldrich Faithful<\/a> covenant.<\/li><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Deacons.<\/li><li>One can be found near the <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Water Reserve<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"anor-londo\">Anor Londo<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Deacons.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-dreg-heap\">The Dreg Heap<\/a> (<i><a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a><\/i>)<ul><li>Dropped by longstaff-wielding Murkmen.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Offer Human Dregs to <a data-e=\"archdeacon-mcdonnell\">Archdeacon McDonnell<\/a> in the corner of the <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Water Reserve<\/a> to rank up within the <a data-e=\"aldrich-faithful\">Aldrich Faithful<\/a> covenant:<\/p><ul><li>Offering 10 dregs rewards the player with Rank 1 and the <a data-e=\"great-deep-soul\">Great Deep Soul<\/a>.<\/li><li>Offering 30 dregs rewards the player with Rank 2 and the <a data-e=\"archdeacons-great-staff\">Archdeacon's Great Staff<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><p>&lt;tabber&gt;Official translation= Proof of a duty fulfilled by the Aldrich Faithful who patiently await the Devourer of Gods' return.<\/p><p>Dregs are the heaviest things within the human body, and will sink to the lowest depths imaginable, where they become the shackles that bind this world. |-|Original description (Japanese) = エルドリッチの神喰らいを待ち続ける 神喰らいの守り手たちが、その使命を果たした証 人の内にある最も重いもの。人の澱み<\/p><p>それはどんな深みにも沈み 故にいつか、世界の枷になるという |-|Literal translation = Proof that Guardians of the God Eater, who continue to wait for Eldritch the God Eater, have fulfilled their mission. The heaviest thing within humans. The stagnation of humanity.<\/p><p>It will sink to any depth, so it is said that it will become the shackles of the world. &lt;/tabber&gt;<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Human_Dregs"},{"id":"human-pine-resin","kind":"item","name":"Human Pine Resin","page":"Human Pine Resin","img":"assets/img/Human_Pine_Resin.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Temporarily applies dark to right-hand weapon.","buy":1500,"sell":100,"held":5,"desc":"Charcoal pine resin rotted with human body fluids.\nTemporarily applies dark to right-hand weapon.\nNormally used in the Undead Settlement for preservation and burials, but can mature into this state, becoming a valuable substance, used in a certain ceremony. Often seen for trade at exorbitant prices.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><ul><li>Three are sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 1,500 souls each, once she has been given the <a data-e=\"morticians-ashes\">Mortician's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"unbreakable-patches\">Unbreakable Patches<\/a> for 1,500 souls each. In the case of Patches' death, his <a data-e=\"patches-ashes\">ashes<\/a> can be given to the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> to increase her stock, allowing her to continue selling these resins.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by the skeletons found along the tunnels that lead to <a data-e=\"irina-of-carim\">Irina<\/a>'s cell.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Adds 95 Dark damage to right-hand weapon for 60 seconds.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Human_Pine_Resin"},{"id":"irinas-ashes","kind":"item","name":"Irina's Ashes","page":"Irina's Ashes","img":"assets/img/Irina_s_Ashes.webp","sub":"Merchant ashes","usage":"Give to the Shrine Handmaid to increase her inventory.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Umbral ash of Irina of Carim. With this, the shrine handmaid will prepare new items.\nIrina was a frail woman. this frailty led to her becoming a saint of Carim, and to her grand treachery.","avail":"<p>Dropped by <a data-e=\"irina-of-carim\">Irina of Carim<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Extends the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a>'s inventory to include items initially sold by <a data-e=\"irina-of-carim\">Irina<\/a>. The items will be exactly the same as Irina's stock at the time of her death, including items from divine tomes. Items that were already bought from Irina will be listed but exhausted.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Irina's_Ashes"},{"id":"izalith-pyromancy-tome","kind":"item","name":"Izalith Pyromancy Tome","page":"Izalith Pyromancy Tome","img":"assets/img/Izalith_Pyromancy_Tome.webp","sub":"Spell book","usage":"Give to Cornyx of the Great Swamp to learn chaos pyromancies of Izalith.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"A pyromancy tome from Izalith containing pyromancies of the witches.\nGive to the old master pyromancer to learn chaos pyromancies of Izalith.\nChaos pyromancies manipulate lava, and birthed all later forms of pyromancy.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"smouldering-lake\">Smouldering Lake<\/a>. From the <a data-e=\"smouldering-lake\">Old King's Antechamber<\/a> bonfire, head into the passage with the Demon Cleric and proceed forward into a room guarded by three Smouldering Ghrus. The tome can be looted from a corpse &quot;praying&quot; in front of a statue.<\/p>","use":"<p>Giving the tome to <a data-e=\"cornyx-of-the-great-swamp\">Cornyx of the Great Swamp<\/a> will unlock the following pyromancies in his stock of wares:<\/p><table><tr><th>Quantity<\/th><th>Item<\/th><th>Cost<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"great-chaos-fire-orb\">Great Chaos Fire Orb<\/a><\/td><td>10,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"chaos-storm\">Chaos Storm<\/a><\/td><td>12,000<\/td><\/tr><\/table>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Izalith_Pyromancy_Tome"},{"id":"jailbreakers-key","kind":"item","name":"Jailbreaker's Key","page":"Jailbreaker's Key","img":"assets/img/Jailbreaker_s_Key.webp","sub":"Key item","usage":"Unlocks the barred window in the Irithyll Dungeon.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":99,"desc":"Key to the barred window in the Irithyll dungeon.\nBut the window only leads to a bottomless black pit below, and above, a paltry view of the ruined Profaned Capital.\nThe very architecture appears to be a cruel joke the jailers played on would-be escapees.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a>, in a cell at the end of the second floor, in the hallway that is accessed by traveling through the hole connecting two adjacent cells.<\/p>","use":"<p>Unlocks the barred window found at the end on the first corridor on the second floor of the <a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Jailbreaker's_Key"},{"id":"jailers-key-ring","kind":"item","name":"Jailer's Key Ring","page":"Jailer's Key Ring","img":"assets/img/Jailer_s_Key_Ring.webp","sub":"Key item","usage":"Unlocks many cell doors in the Irithyll Dungeon, including Karla's.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Ring of keys to the Irithyll dungeon held by the jailer.\nOpens most cell doors.\nOn what grounds do they remain imprisoned, considering that by now they are mindless Hollows, or unrealized, gibbering fools?","avail":"<p>Found in the upper levels of the Giant Slave's cell in the <a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a>. To reach it, the player must head through the toxic swamp of the <a data-e=\"profaned-capital\">Profaned Capital<\/a>, up the chapel, and through a passage with a hole on the wall overlooking the giant and guarded by two invisible Jailers. The key lies at the end of the hallway.<\/p>","use":"<p>Unlocks three cells in the <a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a>:<\/p><ol><li>Unlocks a cell near the <a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a> bonfire with a corpse holding a <a data-e=\"rusted-gold-coin\">Rusted Gold Coin<\/a>.<\/li><li>Unlocks both gates of a cell on the lower-east wing of the first cell block with a corpse holding the <a data-e=\"prisoner-chiefs-ashes\">Prisoner Chief's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><li>Unlocks <a data-e=\"karla\">Karla<\/a>'s cell in the second cell block. The area is patrolled by several Jailers.<\/li><\/ol>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Jailer's_Key_Ring"},{"id":"karlas-ashes","kind":"item","name":"Karla's Ashes","page":"Karla's Ashes","img":"assets/img/Karla_s_Ashes.webp","sub":"Merchant ashes","usage":"Give to the Shrine Handmaid to increase her inventory.","buy":null,"sell":null,"held":1,"desc":"Umbral ash of Karla. With this, the shrine handmaid will prepare new items.\nThe spurned child of the Abyss never dies, but phases in and out of its fringes. Only, there is no one to search for her any longer.","avail":"<p>Dropped by <a data-e=\"karla\">Karla<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Give to the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> to extend her inventory to include spells sold by Karla at the time of death.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Karla's_Ashes"},{"id":"kukri","kind":"item","name":"Kukri","page":"Kukri","img":"assets/img/Kukri.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Inflict physical damage and bleed buildup.","buy":50,"sell":10,"held":30,"desc":"Small throwing machete.\nThrow at enemies to cause bleeding damage.\nA unique weapon originally used by swordsmen of Carthus, but now popular among bandits and thieves.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 50 souls each once she has been given the <a data-e=\"grave-wardens-ashes\">Grave Warden's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a><ul><li>Nine are found on a corpse hanging high from the tree where the Evangelist and the peasants are praying. Use a ranged attack to bring the body down.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"catacombs-of-carthus\">Catacombs of Carthus<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Skeletons and Skeleton Swordsmen.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Kukri"},{"id":"large-arrow","kind":"item","name":"Large Arrow","page":"Large Arrow (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Large_Arrow__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Ammunition","usage":"Deal 55 physical damage to target.","buy":50,"sell":1,"held":99,"desc":"Large, more powerful arrows with a shorter range due to their weight.\nSimultaneously equip up to two types of arrows, and switch between them as needed.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"greirat-of-the-undead-settlement\">Greirat of the Undead Settlement<\/a> for 50 souls each, once he has returned from his first pillaging journey.<ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> after she has been given <a data-e=\"greirats-ashes\">Greirat's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Large_Arrow_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"large-soul-of-a-crestfallen-knight","kind":"item","name":"Large Soul of a Crestfallen Knight","page":"Large Soul of a Crestfallen Knight","img":"assets/img/Large_Soul_of_a_Crestfallen_Knight.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Consume to acquire 20,000 souls.","buy":null,"sell":20000,"held":99,"desc":"Large soul found in the corpse of a crestfallen knight.\nUse to acquire a large amount of souls.\nLet the Fire Keeper transform this sovereignless soul into a source of strength, for to be Unkindled is to be a vessel for souls.","avail":"<p>A total of six can be found in each playthrough. Three are found in the base game, one in <i>Ashes of Ariandel<\/i> and two in <i><a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a><\/i>:<\/p><ul><li><a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a><ul><li>On the fifth floor of the library, in the area with four Grand Archives Scholars. The item is at the other end of the central bookshelves, where several Clawed Curses spawn.<\/li><li>In the big courtyard past the roofs section, where Lion Knight Albert, Black Hand Kamui and Daughter of Crystal Kriemhild attack the player. The soul can be looted from a corpse right before the encounter.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul><ul><li><a data-e=\"archdragon-peak\">Archdragon Peak<\/a><ul><li>Past the <a data-e=\"archdragon-peak\">Great Belfry<\/a>, there is a large courtyard with ruins and numerous Man Serpents. The item is found on a corpse close to <a data-e=\"hawkwood\">Hawkwood the Deserter<\/a>'s summon sign.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul><ul><li><a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a><ul><li>In the <a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Snowy Mountain Pass<\/a>, near the end is a valley with an <a data-e=\"earth-seeker\">Earth Seeker<\/a> wielding Millwood Knight. The soul can be found on a corpse lying against the large tree in the center of the valley.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul><ul><li><a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a><ul><li>At the end of the great stairway leading to the <a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">Ringed City Streets<\/a>, three Harald Legion Knights will rise up from the swamp. The soul can be found on a corpse in front of them.<\/li><li>On the way to the Purging Monument, after climbing down the ladder and crossing the bridge over the great stairway, the soul can be found on a corpse to the left of the bridge, with the path leading to the Purging Monument on the right.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 20,000 souls.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Large_Soul_of_a_Crestfallen_Knight"},{"id":"large-soul-of-a-deserted-corpse","kind":"item","name":"Large Soul of a Deserted Corpse","page":"Large Soul of a Deserted Corpse","img":"assets/img/Large_Soul_of_a_Deserted_Corpse.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Consume to acquire 400 souls.","buy":null,"sell":400,"held":99,"desc":"Large soul found in a deserted corpse.\nUse to acquire souls.\nLet the Fire Keeper transform this sovereignless soul into a source of strength, for to be Unkindled is to be a vessel for souls.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">High Wall of Lothric<\/a><ul><li>On the upper floor, in front of the Lothric Wyvern.<\/li><li>On the roof with the Pus of Man.<\/li><li>Near the entrance to the small courtyard with the Winged Knight.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a><ul><li>Left of the initial location at the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Foot of the High Wall<\/a>.<\/li><li>To the right of the big open area with several peasants and an Evangelist.<\/li><li>On a cliff behind a house located just after exiting the far-left building of the big open area with the first Evangelist and before reaching the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Dilapidated Bridge<\/a>. The path is hidden behind some barrels.<\/li><li>In the cemetery past the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Dilapidated Bridge<\/a>.<\/li><li>Dropped by the Giant Hound Rat.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Corpse Grubs.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"untended-graves\">Untended Graves<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Gravetender Hollows.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 400 souls.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Large_Soul_of_a_Deserted_Corpse"},{"id":"large-soul-of-a-nameless-soldier","kind":"item","name":"Large Soul of a Nameless Soldier","page":"Large Soul of a Nameless Soldier (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Large_Soul_of_a_Nameless_Soldier__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Soul item","usage":"Consume to acquire 3,000 souls.","buy":null,"sell":3000,"held":99,"desc":"Large soul found in the corpse of a nameless soldier.\nUse to acquire souls.\nLet the Fire Keeper transform this sovereignless soul into a source of strength, for to be Unkindled is to be a vessel for souls.","avail":"<p>Fifteen can be found in each playthrough.<\/p><ul><li><a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a><ul><li>In the farthest reaches of the swamp, close to the flame patrolled by Elder Ghrus. In the deep waters populated by Basilisks, a corpse can be spotted due to its outstretched hand sticking out of the water. The soul item can be looted from it.<\/li><li>In the same area as above, close to where Yellowfinger Heysel invades the player, there is an alcove near the stairs that lead up to the flame from the deep swamp. Another drowned corpse here holds the item.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"catacombs-of-carthus\">Catacombs of Carthus<\/a><ul><li>Amidst the field of bones before the suspension bridge that leads to <a data-e=\"high-lord-wolnir\">High Lord Wolnir<\/a> are two corpses. One of the corpses holds the item.<\/li><li>In the path beneath the suspension bridge leading to <a data-e=\"smouldering-lake\">Smouldering Lake<\/a> guarded by the Fire Demon and several resurrecting skeletons, one of the corpses on the lowest tier can be looted for the consumable.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a><ul><li>Found on a corpse close to the Central Irithyll bonfire, next to a nearby outer railing.<\/li><li>In the courtyard after the initial wave of Pontiff Knights is a fountain patrolled by Irithyllian Slaves and which a Fire Witch will approach towards. Next to the fountain are two corpses, one of which holds the item.<\/li><li>Once the main road diverges and a small side path to the left grants access to the Church of Yorshka, there is a corpse propped up against a statue on the left side right before the central plaza with the Fire Witch and Pontiff Knights, which can be looted for the consumable.<\/li><li>On a corpse within the dried riverbed past the Church of Yorshka. The corpse resides on one of the islands along the path to the Distant Manor.<\/li><li>Beyond the Distant Manor, in an alleyway leading back up to the main Irithyll plaza, there is a tree near which the Londor Pale Shade will invade the player if they are not in good graces with <a data-e=\"yuria-of-londor\">Yuria of Londor<\/a>. At the base of the tree is a corpse holding the item.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a><ul><li>Within the initial cell block, in the wing that contains the <a data-e=\"jailbreakers-key\">Jailbreaker's Key<\/a> shortcut there is a lone corpse on the lower floor that is guarded by an Infested Corpse. The corpse can be looted for the item.<\/li><li>Upon reaching the bottom-most cell block patrolled by multiple Jailers and leading to the <a data-e=\"profaned-capital\">Profaned Capital<\/a>, an elevator can be accessed which grants access to a shortcut back to the initial cell block. Close to the door which can be unlocked to facilitate the shortcut is a corpse holding the consumable.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a><ul><li>Upon dropping down into the moat in the Dragon Barracks that is below the perch of the two Lothric Wyverns, a path to the right leads around and back to the bonfire. After dealing with the Hollow Assassins that guard this path, a corpse dangling from the ledge that drops down to the bonfire can be looted for the item.<\/li><li>Found on a corpse in the area to the left of the moat path. Prior to crossing the open keep to the powder barrel room, the corpse can be found leaning against a column in the open, near the stairs that lead down to the Boreal Outrider Knight.<\/li><li>In the powder barrel room, there is a ladder that leads to the foot of one of the Lothric Wyverns. At the top of the ladder is a corpse dangling over the ledge which can be looted for the soul.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"archdragon-peak\">Archdragon Peak<\/a><ul><li>In the <a data-e=\"ancient-wyvern\">Ancient Wyvern<\/a> battle arena, on a corpse in the open path beneath the Wyvern's landing zone. It can be found in the area leading towards the building where the first wave of Man Serpents are encountered.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 3,000 souls.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Large_Soul_of_a_Nameless_Soldier_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"large-soul-of-a-proud-paladin","kind":"item","name":"Large Soul of a Proud Paladin","page":"Large Soul of a Proud Paladin","img":"assets/img/Large_Soul_of_a_Proud_Paladin.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Consume to acquire 1,000 souls.","buy":null,"sell":1000,"held":99,"desc":"Large soul found in the corpse of a proud paladin.\nUse to acquire many souls.\nLet the Fire Keeper transform this sovereignless soul into a source of strength, for to be Unkindled is to be a vessel for souls.","avail":"<p>Can only be obtained in NG+ onward, where it replaces the <a data-e=\"large-soul-of-a-deserted-corpse\">Large Soul of a Deserted Corpse<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 1,000 souls.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Large_Soul_of_a_Proud_Paladin"},{"id":"large-soul-of-a-seasoned-warrior","kind":"item","name":"Large Soul of a Seasoned Warrior","page":"Large Soul of a Seasoned Warrior","img":"assets/img/Large_Soul_of_a_Seasoned_Warrior.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Consume to acquire 7,500 souls.","buy":null,"sell":7500,"held":99,"desc":"Large soul found in the corpse of a seasoned warrior.\nUse to acquire a great helping of souls.\nLet the Fire Keeper transform this sovereignless soul into a source of strength, for to be Unkindled is to be a vessel for souls.","avail":"<p>Can only be obtained in NG+ onward, where it replaces the <a data-e=\"large-soul-of-a-nameless-soldier\">Large Soul of a Nameless Soldier<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 7,500 souls.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Large_Soul_of_a_Seasoned_Warrior"},{"id":"large-soul-of-a-weary-warrior","kind":"item","name":"Large Soul of a Weary Warrior","page":"Large Soul of a Weary Warrior","img":"assets/img/Large_Soul_of_a_Weary_Warrior.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Consume to acquire 8,000 souls.","buy":null,"sell":8000,"held":99,"desc":"Large soul found in the corpse of a battle-weary warrior.\nUse to acquire a large amount of souls.\nLet the Fire Keeper transform this sovereignless soul into a source of strength, for to be Unkindled is to be a vessel for souls.","avail":"<p>Fifteen can be obtained per playthrough. Six can be found in the base game, two in <i>Ashes of Ariandel<\/i> and seven in <i><a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a><\/i>:<\/p><ul><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a><ul><li>On the path from the bottom floor cell block towards the <a data-e=\"profaned-capital\">Profaned Capital<\/a>, one can be looted from a corpse prior to encountering a Gargoyle.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"anor-londo\">Anor Londo<\/a><ul><li>Past the two Silver Knights that patrol the stairs to the cathedral, to the left before the gate leading to the Giant Blacksmith is a corpse.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"profaned-capital\">Profaned Capital<\/a><ul><li>On the path leading to <a data-e=\"yhorm-the-giant\">Yhorm the Giant<\/a>. Past the Gargoyle guarding the narrow bridge is a corpse outside the side building entrance.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a><ul><li>Found on a corpse on the path to the Dragon Barracks. Before going up the stairs guarded by the two crossbow-wielding Hollow Soldiers, keep going down the left path. The corpse is near a parapet patrolled by a Large Hollow Soldier.<\/li><li>After reaching the lever that opens the castle gate, there is a corpse perched on a drop-down above an <a data-e=\"lothric-knight-greatsword\">ultra greatsword<\/a> wielding Lothric Knight.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"archdragon-peak\">Archdragon Peak<\/a><ul><li>Found at the beginning of the <a data-e=\"ancient-wyvern\">Ancient Wyvern<\/a> boss fight. Immediately under the wyvern's landing zone is a corpse holding the item.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a><ul><li>In the Snowfield, within the village guarded by several Millwood Knights. The soul can be found on a dead Millwood Knight at the top of the tower, near the <a data-e=\"captains-ashes\">Captain's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><li>On top of the closed chapel at the end of the Corvian Settlement that houses <a data-e=\"way-of-white-corona\">Way of White Corona<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-dreg-heap\">The Dreg Heap<\/a><ul><li>On the hidden path to the right after meeting <a data-e=\"amnesiac-lapp\">Amnesiac Lapp<\/a>. After the initial drop-down leading to <a data-e=\"projected-heal\">Projected Heal<\/a>, there is another drop-down that is guarded by two root-infested Lothric Knights. To the left after the landing is a corpse holding the item.<\/li><li>In the Earthen Peak Ruins, there is a cave that offers shelter from the third Angel. Past the Harald Legion Knight is a pillar surrounded by numerous Poisonhorn Bugs, and a corpse holding the soul.<\/li><li>Another can be found in the open swamp beneath the Angel, patrolled by another Harald Knight.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a><ul><li>At the Mausoleum Lookout, a corpse in the open area guarded by the Judicator Giant holds the item. It is at the end of the graveyard roughly under where the fire-breathing dragon head spawns to prevent progress.<\/li><li>In the swamp within the Ringed City Streets. The soul is held by a corpse in the middle of the swamp, near the patrol path of the Judicator Giant.<\/li><li>On the cliffside path to the Shared Grave that is guarded by <a data-e=\"darkeater-midir\">Darkeater Midir<\/a>, the right-side path patrolled by Undead Clerics has a corpse holding the item.<\/li><li>In the shrine past Darkeater Midir, before the stairs leading up to the statue of Gwyn, Lord of Sunlight, there is a doorway leading to a lone Hobbled Cleric. Behind it is an illusory wall hiding a corpse that holds the soul.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 8,000 souls.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Large_Soul_of_a_Weary_Warrior"},{"id":"large-soul-of-an-intrepid-hero","kind":"item","name":"Large Soul of an Intrepid Hero","page":"Large Soul of an Intrepid Hero","img":"assets/img/Large_Soul_of_an_Intrepid_Hero.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Consume to acquire 2,500 souls.","buy":null,"sell":2500,"held":99,"desc":"Large soul found in the corpse of an intrepid hero.\nUse to acquire a great helping of souls.\nLet the Fire Keeper transform this sovereignless soul into a source of strength, for to be Unkindled is to be a vessel for souls.","avail":"<p>Can only be obtained in NG+ onward, where it replaces the <a data-e=\"large-soul-of-an-unknown-traveler\">Large Soul of an Unknown Traveler<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 2,500 souls.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Large_Soul_of_an_Intrepid_Hero"},{"id":"large-soul-of-an-unknown-traveler","kind":"item","name":"Large Soul of an Unknown Traveler","page":"Large Soul of an Unknown Traveler","img":"assets/img/Large_Soul_of_an_Unknown_Traveler.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Consume to acquire 1,000 souls.","buy":null,"sell":1000,"held":99,"desc":"A large soul found in the corpse of an unknown traveler.\nUse to acquire souls.\nLet the Fire Keeper transform this sovereignless soul into a source of strength, for to be Unkindled is to be a vessel for souls.","avail":"<p>A total of nineteen can be obtained per playthrough.<\/p><ul><li><a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Road of Sacrifices<\/a><ul><li>On a corpse at the far end of the Crucifixion Woods, adjacent to the dry land where the Exile Watchdogs are fought. To the left of the stairs that lead to the ladder down to <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a>, a corpse is holding the item.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a><ul><li>On the path to the cathedral from the bonfire immediately after the <a data-e=\"crystal-sage\">Crystal Sage<\/a>, there is a wooded area guarded by three crossbow-wielding Devout of the Deep and several Starved Hounds. On one of the upper cliffs of this area is a corpse propped against a wall holding the consumable.<\/li><li>Two are found on corpses in the rooftop mausoleum, near the white birch tree guarded by the <a data-e=\"giant-archer-of-the-undead-settlement\">Giant Archer of the Undead Settlement<\/a>.<\/li><li>On the cathedral rooftops past the mausoleum, on a corpse propped up against a railing of a circular courtyard immediately past some walkways. The area is patrolled by numerous Thralls and Devout of the Deep, including two clinging to the outside of the railings close to the corpse that will climb over and ambush the player should they attempt to approach the corpse.<\/li><li>Inside of the cathedral, near the second shortcut that leads back to the Cleansing Chapel bonfire, is a side area patrolled by a Cathedral Knight and two Thralls. Near them is a corpse holding the item.<\/li><li>Under the second Giant Slave are several corpses holding items that are guarded by multiple Writhing Rotten Flesh. One of the corpses holds the soul item, while others hold the <a data-e=\"drang-set\">Drang Set<\/a> and other treasures.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a><ul><li>In the deep water patrolled by a Great Crab near the door that opens after extinguishing the three flames, is a white birch tree guarded by the Giant Archer of the Undead Settlement. One of the corpses in this area holds the soul item.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"catacombs-of-carthus\">Catacombs of Carthus<\/a><ul><li>At the bottom of the large stairway that leads into the second half of the catacombs, past the reviving <a data-e=\"carthus-curved-greatsword\">curved greatsword<\/a>-wielding Skeleton Swordsman, there is a hallway with a pressure plate trap guarded by two <a data-e=\"carthus-curved-sword\">sword<\/a> and <a data-e=\"carthus-shield\">Carthus Shield<\/a>-wielding Skeleton Swordsmen. Immediately to the left of the pressure plate trap is a corpse that the item can be looted from.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a><ul><li>Immediately after the Snowfield bonfire, a corpse in the distance holding the item can be seen. Approaching the corpse directly will cause a <a data-e=\"follower-javelin\">javelin<\/a>-wielding Farron Follower to throw a projectile at the player.<\/li><li>After falling into the snowfield proper from the collapsing snowbank, loop to the right to return to the bonfire via a side path guarded by Birch Women and Farron Followers. On the path up towards the top of the cliff, a corpse holding the soul item can be found.<\/li><li>In the open area where the Gravetender Greatwolf is first fought, there is a corpse holding the consumable that is guarded by several Wolves.<\/li><li>On the path towards the decrepit village patrolled by Millwood Knights, after the first encounter with the Gravetender Greatwolf, there is a corpse at the base of a tree on the cliff's edge. The item can be looted from this corpse.<\/li><li>After the second encounter with the Gravetender Greatwolf, there is a collapsing snowbank that eventually leads to the Rope Bridge Cave. On the series of drop-downs there is a corpse on one of the ledges holding the item.<\/li><li>Immediately after the ice slide that leads from the Rope Bridge Cave to the Corvian Settlement, hook a hard right and follow the wall towards the cliff ledge, where a hidden corpse holds the soul item.<\/li><li>Found on a corpse in the riverbed leading into the Corvian Settlement. The first Corvian Knight is encountered immediately prior to this corpse.<\/li><li>Hanging from a window above the Corvian Settlement bonfire is a corpse holding the consumable. It can be reached by turning left after the bridge over the riverbed and navigating a cliff pathway.<\/li><li>After encountering the first <a data-e=\"crow-quills\">rapier<\/a>-wielding Corvian Knight and turning right to navigate the cliffside buildings, a Toxic-breathing Corvian is encountered right before a ladder leading to the village rooftops. To the left of the stairs leading up to this Corvian is a hidden corpse and another Corvian, with the corpse holding the item.<\/li><li>At the top of the previous ladder, a bridge can be crossed that leads to the building where the <a data-e=\"forlorn-corvian-settler\">Forlorn Corvian Settler<\/a> was met. On the same rooftop area where the <a data-e=\"crow-talons\">Crow Talons<\/a> can be found is a corpse holding the item.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 1,000 souls.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Large_Soul_of_an_Unknown_Traveler"},{"id":"large-titanite-shard","kind":"item","name":"Large Titanite Shard","page":"Large Titanite Shard (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Large_Titanite_Shard__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Upgrade material","usage":"Reinforces normal weapons from +3 up to +6.","buy":4000,"sell":300,"held":99,"desc":"Titanite shard for weapon reinforcement.\nReinforces weapons to +6.\nTitanite shards are fragments of\nthe Legendary Slabs. Titanite is\netched into weapons to reinforce.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><ul><li>One can be obtained by trading either a <a data-e=\"firebomb\">Firebomb<\/a> or a <a data-e=\"rope-firebomb\">Rope Firebomb<\/a> with Pickle Pee (only once per playthrough).<\/li><li>An unlimited amount can be bought from the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> once she is given the <a data-e=\"easterners-ashes\">Easterner's Ashes<\/a> for 4,000 souls each.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">High Wall of Lothric<\/a><ul><li>Guaranteed drop from Lothric Wyvern.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"smouldering-lake\">Smouldering Lake<\/a><ul><li>Five are found on corpses scattered along the lake area.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a><ul><li>Guaranteed drop from Silver Knights. (×2)<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a><ul><li>Guaranteed drop from Giant Slaves (one each).<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"catacombs-of-carthus\">Catacombs of Carthus<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Skeleton Wheels.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a><ul><li>Three are dropped by the Gravetender Greatwolf each time it is encountered before its boss fight.<\/li><li>Can be dropped by Farron Followers.<\/li><li>Sometimes dropped by Corvian Knights.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by the Lothric Knights (both red and blue varieties; one to two shards)<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Reinforces normal weapons from +3 up to +6.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Large_Titanite_Shard_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"lift-chamber-key","kind":"item","name":"Lift Chamber Key","page":"Lift Chamber Key","img":"assets/img/Lift_Chamber_Key.webp","sub":"Key item","usage":"Unlocks the lift in the High Wall of Lothric.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":99,"desc":"Key to the room of the lift that descends to the deepest dungeon in Lothric.\nA surviving Darkwraith, from the land swallowed by darkness, is said to be held here.","avail":"<p>Obtained from <a data-e=\"ringfinger-leonhard\">Ringfinger Leonhard<\/a> when spoken to after obtaining a <a data-e=\"pale-tongue\">Pale Tongue<\/a> (can be found in <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a> and <a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a> or dropped by Darkwraiths in <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a>).<\/p>","use":"<p>Unlocks the door to a lift in the <a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">High Wall of Lothric<\/a>. The door can be found downstairs from the Tower on the Wall bonfire, opposite to a halberd-wielding hollow, and takes the player down to a hidden chamber with a Darkwraith that drops the <a data-e=\"red-eye-orb\">Red Eye Orb<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Lift_Chamber_Key"},{"id":"lightning-bolt","kind":"item","name":"Lightning Bolt","page":"Lightning Bolt (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Lightning_Bolt__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Ammunition","usage":"Inflicts 110 lightning damage.","buy":300,"sell":3,"held":99,"desc":"Bolts imbued with lightning created by the giant blacksmith of the gods.\nHowever, the gods never used crossbows.\nThese bolts are likely artifacts of the dragonless era, when the pact between gods and humans was upheld.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"greirat-of-the-undead-settlement\">Greirat of the Undead Settlement<\/a> when he returns from his pillaging journey to <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a>.<\/li><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> if given <a data-e=\"greirats-ashes\">Greirat's Ashes<\/a>, provided that he returned successfully from his first pillaging journey.<\/li><li>Ten bolts can be found in the <a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a>, on a wooden roof only accessible by climbing a ladder located near the Mimic that drops <a data-e=\"dragonslayer-lightning-arrow\">Dragonslayer Lightning Arrows<\/a>, in a small passage near the feet of the chained Giant Slave.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Lightning Bolts inflict lightning damage, dealing additional damage to most enemies, especially those which are weak to this element. Likewise, the additional damage is greatly reduced on enemies resistant to lightning.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Lightning_Bolt_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"lightning-gem","kind":"item","name":"Lightning Gem","page":"Lightning Gem","img":"assets/img/Lightning_Gem.webp","sub":"Upgrade material","usage":"Used in infusion to create lightning weapons.","buy":null,"sell":500,"held":99,"desc":"A gem of infused titanite. Found in the aftermath of dragon hunts.\nUsed in infusion to create lightning weapons.\nLightning weapons inflict lightning damage, and scale with faith.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><ul><li>One can be obtained by trading the Xanthous Crown with Pickle Pee (only once per playthrough).<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a><ul><li>At the end of the main street, near the Church of Yorshka.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Lothric Knights.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"archdragon-peak\">Archdragon Peak<\/a><ul><li>One is found at the top of the large stone outcropping near the area where the player spawns upon entering from <a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a>.<\/li><li>Dropped by Man Serpents.<\/li><li>Dropped by Giant Man Serpents.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Pygmies.<\/li><li>Found in a side room in the Shared Grave area, in the area under the Crystal Lizard trap.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Infuses a weapon with Lightning damage as well as granting Faith scaling, but reducing Strength and Dexterity scaling, as well as reducing base damage. Scaling soft caps at 40 Faith.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Lightning_Gem"},{"id":"lightning-urn","kind":"item","name":"Lightning Urn","page":"Lightning Urn (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Lightning_Urn__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Explodes upon contact, inflicting lightning damage.","buy":700,"sell":100,"held":20,"desc":"Dragon-hunting tool used by Lothric knights. Explodes upon contact, inflicting lightning damage.\nThe knights of Lothric have since tamed dragons, but were once hunters of dragons themselves.\nThis explains their special hunting gear, and why they worshipped the sun.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><ul><li>Six are sold by <a data-e=\"greirat-of-the-undead-settlement\">Greirat of the Undead Settlement<\/a> once he returns from pillaging the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a>.<\/li><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 700 souls each, once she has been given <a data-e=\"greirats-ashes\">Greirat's Ashes<\/a> after he was sent to pillage <a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a><ul><li>Three are found in the moat guarded by the two Lothric Wyverns, behind some crates in the room before fighting the Hollow Assassins.<\/li><li>Six are found on a corpse immediately past the bridge under the left-side (white) Wyvern, which can only be safely retrieved once the wyverns are defeated.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"archdragon-peak\">Archdragon Peak<\/a><ul><li>Four are found within the <a data-e=\"ancient-wyvern\">Ancient Wyvern<\/a> arena. On the path to the left, prior to the building where the first Man Serpents in the arena are encountered, a corpse to the left of the entrance holds the items.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-dreg-heap\">The Dreg Heap<\/a><ul><li>Four are found on a corpse laying next to the first building after encountering the first Angel, before entering the chapel with the two Lothric Knights. A Murkman will attempt to ambush the player nearby.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Inflicts 150 Lightning damage, scaling with the wielder's Faith. If it explodes on a watery surface, it generates a shockwave that inflicts 80 Lightning damage in an area shortly after impact.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Lightning_Urn_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"logans-scroll","kind":"item","name":"Logan's Scroll","page":"Logan's Scroll","img":"assets/img/Logan_s_Scroll.webp","sub":"Spell book","usage":"Give to Orbeck of Vinheim to to learn Big Hat Logan's sorceries.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Secret scroll of the Profaned Capital court sorcerers, containing sorceries of Logan.\nGive to a sorcerer to learn Logan's Sorceries.\nThe court sorcerers used this scroll to claim heirship to Logan's legacy, though how that claim stands up to closer scrutiny is another story.","avail":"<p>Dropped by the Court Sorcerer Eamon in the <a data-e=\"profaned-capital\">Profaned Capital<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Give to <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a> in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> to upgrade his stock of sorceries:<\/p><table><tr><th>Quantity<\/th><th>Item<\/th><th>Cost<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"homing-soulmass\">Homing Soulmass<\/a><\/td><td>6,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"soul-spear\">Soul Spear<\/a><\/td><td>5,000<\/td><\/tr><\/table>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Logan's_Scroll"},{"id":"londor-braille-divine-tome","kind":"item","name":"Londor Braille Divine Tome","page":"Londor Braille Divine Tome","img":"assets/img/Londor_Braille_Divine_Tome.webp","sub":"Spell book","usage":"Give to either Irina or Karla to learn miracles of Londor.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"A braille tome of Londor, first spoken by Liliane of the Sable Church.\nGive this to a storyteller to learn miracles of Londor.\nThis is a forbidden tome, as it offers salvation to all Hollows, and conversely curses all things living.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"yuria-of-londor\">Yuria of Londor<\/a> for 50 souls in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>The tome can be given to either <a data-e=\"irina-of-carim\">Irina of Carim<\/a> or <a data-e=\"karla\">Karla<\/a> in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a>. Once done, the character who received the tome will add the following Dark Miracles to their stock:<\/p><table><tr><th>Available<\/th><th>Item<\/th><th>Cost<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"dark-blade\">Dark Blade<\/a><\/td><td>10,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"vow-of-silence\">Vow of Silence<\/a><\/td><td>15,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"dead-again\">Dead Again<\/a><\/td><td>5,000<\/td><\/tr><\/table>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Londor_Braille_Divine_Tome"},{"id":"lorettas-bone","kind":"item","name":"Loretta's Bone","page":"Loretta's Bone","img":"assets/img/Loretta_s_Bone.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Give to Greirat to progress in his questline.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":99,"desc":"Old, discolored human bone with several holes bored into it.\nA woman's corpse in the Undead Settlement was found clutching this bone. Her name was Loretta.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a>, on a corpse hanging on the balcony of the first house after the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a> bonfire. The player needs to cut the body's ropes to make it fall, preferably by using a long reach weapon. The body can be looted once they have made their way to ground level.<\/p>","use":"<ul><li>Give to <a data-e=\"greirat-of-the-undead-settlement\">Greirat<\/a> in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> to progress through his questline.<\/li><li>Can be traded with Pickle Pee in exchange for a <a data-e=\"ring-of-sacrifice\">Ring of Sacrifice<\/a> (only once per playthrough).<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Loretta's_Bone"},{"id":"millwood-greatarrow","kind":"item","name":"Millwood Greatarrow","page":"Millwood Greatarrow","img":"assets/img/Millwood_Greatarrow.webp","sub":"Ammunition","usage":"Deal 97 physical damage to target.","buy":800,"sell":30,"held":30,"desc":"Heavy, sturdy greatarrows made of black oak that deal heavy damage but have limited range.\nCan only be fired using a greatbow.\nIt is said that the Millwood Knights used these to face their sworn enemy, the Abyss Dragon.","avail":"<ul><li>Purchased from the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 800 souls after giving her the <a data-e=\"captains-ashes\">Captain's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><li>5 are found on a corpse alongside the <a data-e=\"millwood-greatbow\">Millwood Greatbow<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Millwood Greatarrows function much like <a data-e=\"large-arrow\">Large Arrows<\/a> do for conventional bows, in that they deal more damage, but reduce the bow's effective range.<\/p><p>Care should be taken when using these arrows, as like <a data-e=\"onislayer-greatarrow\">Onislayer Greatarrows<\/a>, they are incapable of knocking down their targets, with the only exception being certain weaker enemies upon headshot. As such, they should primarily be used to inflict damage on targets rather than attempting to displace them.<\/p><p>Because of the slow drawing nature of greatbows, it is ideal to equip the <a data-e=\"hawk-ring\">Hawk Ring<\/a>, fire the arrows from an <a data-e=\"onislayer-greatbow\">Onislayer Greatbow<\/a> or fire the arrow using the Puncturing Arrow skill, in order to counter the reduced effective range of the greatarrows.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Millwood_Greatarrow"},{"id":"molotov-cocktail","kind":"item","name":"Molotov Cocktail","page":"Molotov Cocktail (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Molotov_Cocktail__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"-","buy":null,"sell":null,"held":null,"desc":"","avail":"","use":"","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Molotov_Cocktail_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"moonlight-arrow","kind":"item","name":"Moonlight Arrow","page":"Moonlight Arrow (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Moonlight_Arrow__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Ammunition","usage":"Deals 75 Magic damage to target.","buy":500,"sell":3,"held":99,"desc":"Magical arrows said to have been used by the Darkmoon Knights.\nImbued with a silver light, these arrows inflict magic damage.\nIt is said that long ago the God of the Darkmoon Gwyndolin wielded these arrows with a matching golden bow.","avail":"<p><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><\/p><ul><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"greirat-of-the-undead-settlement\">Greirat of the Undead Settlement<\/a> after he successfully returns from pillaging <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a>.<ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> after she is given <a data-e=\"greirats-ashes\">Greirat's Ashes<\/a>, provided they are obtained after he has returned from his second pillaging journey.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul><p><a data-e=\"anor-londo\">Anor Londo<\/a><\/p><ul><li>×6 are found on a ledge inside the cathedral.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Moonlight Arrows deal Magic damage, this makes them useful for fighting enemies with shields, or who are resistant to thrusting damage. In addition, the damage output of these arrows is augmented when fired with the <a data-e=\"darkmoon-longbow\">Darkmoon Longbow<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Moonlight_Arrow_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"morticians-ashes","kind":"item","name":"Mortician's Ashes","page":"Mortician's Ashes","img":"assets/img/Mortician_s_Ashes.webp","sub":"Merchant ashes","usage":"Give to the Shrine Handmaid to increase her inventory.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Umbral ash of a resident of the Undead Settlement who made a living burying corpses.\nWith this, the shrine handmaid will prepare new items.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a>.<\/p><p>From the Dilapidated Bridge, head forward to the cemetery where the <a data-e=\"giant-archer-of-the-undead-settlement\">giant archer's<\/a> arrows rain down. Instead of entering the house on the far end, turn left and head uphill. The ashes are found on a body lying next to a tree.<\/p><p>The player may opt to befriend or kill the giant first to avoid being harassed by the falling arrows while scouting around.<\/p>","use":"<p>Extends the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a>'s inventory to include the following items:<\/p><table><tr><th>Available<\/th><th>Item<\/th><th>Cost<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>6<\/td><td><a data-e=\"alluring-skull\">Alluring Skull<\/a><\/td><td>500<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"charcoal-pine-bundle\">Charcoal Pine Bundle<\/a><\/td><td>300<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"charcoal-pine-resin\">Charcoal Pine Resin<\/a><\/td><td>500<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>3<\/td><td><a data-e=\"ember\">Ember<\/a><\/td><td>2,500<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"grave-key\">Grave Key<\/a><\/td><td>1,500<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>3<\/td><td><a data-e=\"human-pine-resin\">Human Pine Resin<\/a><\/td><td>1,500<\/td><\/tr><\/table>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Mortician's_Ashes"},{"id":"mossfruit","kind":"item","name":"Mossfruit","page":"Mossfruit","img":"assets/img/Mossfruit.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Temporarily boosts bleed, poison, frost, and curse resistance.","buy":null,"sell":100,"held":10,"desc":"A small clump of mossfruit.\nTemporarily boosts bleed, poison, frost, and curse resistance.\nAll mossfruit is the same regardless of its color, and has the effects of moss of all colors.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 1,500 souls each, once she has been given the <a data-e=\"easterners-ashes\">Easterner's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><li>Found in <a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a>.<\/li><li>Dropped by Basilisks.<\/li><li>Dropped by Wolves.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Increases Bleed, Poison, Frost, and Curse resistances by 80 for 60 seconds.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Mossfruit"},{"id":"mound-makers-item","kind":"item","name":"Mound-makers","page":"Mound-makers (item)","img":"assets/img/Mound_makers__item.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Equip to join the Mound-makers covenant.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":null,"desc":"A malformed vertebra found by the mad, with a queer symbol on its inside, proof of the shackles of the Gods. Equip to pledge oneself to the Mound-makers covenant.\nThe mound-makers wish only to add to their mounds, becoming mad spirits whether summoned as co-operators or invaders.\nThey are blithe to those around them, for in their minds, any kill might lead to another shackle.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a>. Given by <a data-e=\"holy-knight-hodrick\">Holy Knight Hodrick<\/a> after talking to him in the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Pit of Hollows<\/a>.<\/p><p>From the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a> bonfire, proceed through the level and in the big open area with praying Peasant Hollows and an Evangelist, turn right toward the stables. Instead of entering, break the crates on the right to uncover a hidden path guarded by numerous Thralls. Proceed through the area and drop to the other side, where a non-hostile Hollow Manservant with an empty cage paces about. Interact with the cage to be transported to the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Pit of Hollows<\/a>, where Hodrick awaits besides the <a data-e=\"mound-makers\">Mound-makers<\/a>' Sacrificial Altar.<\/p><p>Should the player have defeated the <a data-e=\"curse-rotted-greatwood\">Curse-rotted Greatwood<\/a>, this item is dropped by Hodrick when he is defeated alongside <a data-e=\"sirris-of-the-sunless-realms\">Sirris of the Sunless Realms<\/a> during her questline.<\/p>","use":"<p>Equip to pledge oneself to the <a data-e=\"mound-makers\">Mound-makers<\/a> covenant.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Mound-makers_(item)"},{"id":"old-cell-key","kind":"item","name":"Old Cell Key","page":"Old Cell Key","img":"assets/img/Old_Cell_Key.webp","sub":"Key item","usage":"Unlocks the oldest cell in the Profaned Capital.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Key to the oldest cell in the Irithyll dungeon.\nThe first prisoner of the dungeon was a lone giant. Cells for men were built at his feet.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a>, at the end of the sewage system inhabited by Hound Rats and opposite to a Mimic. Picking up the key unleashes several Basilisks in the area.<\/p>","use":"<p>Unlocks the oldest cell in the <a data-e=\"profaned-capital\">Profaned Capital<\/a>. From the <a data-e=\"profaned-capital\">Profaned Capital<\/a> bonfire, climb down the nearby ladder and proceed through the level until reaching a ruined church located among the toxic swamp. Climb up the ladder on the right and head forward until reaching the rooftops (fighting the Court Sorcerer along the way). Look for an open window nearby and jump inside. The cell can be found just ahead, with a body inside holding the <a data-e=\"covetous-gold-serpent-ring\">Covetous Gold Serpent Ring<\/a>.<\/p><p>If the player followed <a data-e=\"siegward-of-catarina\">Siegward<\/a>'s questline, he can also be found at this location and will present a <a data-e=\"titanite-slab\">Titanite Slab<\/a> in gratitude for freeing him.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Old_Cell_Key"},{"id":"old-womans-ashes","kind":"item","name":"Old Woman's Ashes","page":"Old Woman's Ashes","img":"assets/img/Old_Woman_s_Ashes.webp","sub":"Merchant ashes","usage":"Give to the Shrine Handmaid to increase her inventory.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Umbral ash of the old stone-humped woman.\nThings that have dreadfully run their course accrue at the great dreg-heap. This old woman was once the wet nurse of royalty.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"the-dreg-heap\">The Dreg Heap<\/a>, near the first bonfire:<\/p><ul><li>Dropped by the <a data-e=\"stone-humped-hag\">Stone-humped Hag<\/a>.<\/li><li>Also obtained from her corpse at the same location after reaching the Filianore's Rest bonfire.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Give to the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> to include items previously sold by the <a data-e=\"stone-humped-hag\">Stone-humped Hag<\/a> to her stock of wares.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Old_Woman's_Ashes"},{"id":"onislayer-greatarrow","kind":"item","name":"Onislayer Greatarrow","page":"Onislayer Greatarrow","img":"assets/img/Onislayer_Greatarrow.webp","sub":"Ammunition","usage":"Deal 60 physical damage to target.","buy":600,"sell":3,"held":30,"desc":"Large arrows used to destroy giant horned oni in an eastern land.\nCan only be used with greatbows.\nMade from the feathers of an aged crow, it is said that these arrows fly as straight as their master.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 600 souls each, once she has been given the <a data-e=\"easterners-ashes\">Easterner's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><li>8 are found in the <a data-e=\"profaned-capital\">Profaned Capital<\/a>, on the stone bridge patrolled by the Gargoyle that leads towards <a data-e=\"yhorm-the-giant\">Yhorm the Giant<\/a>'s boss arena, above where the <a data-e=\"onislayer-greatbow\">Onislayer Greatbow<\/a> is found.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Onislayer_Greatarrow"},{"id":"orbecks-ashes","kind":"item","name":"Orbeck's Ashes","page":"Orbeck's Ashes","img":"assets/img/Orbeck_s_Ashes.webp","sub":"Merchant ashes","usage":"• Give to the Shrine Handmaid to increase her inventory. • Give to Yuria to receive the Morion Blade.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Umbral ash of Orbeck of Vinheim. With this, the shrine handmaid will prepare new items.\nOrbeck was fascinated with sorcery but without means, so offered to serve as an assassin in exchange for acceptance into the Dragon Academy, believing that one day he could reinvent himself as a sorcerer.","avail":"<ul><li>Dropped by <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a>.<\/li><li>Alternatively, they can be found on Orbeck's corpse in the <a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a> upon the completion of his questline and defeating the <a data-e=\"lorian-elder-prince-and-lothric-younger-prince\">Twin Princes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<ul><li>Extends the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a>'s inventory to include items sold by Orbeck of Vinheim upon his death, i.e. his Sorceries.<\/li><li>Can be given to <a data-e=\"yuria-of-londor\">Yuria of Londor<\/a> to receive the <a data-e=\"morion-blade\">Morion Blade<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Orbeck's_Ashes"},{"id":"paladins-ashes","kind":"item","name":"Paladin's Ashes","page":"Paladin's Ashes","img":"assets/img/Paladin_s_Ashes.webp","sub":"Merchant ashes","usage":"Give to the Shrine Handmaid to increase her inventory.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Umbral ash of a worn-out paladin who sought the Cathedral of the Deep. With this, the shrine handmaid will prepare new items.\nThis paladin paid quite a price for his headstrong justice.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a>.<\/p><p>From the <a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a> bonfire, head toward the stairs and turn left, following a small path downhill. The ashes are located on a corpse lying on the far end, behind the Fallen Knight.<\/p>","use":"<p>Extends the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a>'s inventory to include the following items:<\/p><table><tr><th>Available<\/th><th>Item<\/th><th>Cost<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>4<\/td><td><a data-e=\"blooming-purple-moss-clump\">Blooming Purple Moss Clump<\/a><\/td><td>1,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"canvas-talisman\">Canvas Talisman<\/a><\/td><td>3,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"crescent-axe\">Crescent Axe<\/a><\/td><td>4,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"duel-charm\">Duel Charm<\/a><\/td><td>500<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"lloyds-shield-ring\">Lloyd's Shield Ring<\/a><\/td><td>2,500<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"morning-star\">Morning Star<\/a><\/td><td>2,500<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"undead-hunter-charm\">Undead Hunter Charm<\/a><\/td><td>500<\/td><\/tr><\/table>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Paladin's_Ashes"},{"id":"pale-pine-resin","kind":"item","name":"Pale Pine Resin","page":"Pale Pine Resin","img":"assets/img/Pale_Pine_Resin.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Temporarily applies magic to right-hand weapon.","buy":1000,"sell":100,"held":20,"desc":"Pale pine resin that faintly glimmers.\nTemporarily applies magic to right-hand weapon.\nThe blood red substance sometimes found within suggests there is more to this so-called resin than meets the eye.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 1,000 souls each, once she has been given the <a data-e=\"prisoner-chiefs-ashes\">Prisoner Chief's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Wretches.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a><ul><li>1 found on a corpse inside the room before the lever that raises the main gate to the castle, near the Mimic that drops three <a data-e=\"titanite-scale\">Titanite Scales<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Adds 90 Magic damage to right-hand weapon for 60 seconds.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Pale_Pine_Resin"},{"id":"pale-tongue","kind":"item","name":"Pale Tongue","page":"Pale Tongue","img":"assets/img/Pale_Tongue.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Give to Rosaria to either reallocate attributes, change appearance, or rank up in Rosaria's Fingers.","buy":null,"sell":10,"held":99,"desc":"Proof of a red orb invader's victory over a Host of Embers.\nClaiming tongues as trophies was originally the practice of an infamous troupe of invaders, who offered them to their speechless goddess.","avail":"<h4>Single player<\/h4><ul><li><a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a><ul><li>In the same area where the Demon is encountered, can be looted from the leftmost hanging corpse. The corpses can be dropped by using the piece of ceiling debris below as a stepping platform or via ranged attacks.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a><ul><li>In the sludge at the feet of the Giant Slave that is sleeping next to the stairway that leads to the prayer area before <a data-e=\"deacons-of-the-deep\">Deacons of the Deep<\/a>.<\/li><li>On the roof area, outside of the entrance to the rafters. It is being guarded by two Thralls.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Darkwraiths.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul><h4>Online play<\/h4><ul><li>Gained through successful invasions whilst in the <a data-e=\"rosarias-fingers\">Rosaria's Fingers<\/a> covenant.<\/li><li>Obtained by invading other players while not wearing any of the covenant items.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<ul><li>Offered to Saint Rosaria to gain ranks within the <a data-e=\"rosarias-fingers\">Rosaria's Fingers<\/a> covenant.<\/li><li>Offering one to Rosaria allows the player to respec attributes or change appearance up to five times in a single playthrough.<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Pale_Tongue"},{"id":"patches-ashes","kind":"item","name":"Patches' Ashes","page":"Patches' Ashes","img":"assets/img/Patches__Ashes.webp","sub":"Merchant ashes","usage":"Give to the Shrine Handmaid to increase her inventory.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Umbral ash of Unbreakable Patches. With this, the shrine handmaid will prepare new items.\nPatches never lost heart, and never looked back.\nHe marched in one direction, and that direction was dead ahead. Did you see him passing by?","avail":"<p>Dropped by <a data-e=\"unbreakable-patches\">Unbreakable Patches<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Extends the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a>'s inventory to include items initially sold by <a data-e=\"unbreakable-patches\">Patches<\/a>.<\/p><table><tr><th>Available<\/th><th>Item<\/th><th>Cost<\/th><\/tr><tr><td><\/td><td><a data-e=\"alluring-skull\">Alluring Skull<\/a><\/td><td>800<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><\/td><td>Black Leather Armor<\/td><td>2,500<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><\/td><td>Black Leather Boots<\/td><td>2,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><\/td><td>Black Leather Gloves<\/td><td>2,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>4<\/td><td><a data-e=\"ember\">Ember<\/a><\/td><td>5,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><\/td><td><a data-e=\"firebomb\">Firebomb<\/a><\/td><td>300<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><\/td><td><a data-e=\"human-pine-resin\">Human Pine Resin<\/a><\/td><td>1,500<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><\/td><td><a data-e=\"parrying-dagger\">Parrying Dagger<\/a><\/td><td>2,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><\/td><td><a data-e=\"red-bug-pellet\">Red Bug Pellet<\/a><\/td><td>1,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><\/td><td><a data-e=\"rope-firebomb\">Rope Firebomb<\/a><\/td><td>300<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><\/td><td><a data-e=\"rubbish\">Rubbish<\/a><\/td><td>200<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><\/td><td><a data-e=\"rusted-coin\">Rusted Coin<\/a><\/td><td>200<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>2<\/td><td><a data-e=\"shotel\">Shotel<\/a><\/td><td>4,000<\/td><\/tr><\/table>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Patches'_Ashes"},{"id":"poison-arrow","kind":"item","name":"Poison Arrow","page":"Poison Arrow (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Poison_Arrow__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Ammunition","usage":"Deal 10 physical damage and 30 Poison build-up.","buy":120,"sell":1,"held":99,"desc":"Arrows with poisoned tips.\nInflict poison damage that gradually wears down foes.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"unbreakable-patches\">Unbreakable Patches<\/a>, once he becomes a merchant, for 120 souls each.<\/li><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 120 souls each, after she is given <a data-e=\"patches-ashes\">Patches' Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Poison arrows deal minor physical damage as well as causing 30 Poison build-up.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Poison_Arrow_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"poison-gem","kind":"item","name":"Poison Gem","page":"Poison Gem","img":"assets/img/Poison_Gem.webp","sub":"Upgrade material","usage":"Used in infusion to create poison weapons.","buy":null,"sell":300,"held":99,"desc":"A gem of infused titanite. Discovered in the rotted forest of Farron.\nUsed in infusion to create poison weapons.\nSuch weapons inflict poison-laced damage that gradually eats away at foes.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Ghrus (<a data-e=\"rotten-ghru-dagger\">dagger<\/a> and <a data-e=\"rotten-ghru-spear\">spear<\/a> wielders, and Mad Ghrus).<\/li><li>Dropped by Rotten Slugs.<\/li><li>Dropped by Elder Ghrus.<\/li><li>Found on a corpse guarded by a trio of Elder Ghrus near the Keep Ruins bonfire.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"profaned-capital\">Profaned Capital<\/a><ul><li>Found in the big cavern opposite to the ruined chapel in the toxic swamp.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a><ul><li>Found in a Giant Fly nest shortly past the Snowfield bonfire, guarded by a Giant Fly.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Infuses a weapon with Poison, allowing it to inflict the Poison status effect and increasing in effectiveness with the wielder's Luck. Weapons that innately inflict Poison build-up are granted increased build-up and improved Luck scaling.<\/p><p>Greatly reduces Strength, Dexterity, Intelligence and Faith scaling, as well as base damage.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Poison_Gem"},{"id":"poison-kukri","kind":"item","name":"Poison Kukri","page":"Poison Kukri","img":"assets/img/Poison_Kukri.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"-","buy":null,"sell":null,"held":null,"desc":"","avail":"","use":"","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Poison_Kukri"},{"id":"poison-throwing-knife","kind":"item","name":"Poison Throwing Knife","page":"Poison Throwing Knife (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Poison_Throwing_Knife__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Throw at enemies to inflict poison damage.","buy":100,"sell":10,"held":40,"desc":"A throwing knife dipped in poison.\nThrow at enemies to inflict poison damage.\nUsed by assassins of Londor, land of Hollows.\nThe poison is jokingly known as Hollow's blood.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"yuria-of-londor\">Yuria of Londor<\/a> for 100 souls.<ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> once she has been given <a data-e=\"yurias-ashes\">Yuria's Ashes<\/a> or the <a data-e=\"hollows-ashes\">Hollow's Ashes<\/a> (only one or the other may be obtained in a given playthrough).<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Throw at enemies to inflict 47 Thrust damage, scaling with the player's Strength and Dexterity, and increase target's Poison buildup by 25, scaling with the player's Luck. Knives do not stagger the target but can be thrown very quickly.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Poison_Throwing_Knife_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"prism-stone","kind":"item","name":"Prism Stone","page":"Prism Stone (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Prism_Stone__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Can be used as path markers.","buy":10,"sell":5,"held":99,"desc":"Warm pebble emitting a beautiful phasing aura of seven colors, with a very rare eighth.\nThe prism stone does nothing special, but can serve as a path marker, or perhaps dropped off a cliff to judge height by the sound of its descent. If a loud noise is heard upon its landing, then a fall from the ledge is surely lethal.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 10 souls each.<\/li><li>Ten can be found in the <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a>, looted from a corpse near the first brazier in the poison swamp.<\/li><li>Ten can be found in the <a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>When used, the player will drop one of these pebbles on the ground; each stone dropped will begin to sparkle in one of a few various colors, serving as a sort of marker. Known colors include: blue, green, purple, yellow, white and orange. What color a dropped stone will become is random and cannot be chosen.<\/p><p>They can also be dropped from ledges or cliffs in order to judge whether the player will survive a fall or not. If the stone emits a scream, then the drop is fatal.<\/p><p>In online play, Prism Stones can be useful for White Phantoms to guide hosts through levels, by signaling areas and items of interest (such as treasure chests and levers) or to provide trace amounts of light without equipping a <a data-e=\"torch\">Torch<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Prism_Stone_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"prisoner-chiefs-ashes","kind":"item","name":"Prisoner Chief's Ashes","page":"Prisoner Chief's Ashes","img":"assets/img/Prisoner_Chief_s_Ashes.webp","sub":"Merchant ashes","usage":"Give to the Shrine Handmaid to increase her inventory.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Umbral ash of the prisoner chief of the catacombs.\nWith this, the shrine handmaid will prepare new items.\nThe prisoner chief used his clout to hoard all manner of things, but died without putting them to use.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a>, on a corpse in one of the cells of the final cell block of the dungeon. The <a data-e=\"jailers-key-ring\">Jailer's Key Ring<\/a> is needed to unlock the door.<\/p>","use":"<p>Extends the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a>'s inventory to include the following items:<\/p><table><tr><th>Available<\/th><th>Item<\/th><th>Cost<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td>Karla's Coat<\/td><td>8,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td>Karla's Gloves<\/td><td>5,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td>Karla's Pointed Hat<\/td><td>5,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td>Karla's Trousers<\/td><td>5,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"pale-pine-resin\">Pale Pine Resin<\/a><\/td><td>1,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"rime-blue-moss-clump\">Rime-blue Moss Clump<\/a><\/td><td>500<\/td><\/tr><\/table>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Prisoner_Chief's_Ashes"},{"id":"profaned-coal","kind":"item","name":"Profaned Coal","page":"Profaned Coal","img":"assets/img/Profaned_Coal.webp","sub":"Coal","usage":"Give to Andre to infuse weapons with Dark, Blood or Hollow.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Coal used for weapon infusion.\nRemnants of the fire that burned down the Profaned Capital, preserved in an icy skull.\nGive to the blacksmith in the shrine to allow the use of gems for dark, blood, and hollow infusion.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a>, in the lower cell block that precedes the route to the <a data-e=\"profaned-capital\">Profaned Capital<\/a>. It is inside the cell containing several Wretches, just opposite of <a data-e=\"karla\">Karla<\/a>'s cell.<\/p>","use":"<p>Give the coal to <a data-e=\"blacksmith-andre\">Blacksmith Andre<\/a> in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> to allow usage of the following gems for infusions:<\/p><ul><li><a data-e=\"dark-gem\">Dark Gem<\/a> → Dark<\/li><li><a data-e=\"blood-gem\">Blood Gem<\/a> → Blood<\/li><li><a data-e=\"hollow-gem\">Hollow Gem<\/a> → Hollow<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Profaned_Coal"},{"id":"proof-of-a-concord-kept","kind":"item","name":"Proof of a Concord Kept","page":"Proof of a Concord Kept","img":"assets/img/Proof_of_a_Concord_Kept.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Used to rank up in the Blade of the Darkmoon and Blue Sentinels covenants.","buy":null,"sell":10,"held":99,"desc":"Blood-drained, shrunken ear.\nSouvenir taken for subduing the guilty.\nThe knights called the Blades of the Darkmoon punish the guilt-soaked offenders of the Gods and take this as proof of their conquest.\nThe earless corpses of the guilty will be left behind as a warning to others, inspiring both fear and respect for the Gods. Such is the eternal mandate of the Dark Sun.","avail":"<ul><li>Received as a reward for defeating the guilty (an invader) as a <a data-e=\"blade-of-the-darkmoon\">Blade of the Darkmoon<\/a> or <a data-e=\"blue-sentinels\">Blue Sentinel<\/a>.<\/li><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a><ul><li>One is found on a body lying next to a tree, outside of the <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Church of Yorshka<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"anor-londo\">Anor Londo<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Silver Knights.<\/li><li>One is found at the middle of the left staircase in the cathedral's main hall, next to three Deacons.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Give to <a data-e=\"company-captain-yorshka\">Captain Yorshka<\/a> in <a data-e=\"anor-londo\">Anor Londo<\/a> to rank up in the <a data-e=\"blade-of-the-darkmoon\">Blade of the Darkmoon<\/a> and <a data-e=\"blue-sentinels\">Blue Sentinels<\/a> covenants.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Proof_of_a_Concord_Kept"},{"id":"proof-of-a-concord-well-kept","kind":"item","name":"Proof of a Concord Well Kept","page":"Proof of a Concord Well Kept","img":"assets/img/Proof_of_a_Concord_Well_Kept.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Use to acquire two Proof of a Concord Kept.","buy":null,"sell":null,"held":99,"desc":"Distinguished proof that one has hunted the enemies of the gods, as per the ancient accord with the Way of Blue.\nThe layered ear of a dark spirit is the mark of a particularly guilty offender, one who has flagrantly violated one god or another.\nUse to acquire two Proof of a Concord Kept.","avail":"<p>As a <a data-e=\"blue-sentinels\">Blue Sentinel<\/a> or <a data-e=\"blade-of-the-darkmoon\">Darkmoon Blade<\/a> summoned into the world of a <a data-e=\"way-of-blue\">Way of Blue<\/a> adherent, this item is obtained by defeating a red invader who has equipped the <a data-e=\"aldrich-faithful-item\">Aldrich Faithful (item)<\/a> covenant item.<\/p>","use":"<p>Use to acquire two <a data-e=\"proof-of-a-concord-kept\">Proofs of a Concord Kept<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Proof_of_a_Concord_Well_Kept"},{"id":"purging-stone","kind":"item","name":"Purging Stone","page":"Purging Stone (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Purging_Stone__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Cures hollowing.","buy":"Varies","sell":500,"held":99,"desc":"Ash-colored stone encasing a skull.\nReduces undead curse build-up and cures hollowing.\nInhabitants of Londor, the land of Hollows, use this secret treasure to feign normalcy.\nOccasionally, a Hollow fools even himself, and turns on his own kind.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"yuria-of-londor\">Yuria of Londor<\/a> for 4,500 souls each.<ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for the same price once she is given <a data-e=\"yurias-ashes\">Yuria's Ashes<\/a>. If she is given the <a data-e=\"hollows-ashes\">Hollow's Ashes<\/a> instead, she will sell them for 3,000 souls.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li>Dropped by Sewer Centipedes.<\/li><li>Four can be found in the <a data-e=\"profaned-capital\">Profaned Capital<\/a>:<ul><li>One is found in the Toxic swamp with multiple Sewer Centipedes.<\/li><li>Three may be found inside the chapel containing three Monstrosities of Sin.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li>Two are found in <a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a>, on the path leading to the Ringed Inner Wall bonfire and guarded by multiple Undead Clerics.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Resets Hollowing to 0. Does not remove the <a data-e=\"dark-sigil\">Dark Sigil<\/a>, so Hollowing will still build up as a result of player death.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Purging_Stone_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"purple-moss-clump","kind":"item","name":"Purple Moss Clump","page":"Purple Moss Clump (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Purple_Moss_Clump__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Reduces poison buildup. Cures Poison status.","buy":500,"sell":50,"held":99,"desc":"Medicinal purple moss clump.\nReduces poison build-up. Cures poison.\nPoison builds up in the body, and when it breaks out, it causes gradual damage over a period of time.\nPoison can be exasperating, so be sure to carry sufficient moss clumps when traveling to a blighted area.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><ul><li>Six are sold initially by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 500 souls each.<\/li><li>The <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Handmaid<\/a> will sell an unlimited amount once she has been given the <a data-e=\"paladins-ashes\">Paladin's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Road of Sacrifices<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Lesser Crabs.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a><ul><li>From the <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a> bonfire, exit the building and turn right. The clumps are found on a corpse at the end of the path. (×3)<\/li><li>On top of one of the two broken bridge sections, near the area with the first brazier and opposite to the <a data-e=\"greatsword\">Greatsword<\/a>. (×4)<\/li><li>Found just in front of the second brazier. (×2)<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Reduces poison buildup. Cures Poison status.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Purple_Moss_Clump_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"quelana-pyromancy-tome","kind":"item","name":"Quelana Pyromancy Tome","page":"Quelana Pyromancy Tome","img":"assets/img/Quelana_Pyromancy_Tome.webp","sub":"Spell book","usage":"Give to Karla to learn Quelana's pyromancies.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"A pyromancy tome of Quelana containing her unique spells. These pyromancies can only be taught by a female master.\nGive to a female pyromancy master to learn Quelana's pyromancies.\nQuelana, the sole surviving witch of Izalith, once accepted a human pupil, but after the pupil moved on, she never took another.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"smouldering-lake\">Smouldering Lake<\/a>.<\/p><p>From the Old King's Antechamber bonfire, follow a nearby corridor (through a hidden wall) that leads to a room with two Demon Clerics. Drop down and follow a passageway nearby containing several Hound Rats. Hitting the wall directly opposite to this corridor reveals an illusory wall (the wall can be identified by a blue glow). The corpse of a giant spider-humanoid lies behind it, along with the tome.<\/p>","use":"<p>Giving the tome to <a data-e=\"karla\">Karla<\/a> in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> unlocks the following pyromancies for purchase:<\/p><ul><li><a data-e=\"fire-whip\">Fire Whip<\/a><\/li><li><a data-e=\"firestorm\">Firestorm<\/a><\/li><li><a data-e=\"rapport\">Rapport<\/a><\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Quelana_Pyromancy_Tome"},{"id":"raw-gem","kind":"item","name":"Raw Gem","page":"Raw Gem","img":"assets/img/Raw_Gem.webp","sub":"Upgrade material","usage":"Used in infusion to create raw weapons.","buy":null,"sell":150,"held":99,"desc":"A gem of infused titanite.\nForged the weapons of Lothric foot soldiers.\nUsed in infusion to create raw weapons.\nRaw weapons are easily wielded and have higher attack, but lose scaling effects.","avail":"<ul><li>Dropped by Hollow Soldiers<\/li><li>Dropped by a Crystal Lizard in the <a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">High Wall of Lothric<\/a>, on the rooftops, behind a Pus of Man.<\/li><li>Guarded by the <a data-e=\"undead-hunter-charm\">Undead Hunter Charm<\/a> throwing Hollow Soldier in <a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a> before the gate to the Dragonslayer Armor bossfight.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>When infusing a weapon with Raw, the weapon gains greatly increased base damage, but loses any and all scaling with Strength and Dexterity.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Raw_Gem"},{"id":"red-bug-pellet","kind":"item","name":"Red Bug Pellet","page":"Red Bug Pellet","img":"assets/img/Red_Bug_Pellet.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Boosts Fire damage absorption for 60 seconds.","buy":1000,"sell":200,"held":5,"desc":"Medicinal pellet made from crushed insects. The red type temporarily boosts fire damage absorption.\nPrepared in the Cathedral of the Deep by evangelists, who dole them out to followers to ease their suffering when they burn.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><ul><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"unbreakable-patches\">Unbreakable Patches<\/a> in for 1,000 souls each.<\/li><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for the same price if she is given <a data-e=\"patches-ashes\">Patches' Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Devouts of the Deep.<\/li><li>Dropped by Devout Bombers.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Boosts Fire damage absorption by 15% for 60 seconds, 10% in PvP.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Red_Bug_Pellet"},{"id":"red-eye-orb","kind":"item","name":"Red Eye Orb","page":"Red Eye Orb (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Red_Eye_Orb__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Online item","usage":"Invade other worlds at will.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Online play item.\nInvade other worlds at will.\nDefeat the Host of Embers of the world you have invaded to gain the strength of the fire.\nThe Red Eye Orb is rooted in a tiny land swallowed by darkness long ago. Some choose to put the orb to other uses. To embark on this path, enter the service of Rosaria in the Cathedral of the Deep.","avail":"<p>The player must defeat a Darkwraith located at the bottom of a tower in the <a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">High Wall of Lothric<\/a> after receiving the <a data-e=\"lift-chamber-key\">Lift Chamber Key<\/a> provided by <a data-e=\"ringfinger-leonhard\">Ringfinger Leonhard<\/a> once they have obtained a <a data-e=\"pale-tongue\">Pale Tongue<\/a>.<\/p><p>From the <a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">Tower on the Wall<\/a> bonfire, make way to the bottom of the tower and unlock the barred door with the key given by Leonhard. Ride the lift down and fight the Darkwraith there. The item will be automatically added to the player's inventory once he dies.<\/p>","use":"<p>Using this infinite consumable will allow a player to invade another player's world as a dark spirit. A Host of Embers can only be invaded in this manner if the boss for the area is still alive. Unlike in the first <i>Dark Souls<\/i>, usage of this item is not restricted to any specific covenant, and victory requirements will vary depending on the covenant that the player has pledged themselves to.<\/p><p>Invasion ranges can also vary depending on covenant status. In all cases, invasion range is based on the player's Soul Level.<\/p><table><tr><th>Invasion type<\/th><th>Lower Limit<\/th><th>Upper Limit<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>Red Spirit (below level 351)<\/td><td>90% of player's Soul Level<\/td><td>110% of player's Soul Level + 20<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><a data-e=\"mound-makers\">Mound-makers<\/a> (below level 351)<\/td><td>90% of player's Soul Level<\/td><td>115% of player's Soul Level + 20<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Any (level 351 and higher)<\/td><td>Soul Level 351<\/td><td>None<\/td><\/tr><\/table>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Red_Eye_Orb_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"red-sign-soapstone","kind":"item","name":"Red Sign Soapstone","page":"Red Sign Soapstone (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Red_Sign_Soapstone__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Online item","usage":"Create a hostile red invasion sign.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Online play item.\nCreate a hostile red invasion sign.\nBe summoned to another world as a dark spirit, and defeat the Host of Embers to gain the strength of fire.\nNot all dark spirits are unsporting, or they wouldn't make use of this soapstone.","avail":"<p>Obtained after killing the non-hostile Man-grub outside of <a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Rosaria's Bed Chamber<\/a> in the <a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Creates a red summon sign, allowing others to invite the player into their world as a dark spirit.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Red_Sign_Soapstone_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"refined-gem","kind":"item","name":"Refined Gem","page":"Refined Gem","img":"assets/img/Refined_Gem.webp","sub":"Upgrade material","usage":"Used in infusion to create refined weapons.","buy":5000,"sell":150,"held":99,"desc":"A gem of infused titanite.\nForged the weapons of Lothric knights.\nUsed in infusion to create refined weapons.\nRefined weapons are difficult to wield properly, and scale effectively with strength and dexterity.","avail":"<p><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><\/p><ul><li>x3 sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 5,000 souls apiece once she is given the <a data-e=\"captains-ashes\">Captain's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><p><a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">High Wall of Lothric<\/a><\/p><ul><li>×1 guaranteed drop per game cycle from the blue-caped Lothric Knight found outside <a data-e=\"emma-high-priestess-of-lothric-castle\">Emma<\/a>'s chapel.<ul><li>Afterward, the knight also has a rare chance to drop them as loot.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul><p><a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a><\/p><ul><li>×1 found between the two Lothric Wyverns.<\/li><li>Rare drop from Lothric Knights.<\/li><\/ul><p><a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a><\/p><ul><li>×1 dropped by the Crystal Lizard on the sixth floor, before exiting to the roofs section.<\/li><li>Dropped by red-eyed Lothric Knights.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Can be used to create Refined weapons through <a data-e=\"blacksmith-andre\">Blacksmith Andre<\/a> in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a>.<\/p><p>Infusing a weapon with a Refined Gem will increase the scaling bonuses from both Strength and Dexterity, without compromising one or the other, while also equalizing their scaling. While it does also lower the weapon's base damage slightly, the improved scaling bonuses, in most cases, will result in an overall damage increase.<\/p><p>Refined infusions are a solid choice if a player is utilizing a quality build, where Strength and Dexterity are leveled equally. Furthermore, Refined weapons are still able to be fully buffed by resins, bundles, or spells.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Refined_Gem"},{"id":"repair-powder","kind":"item","name":"Repair Powder","page":"Repair Powder (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Repair_Powder__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Repairs equipped weapons and armor, as long as they are not broken.","buy":"Varies","sell":200,"held":20,"desc":"Lightly enchanted golden powder.\nRepairs equipped weapons and armor, as long as they haven't already broken.\nUse of a weapon depletes its durability, eventually causing it to break.\nAs long as a weapon is not broken, its durability can be restored at a bonfire, but for distant journeys, one may wish to prepare ahead.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 600 souls each.<\/li><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"greirat-of-the-undead-settlement\">Greirat of the Undead Settlement<\/a> for 300 souls once he has returned from pillaging the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a>. The Shrine Handmaid will update her stock to sell at the reduced price once she has been given <a data-e=\"greirats-ashes\">Greirat's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><li><a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a><ul><li>Two are found on a corpse on the second floor of the first building filled with Thralls, around the corner from the corpse holding <a data-e=\"lorettas-bone\">Loretta's Bone<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a><ul><li>Four are found on a corpse in the swamp where Yellowfinger Heysel invades, in the shallow swamp infested with Basilisks and close to the cave containing the <a data-e=\"antiquated-set\">Antiquated Set<\/a> and <a data-e=\"golden-scroll\">Golden Scroll<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a><ul><li>Three can be found on a corpse in the area where the white birch tree sits, guarded by the <a data-e=\"giant-archer-of-the-undead-settlement\">Giant Archer of the Undead Settlement<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Restores 150 durability to all equipped weapons and armor. Weapons that are fully broken cannot have durability restored.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Repair_Powder_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"rime-blue-moss-clump","kind":"item","name":"Rime-blue Moss Clump","page":"Rime-blue Moss Clump","img":"assets/img/Rime_blue_Moss_Clump.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Reduces Frost build-up. Cures Frostbite status.","buy":500,"sell":50,"held":99,"desc":"Moss clump radiating gentle heat and light.\nReduces frost build-up. Cures frostbite status.\nFrost accumulates in the body causing frostbite, which sap one's health, lowers absorption, and slows stamina recovery.\nWeapons imbued with frost are a rare thing indeed, most of them originating in the Boreal Valley.","avail":"<p>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 500 souls each, once she has been given the <a data-e=\"prisoner-chiefs-ashes\">Prisoner Chief's Ashes<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>These clumps can be especially useful in PvP action against an opponent who uses a Frost imbued weapon, or on PvE enemies, most notably those residing in the <a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a> The simple lack of stamina recovery and increase in damage received could end one's battle quicker than expected.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Rime-blue_Moss_Clump"},{"id":"ritual-spear-fragment","kind":"item","name":"Ritual Spear Fragment","page":"Ritual Spear Fragment","img":"assets/img/Ritual_Spear_Fragment.webp","sub":"Online item","usage":"Summons a row of upward-thrusting ritual spears.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Online play item.\nA fragment of the matching ritual spears once held by the knights of Princess Filianore.\nThey are the namesake of the Spears of the Church.\nWhen Spears of the Church face unduly treacherous foes, this allows them to draw upon former majesty, and summon a row of upward-thrusting ritual spears.","avail":"<p>Found on a corpse outside of the <a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">Church of Filianore<\/a>, near the <a data-e=\"ringed-knight-paired-greatswords\">greatswords<\/a>-wielding Ringed Knight.<\/p>","use":"<p>Upon use, the wielder brandishes their weapon forward, gaining the Perseverance effect immediately upon item use. After a short delay, during which the ground in front of the wielder glows, a row of upwardly-thrusting spears encased in lightning are conjured, surging forward. The spears persist for several seconds, acting as a barrier that damages foes that walk into them, though allowing free movement to the wielder.<\/p><p>This item does not require Focus Points to cast, but has a cooldown inbetween uses. The cooldown reduces in tandem with the number of summoned phantoms present.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Ritual_Spear_Fragment"},{"id":"rope-black-firebomb","kind":"item","name":"Rope Black Firebomb","page":"Rope Black Firebomb","img":"assets/img/Rope_Black_Firebomb.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"A black firebomb that is thrown behind, inflicting great fire damage.","buy":300,"sell":100,"held":10,"desc":"Black bisque urn attached to a string and filled with black powder.\nThrown behind and explodes, inflicting fire damage.\nNo different to a black firebomb, save for the direction in which is is thrown. Enables a different fighting style, and flexibility in adjusting to one's circumstances.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"unbreakable-patches\">Unbreakable Patches<\/a> for 300 souls each.<\/li><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> once she has been given <a data-e=\"patches-ashes\">Patches' Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Rope Black Firebombs are specifically designed to help players escape from chasing enemies. Their odd behavior gives them some versatility and players may use them in imaginative ways in online matches, as their usage is commonly non-expected.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Rope_Black_Firebomb"},{"id":"rope-firebomb","kind":"item","name":"Rope Firebomb","page":"Rope Firebomb","img":"assets/img/Rope_Firebomb.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"A firebomb that is thrown behind, inflicting fire damage.","buy":null,"sell":10,"held":10,"desc":"Bisque urn attached to a string and filled with black powder.\nThrown behind and explodes, inflicting fire damage.\nNo different to a firebomb, save for the direction in which is is thrown. Enables a different fighting style, and flexibility in adjusting to one's circumstances.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"greirat-of-the-undead-settlement\">Greirat of the Undead Settlement<\/a> for 50 souls each.<\/p>","use":"<p>Rope Firebombs are specifically designed to help players escape from chasing enemies. Their odd behavior gives them some versatility and players may use them in imaginative ways in online matches, as their usage is commonly non-expected.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Rope_Firebomb"},{"id":"rosarias-fingers-item","kind":"item","name":"Rosaria's Fingers","page":"Rosaria's Fingers (item)","img":"assets/img/Rosaria_s_Fingers__item.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Equip to join the Rosaria's Fingers covenant.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":null,"desc":"Sacred seal of Archdeacon Klimt, who served Rosaria, Mother of Rebirth. Equip to pledge oneself to the Rosaria's Fingers covenant.\nRosaria's Fingers collect tongues in her name. Some do it to be reborn; others do it to help comfort their voiceless goddess.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a>.<\/p><p>Given by Saint Rosaria in Rosaria's Bed Chamber after talking to her and accepting to join the <a data-e=\"rosarias-fingers\">Rosaria's Fingers<\/a> covenant.<\/p>","use":"<p>Equip to pledge oneself to the Rosaria's Fingers covenant.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Rosaria's_Fingers_(item)"},{"id":"roster-of-knights","kind":"item","name":"Roster of Knights","page":"Roster of Knights","img":"assets/img/Roster_of_Knights.webp","sub":"Online item","usage":"Allows to check the Blade of the Darkmoon leaderboard.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Online play item. A roster of knights of the Darkmoon who have served since the age of the old Royals.\nUse to discover the names of Darkmoon Knights, an order of elite knights shrouded in shadows.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a>. From the <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Church of Yorshka<\/a>, head towards the graveyard and turn right before exiting the church. The roster can be found on a corpse next to the staircase.<\/p>","use":"<p>The Roster of Knights allows the player to check the <a data-e=\"blade-of-the-darkmoon\">Blade of the Darkmoon<\/a> leaderboard.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Roster_of_Knights"},{"id":"rotten-pine-resin","kind":"item","name":"Rotten Pine Resin","page":"Rotten Pine Resin (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Rotten_Pine_Resin__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Temporarily applies poison to right-hand weapon.","buy":500,"sell":100,"held":5,"desc":"Pine resin that has rotted and turned poisonous. Likely rotten from the start.\nTemporarily applies poison to right-hand weapon.\nFarron Keep was swallowed by the rotted wood, where the blunt-horned Ghrus concoct this resin.","avail":"<ul><li>Dropped by Ghrus in <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a>.<\/li><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 500 souls once she is given the <a data-e=\"dreamchasers-ashes\">Dreamchaser's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Adds 45 Poison build-up to right-hand weapon. Buff lasts for 60 seconds.<\/p><p>The build-up increase scales with the Luck of the wielder, up to 59 build-up at 50 Luck.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Rotten_Pine_Resin_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"rubbish","kind":"item","name":"Rubbish","page":"Rubbish (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Rubbish__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Item with absolutely no use at all.","buy":200,"sell":1,"held":99,"desc":"Rubbish with no value.\nWho in their right mind would bother carrying this around? Perhaps you need help.","avail":"<p><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><\/p><ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 200 souls each.<\/li><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"unbreakable-patches\">Unbreakable Patches<\/a> for 200 souls each.<\/li><\/ul><p><a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a><\/p><ul><li>Dropped by Peasant Hollows.<\/li><li>Dropped by Hollow Manservants.<\/li><\/ul><p><a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Road of Sacrifices<\/a><\/p><ul><li>Dropped by Hollow Manservants.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Rubbish_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"rusted-coin","kind":"item","name":"Rusted Coin","page":"Rusted Coin (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Rusted_Coin__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Increases item discovery by 50 units for 60 seconds.","buy":200,"sell":50,"held":10,"desc":"An old rusted copper coin.\nCrushing the coin boosts item discovery.\nThose who have lost their fortunes rely upon this superstitious practice, hoping to retrieve what was once theirs and more.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a><ul><li>Two can be found by jumping from the roof of a house near the second Evangelist to a wooden balcony located above a Crystal Lizard, near the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Dilapidated Bridge<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><ul><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"unbreakable-patches\">Unbreakable Patches<\/a> for 200 souls each. If Patches dies, give his <a data-e=\"patches-ashes\">ashes<\/a> to the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> to increase her stock, allowing her to sell them at the same price.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li>Dropped by Jailer Handmaids.<\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-dreg-heap\">The Dreg Heap<\/a> <i>(<a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a>)<\/i><ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"stone-humped-hag\">Stone-humped Hag<\/a> for 200 souls each. If she dies, give her <a data-e=\"old-womans-ashes\">ashes<\/a> to the Shrine Handmaid to increase her stock, allowing her to sell them at the same price.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Increases Item Discovery by 50 units for 60 seconds.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Rusted_Coin_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"rusted-gold-coin","kind":"item","name":"Rusted Gold Coin","page":"Rusted Gold Coin","img":"assets/img/Rusted_Gold_Coin.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Boosts item discovery by 100 units for 60 seconds.","buy":null,"sell":150,"held":99,"desc":"A rusty old gold coin that surely has no currency.\nCrushing the coin gives a large, if temporary, boost to item discovery.\nA rich man lost his fortune, but it returned to him twinfold. He was swift to squander his retrieved fortune., smugly confident that it was bound to double once again.","avail":"<ul><li>A set of 7 coins can be chosen as a burial gift at the beginning of the game.<\/li><li><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><ul><li>Gifted by <a data-e=\"unbreakable-patches\">Unbreakable Patches<\/a> if the player does not forgive him for trapping them in the tower containing the <a data-e=\"fire-keeper-soul\">Fire Keeper Soul<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a><ul><li>One is found on a corpse near the extinguishable flame nearest where Yellowfinger Heysel invades the player, hidden behind the wall to the right of the flame.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a><ul><li>One is found at a dead end alley after the <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Church of Yorshka<\/a>, on a corpse being devoured by two Irithyllian Beast-Hounds.<\/li><li>One is found on a corpse at the Distant Manor, off the ledge at the bottom of the curved staircase.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a><ul><li>One is found on a corpse shortly after the Irithyll Dungeon bonfire, in the last cell on the right before the first Jailer. The cell is locked and requires the <a data-e=\"jailers-key-ring\">Jailer's Key Ring<\/a> to open.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"profaned-capital\">Profaned Capital<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Jailer Handmaids throughout the level.<\/li><li>Two are dropped by a Mimic in the treasury hall to the right of <a data-e=\"yhorm-the-giant\">Yhorm<\/a>'s boss arena.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a><ul><li>Three are found on a separated rooftop within the Corvian Settlement, which requires climbing to the crosswalks to the cliff above the settlement and then dropping down to reach.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-dreg-heap\">The Dreg Heap<\/a><ul><li>Three are sold by the <a data-e=\"stone-humped-hag\">Stone-humped Hag<\/a> directly in front of the Dreg Heap bonfire for 1800 souls each.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Increases Item Discovery by 100 points for 60 seconds.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Rusted_Gold_Coin"},{"id":"sages-coal","kind":"item","name":"Sage's Coal","page":"Sage's Coal","img":"assets/img/Sage_s_Coal.webp","sub":"Coal","usage":"Give to Andre to infuse weapons with crystal, blessed, or deep.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Coal used for weapon infusion\nThe white magic flame produced by this coal was given to the Undead Legion long ago by one of the Crystal Sage twins.\nGive to the blacksmith in the shrine to allow the use of gems for crystal, blessed, and dark infusion.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a>. From the <a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Farron Keep<\/a> bonfire, proceed through the area along the left-hand side until reaching a small, circular structure guarded by a Darkwraith. The coal lies within.<\/p>","use":"<p>Give the coal to <a data-e=\"blacksmith-andre\">Blacksmith Andre<\/a> in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> to allow usage of the following gems for infusions:<\/p><ul><li><a data-e=\"crystal-gem\">Crystal Gem<\/a><\/li><li><a data-e=\"blessed-gem\">Blessed Gem<\/a><\/li><li><a data-e=\"deep-gem\">Deep Gem<\/a><\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Sage's_Coal"},{"id":"sages-scroll","kind":"item","name":"Sage's Scroll","page":"Sage's Scroll","img":"assets/img/Sage_s_Scroll.webp","sub":"Spell book","usage":"Give to Orbeck of Vinheim to learn the sorceries of the Crystal Sages.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Scroll containing sorceries of the Crystal Sages.\nGive to a sorcerer to learn sorceries of the Sages.\nAs any sorcerer knows, sorcery is a talent, and these sorceries were refined to nurture a very special talent.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a>. From the <a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Keep Ruins<\/a> bonfire, head down the path, turn left and look for a family of dead Mushroom people and several Ghrus scattered around. The scroll will be nearby.<\/p>","use":"<p>Give to <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a> in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> to upgrade his stock of Sorceries:<\/p><table><tr><th>Quantity<\/th><th>Item<\/th><th>Cost<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"great-farron-dart\">Great Farron Dart<\/a><\/td><td>2,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"farron-hail\">Farron Hail<\/a><\/td><td>5,000<\/td><\/tr><\/table>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Sage's_Scroll"},{"id":"seed-of-a-giant-tree","kind":"item","name":"Seed of a Giant Tree","page":"Seed of a Giant Tree","img":"assets/img/Seed_of_a_Giant_Tree.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"World enemies react to invaders.","buy":null,"sell":100,"held":3,"desc":"Makes enemies react to invaders.\nThe giant trees were also known as watcher trees, and their seed unmask invaders.\nWhen used effectively, these seeds will help counter dark spirits.","avail":"<p>Obtained from the giant tree located just outside of the upper exit in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a>.<\/p><p>Every time a player is invaded, whether by an NPC or by another player, there is a chance that they will be able to pick a Seed from the tree. If a Seed is not available following an invasion, the probability increases incrementally until a Seed spawns, after which the chance resets.<\/p>","use":"<p>Upon use, enemies in the player's world will react to red and purple spirits, whether they are invaders or if they are summoned via a <a data-e=\"red-sign-soapstone\">Red Sign Soapstone<\/a>. The effect lasts for 45 seconds.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Seed_of_a_Giant_Tree"},{"id":"sharp-gem","kind":"item","name":"Sharp Gem","page":"Sharp Gem","img":"assets/img/Sharp_Gem.webp","sub":"Upgrade material","usage":"Used in infusion to create Sharp weapons.","buy":null,"sell":300,"held":99,"desc":"A gem of infused titanite. Forged the unique curved swords of Carthus.\nUsed in infusion to create sharp weapons.\nA swordsman can appreciate a sharp weapon, for they scale effectively with dexterity.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a><ul><li>Guaranteed drop from the Crystal Lizard found on the ledge above the Dilapidated Bridge bonfire.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"catacombs-of-carthus\">Catacombs of Carthus<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Skeleton Swordsmen.<\/li><li>Found on a corpse in the lower level of the multi-layered area immediately past the first bridge, in the room with a Skeleton Swordsman wielding a shotel. The corpse can be found on a ledge of an opening that overlooks the bottomless pit below the bridge.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a><ul><li>Guaranteed drop from a Crystal Lizard found on the rooftops. It is found after passing the first spear-wielding Gargoyle and is next to another Crystal Lizard. The left lizard is the one which drops the Sharp Gem.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Corvian Knights.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Infusing a weapon with the Sharp property will increase the Dexterity scaling on that weapon, and as such, is an excellent choice for players who invested heavily into dexterity. As a result of the infusion, however, the Strength scaling will be lowered, or entirely removed on some weapons, and the weapon's base damage will be slightly reduced.<\/p><p>Weapons that scale well with dexterity from their base level will benefit greatly from sharp infusions.<\/p><p>As of the 1.32 Regulations patch, Sharp-infused weapons will gain increased scaling at very high levels of Dexterity. Between 40 and 60 Dexterity, scaling is poor, however beyond 60 Dexterity it will greatly increase until it gradually begins to fall off at roughly 80 Dexterity.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Sharp_Gem"},{"id":"shriving-stone","kind":"item","name":"Shriving Stone","page":"Shriving Stone","img":"assets/img/Shriving_Stone.webp","sub":"Upgrade material","usage":"Removes weapon infusions.","buy":null,"sell":100,"held":99,"desc":"A gem of infused titanite.\nAlso known as stark stone.\nReverses weapon infusion.\nHas the benefit of undoing the effects of infusion without reducing the reinforcement level.","avail":"<ul><li>Dropped by Corvians.<\/li><li><a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Road of Sacrifices<\/a><ul><li>Below the first ledge, near the second Corvian encountered.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a><ul><li>Behind the main gate, once opened.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a><ul><li>On the third floor of the library, on a corpse lying at the end of the left corridor from the wooden bridge.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Used to remove any type of infusion from a weapon, returning it to its original state.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Shriving_Stone"},{"id":"siegbr-u","kind":"item","name":"Siegbräu","page":"Siegbräu","img":"assets/img/Siegbräu.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Restores HP equal to 20% of your maximum HP + 100 and boosts frost resistance for 60 seconds.","buy":null,"sell":1000,"held":10,"desc":"Special brew of Siegward of Catarina.\nPerfect for travel in its jolly barrel mug.\nRestores HP and temporarily boosts frost resistance.\nLeave it to Siegward to discover a drink that even an Undead can enjoy. Perhaps his long years spent Undead have left him wanting to drain a cup or two and revel as if he were still among the living.","avail":"<p>Up to three Siegbräus can be collected in a single playthrough in the base game, all of them presented by <a data-e=\"siegward-of-catarina\">Siegward of Catarina<\/a> during various stages throughout his questline:<\/p><ul><li><a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a>: Given by Siegward after defeating the Demon.<\/li><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a>: Given after meeting Siegward sleeping in the kitchen near the Distant Manor bonfire.<\/li><li><a data-e=\"profaned-capital\">Profaned Capital<\/a>: Given at the aftermath of <a data-e=\"yhorm-the-giant\">Yhorm the Giant<\/a>'s boss battle if Siegward assisted and survived.<\/li><\/ul><p>Two more per playthrough can be obtained in <i>Dark Souls III: The Ringed City<\/i>:<\/p><ul><li>If the player obtains the <a data-e=\"titanite-slab\">Titanite Slab<\/a> in the <a data-e=\"the-dreg-heap\">Earthen Peak Ruins<\/a> swamp without <a data-e=\"amnesiac-lapp\">Amnesiac Lapp<\/a>'s assistance, he will toast the player and give them a Siegbräu. Otherwise, once he has moved on to the Ringed Inner Wall, a Siegbräu will be left at his location near this bonfire.<\/li><li>Once the player meets Lapp within the Ringed Inner Wall, he will toast them and give them a Siegbräu.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Siegbräu"},{"id":"simple-gem","kind":"item","name":"Simple Gem","page":"Simple Gem","img":"assets/img/Simple_Gem.webp","sub":"Upgrade material","usage":"Used in infusion to create Simple weapons.","buy":null,"sell":500,"held":99,"desc":"A gem of infused titanite, said to be an object of infatuation for victims of stunted development.\nUsed in infusion to create simple weapons.\nSimple weapons inflict magic damage and restore FP very gradually, to help even a simpleton muster some mettle.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by a Crystal Lizard found above the <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Pontiff Sulyvahn<\/a> bonfire, across the lift.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Jailers.<\/li><li>One can be found in a side room near the stairway guarded by three Jailers, protected by a Wretch.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a><ul><li>In the riverbed in the Corvian Settlement. After entering the settlement proper and taking the left-side path after the bridge, drop down into the riverbed behind the gate, where a Sewer Centipede guards it.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a><ul><li>Found on a corpse in the <a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">Shared Grave<\/a> area, in the area under the Crystal Lizard trap.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Infuses weapons with Magic damage, granting Intelligence scaling but reducing Strength and Dexterity scaling, as well as reducing base damage. Compared to the <a data-e=\"crystal-gem\">Crystal<\/a> infusion, the scaling is higher in all areas, but the base damage of the weapon is lower, meaning that the weapon will do less damage overall.<\/p><p>The benefit of the Simple infusion is that when wielded, the weapon slowly regenerates FP at a rate of about 1 FP per 5 seconds, or 0.2 FP per second. Reinforcing it will reduce the tick interval by roughly 0.217 seconds per upgrade level. At +10 reinforcement, a Simple weapon will replenish 1 FP per 2.85 seconds, or roughly 0.35 FP per second.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Simple_Gem"},{"id":"small-doll","kind":"item","name":"Small Doll","page":"Small Doll","img":"assets/img/Small_Doll.webp","sub":"Key item","usage":"Grants access to Irithyll of the Boreal Valley.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Small silverwork doll depicting a young squire.\nIn the legendary old city of Irithyll situated in the Boreal Valley, the Pontiff Sulyvahn gave this doll to valued subjects, so that they might use it to cross the barrier when they return home.\nListen carefully, and you can hear it say, \"Wherever you go, the moon still sets in Irithyll. Wherever you may be, Irithyll is your home.\"","avail":"<p>Obtained after defeating the <a data-e=\"deacons-of-the-deep\">Deacons of the Deep<\/a> in the <a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Breaks the seal on the bridge that grants access to <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Central Irithyll<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Small_Doll"},{"id":"small-lothric-banner","kind":"item","name":"Small Lothric Banner","page":"Small Lothric Banner","img":"assets/img/Small_Lothric_Banner.webp","sub":"Key item","usage":"Used to gain access to the Undead Settlement.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":99,"desc":"Small banner held by Lothric messengers.\nHold up outside the main castle gate to be greeted by an escort.\nWhen the High Wall appeared, the path to the Undead Settlement was blocked, and messengers came bearing this banner. They were sent out with a duty, but had no way of returning.","avail":"<ul><li>Given to the player by <a data-e=\"emma-high-priestess-of-lothric-castle\">Emma, High Priestess of Lothric Castle<\/a> in the <a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">High Wall of Lothric<\/a>'s cathedral.<\/li><li>Dropped by Emma if she is killed by the player.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Allows the player to be carried to the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a> after defeating <a data-e=\"vordt-of-the-boreal-valley\">Vordt of the Boreal Valley<\/a> thanks to an escort of Batwing Demons.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Small_Lothric_Banner"},{"id":"sniper-bolt","kind":"item","name":"Sniper Bolt","page":"Sniper Bolt (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Sniper_Bolt__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Ammunition","usage":"Deal 53 physical damage to target.","buy":150,"sell":3,"held":99,"desc":"Red feathered bolts used by snipers of Carim. Their long range makes them ideal for distant targets.\nThough typically used with Sniper Crossbows in Carim, these bolts can still be used with any kind of crossbow.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"greirat-of-the-undead-settlement\">Greirat of the Undead Settlement<\/a> for 150 souls once he returns from his first pillaging journey.<\/li><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> once she has been given <a data-e=\"greirats-ashes\">Greirat's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Sniper_Bolt_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"soul-of-aldrich","kind":"item","name":"Soul of Aldrich","page":"Soul of Aldrich","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_Aldrich.webp","sub":"Boss soul","usage":"• Consume for 15,000 souls. • Transpose for Lifehunt Scythe. • Transpose for Darkmoon Longbow.","buy":null,"sell":15000,"held":99,"desc":"Soul of Aldrich.\nOne of the twisted souls, steeped in strength.\nUse to acquire many souls, or transpose to extract its true strength.\nWhen Aldrich ruminated on the fading of the fire, it inspired visions of a coming age of the deep sea.\nHe knew the path would be arduous, but he had no fear. He would devour the gods himself.","avail":"<p>Obtained after defeating <a data-e=\"aldrich-devourer-of-gods\">Aldrich, Devourer of Gods<\/a> in <a data-e=\"anor-londo\">Anor Londo<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 15,000 souls or transpose with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth<\/a> to create either the <a data-e=\"lifehunt-scythe\">Lifehunt Scythe<\/a> or the <a data-e=\"darkmoon-longbow\">Darkmoon Longbow<\/a>.<\/p>","transposes":[{"item":"lifehunt-scythe","cost":null},{"item":"darkmoon-longbow","cost":"5,000 souls"}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_Aldrich"},{"id":"soul-of-boreal-valley-vordt","kind":"item","name":"Soul of Boreal Valley Vordt","page":"Soul of Boreal Valley Vordt","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_Boreal_Valley_Vordt.webp","sub":"Boss soul","usage":"• Consume for 2,000 souls. • Transpose for Vordt's Great Hammer. • Transpose for Pontiff's Left Eye.","buy":null,"sell":2000,"held":99,"desc":"Soul of Vordt of the Boreal Valley. One of the twisted souls, steeped in strength.\nUse to acquire many souls, or transpose to extract its true strength.\nVordt served as an outrider knight, never far from the fleeting dancer.","avail":"<p>Obtained after defeating <a data-e=\"vordt-of-the-boreal-valley\">Vordt of the Boreal Valley<\/a> at the bottom of the <a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">High Wall of Lothric<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 2,000 souls or transpose with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth<\/a> to create either the <a data-e=\"vordts-great-hammer\">Vordt's Great Hammer<\/a> or the <a data-e=\"pontiffs-left-eye\">Pontiff's Left Eye<\/a>.<\/p>","transposes":[{"item":"vordts-great-hammer","cost":null},{"item":"pontiffs-left-eye","cost":null}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_Boreal_Valley_Vordt"},{"id":"soul-of-champion-gundyr","kind":"item","name":"Soul of Champion Gundyr","page":"Soul of Champion Gundyr","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_Champion_Gundyr.webp","sub":"Boss soul","usage":"• Consume for 20,000 souls. • Transpose for Gundyr's Halberd. • Transpose for Prisoner's Chain.","buy":null,"sell":20000,"held":99,"desc":"Soul of Champion Gundyr.\nOne of the twisted souls, steeped in strength.\nUse to acquire numerous souls, or transpose to extract its true strength.\nOnce, a champion came late to the festivities, and was greeted by a shrine without fire, and a bell that would not toll.","avail":"<p>Obtained after defeating <a data-e=\"champion-gundyr\">Champion Gundyr<\/a> in the <a data-e=\"untended-graves\">Untended Graves<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 20,000 souls or transpose with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth<\/a> to create either the <a data-e=\"gundyrs-halberd\">Gundyr's Halberd<\/a> or the <a data-e=\"prisoners-chain\">Prisoner's Chain<\/a>.<\/p>","transposes":[{"item":"gundyrs-halberd","cost":null},{"item":"prisoners-chain","cost":null}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_Champion_Gundyr"},{"id":"soul-of-consumed-oceiros","kind":"item","name":"Soul of Consumed Oceiros","page":"Soul of Consumed Oceiros","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_Consumed_Oceiros.webp","sub":"Boss soul","usage":"• Consume for 12,000 souls. • Transpose for Moonlight Greatsword. • Transpose for White Dragon Breath.","buy":null,"sell":12000,"held":99,"desc":"Soul of Oceiros, the Consumed King.\nOne of the twisted souls, steeped in strength.\nUse to acquire numerous souls, or transpose to extract its true strength.\nOceiros went mad trying to harness his royal blood for a greater purpose, leading him to the heretics of the Grand Archives, where he discovered the twisted worship of Seath the paledrake.","avail":"<p>Obtained upon defeating <a data-e=\"oceiros-the-consumed-king\">Oceiros, the Consumed King<\/a> in the <a data-e=\"consumed-kings-garden\">Consumed King's Garden<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 12,000 souls or transpose with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth<\/a> to create either the <a data-e=\"moonlight-greatsword\">Moonlight Greatsword<\/a> or the <a data-e=\"white-dragon-breath\">White Dragon Breath<\/a> sorcery.<\/p>","transposes":[{"item":"white-dragon-breath","cost":"10,000 souls"},{"item":"moonlight-greatsword","cost":"10,000 souls"}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_Consumed_Oceiros"},{"id":"soul-of-darkeater-midir","kind":"item","name":"Soul of Darkeater Midir","page":"Soul of Darkeater Midir","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_Darkeater_Midir.webp","sub":"Boss soul","usage":"• Consume for 20,000 souls. • Transpose for Frayed Blade. • Transpose for Old Moonlight.","buy":null,"sell":20000,"held":99,"desc":"Soul of Darkeater Midir.\nOne of the twisted souls, steeped in strength.\nUse to acquire many souls, or transpose to extract its true strength.\nMidir, descendant of Archdragons, was raised by the gods, and owing to his immortality was given a duty to eternally battle the dark, a duty that he would never forget, even after the gods perished.","avail":"<p>Obtained upon defeating <a data-e=\"darkeater-midir\">Darkeater Midir<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 20,000 souls or transpose with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth<\/a> to create either the <a data-e=\"frayed-blade\">Frayed Blade<\/a> or the <a data-e=\"old-moonlight\">Old Moonlight<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_Darkeater_Midir"},{"id":"soul-of-dragonslayer-armour","kind":"item","name":"Soul of Dragonslayer Armour","page":"Soul of Dragonslayer Armour","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_Dragonslayer_Armour.webp","sub":"Boss soul","usage":"• Consume for 15,000 souls. • Transpose for Dragonslayer Greataxe. • Transpose for Dragonslayer Greatshield.","buy":null,"sell":15000,"held":99,"desc":"Soul of the Dragonslayer Armour.\nOne of the twisted souls, steeped in strength.\nUse to acquire many souls, or transpose to extract its true strength.\nThe Dragonslayer Armour, controlled by the Pilgrim Butterfly, lost its master long ago, but still remembers their sporting hunts.","avail":"<p>Obtained after defeating the <a data-e=\"dragonslayer-armour\">Dragonslayer Armour<\/a> in <a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 15,000 souls or transpose with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth<\/a> to create either the <a data-e=\"dragonslayer-greataxe\">Dragonslayer Greataxe<\/a> or <a data-e=\"dragonslayer-greatshield\">Dragonslayer Greatshield<\/a>.<\/p>","transposes":[{"item":"dragonslayer-greataxe","cost":null},{"item":"dragonslayer-greatshield","cost":null}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_Dragonslayer_Armour"},{"id":"soul-of-high-lord-wolnir","kind":"item","name":"Soul of High Lord Wolnir","page":"Soul of High Lord Wolnir","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_High_Lord_Wolnir.webp","sub":"Boss soul","usage":"• Consume for 10,000 souls. • Transpose for Wolnir's Holy Sword. • Transpose for Black Serpent.","buy":null,"sell":10000,"held":99,"desc":"Soul of the High Lord Wolnir.\nOne of the twisted souls, steeped in strength.\nUse to acquire many souls, or transpose to extract its true strength.\nLord Wolnir of Carthus sentenced countless souls to gruesome deaths, keen to outlive them all.","avail":"<p>Obtained after defeating <a data-e=\"high-lord-wolnir\">High Lord Wolnir<\/a> in the <a data-e=\"catacombs-of-carthus\">Catacombs of Carthus<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 10,000 souls or transpose with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth<\/a> to create either <a data-e=\"wolnirs-holy-sword\">Wolnir's Holy Sword<\/a> or the <a data-e=\"black-serpent\">Black Serpent<\/a> pyromancy.<\/p>","transposes":[{"item":"black-serpent","cost":null},{"item":"wolnirs-holy-sword","cost":null}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_High_Lord_Wolnir"},{"id":"soul-of-pontiff-sulyvahn","kind":"item","name":"Soul of Pontiff Sulyvahn","page":"Soul of Pontiff Sulyvahn","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_Pontiff_Sulyvahn.webp","sub":"Boss soul","usage":"• Consume for 12,000 souls. • Transpose for Greatsword of Judgment. • Transpose for Profaned Greatsword.","buy":null,"sell":12000,"held":99,"desc":"Soul of Pontiff Sulyvahn.\nOne of the twisted souls, steeped in strength.\nUse to acquire many souls, or transpose to extract its true strength.\nPontiff Sulyvahn of Irithyll imprisoned a god of the old royalty in the abandoned cathedral, to be fed to the devourer.","avail":"<p>Obtained after defeating <a data-e=\"pontiff-sulyvahn\">Pontiff Sulyvahn<\/a> in <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 12,000 souls or transpose with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth<\/a> to create either the <a data-e=\"greatsword-of-judgment\">Greatsword of Judgment<\/a> or the <a data-e=\"profaned-greatsword\">Profaned Greatsword<\/a>.<\/p>","transposes":[{"item":"greatsword-of-judgment","cost":"3,000 souls"},{"item":"profaned-greatsword","cost":"3,000 souls"}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_Pontiff_Sulyvahn"},{"id":"soul-of-rosaria","kind":"item","name":"Soul of Rosaria","page":"Soul of Rosaria","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_Rosaria.webp","sub":"Boss soul","usage":"• Use to resurrect Rosaria. • Consume for 5,000 souls. • Transpose for Bountiful Sunlight.","buy":null,"sell":5000,"held":99,"desc":"The soul of Rosaria, Mother of Rebirth, stolen by Ringfinger Leonhard.\nReturn this to her extant corpse, and mother Rosaria will spring back to life.\nAs if nothing had ever happened.","avail":"<p>Obtained by using the <a data-e=\"black-eye-orb\">Black Eye Orb<\/a> in Gwynevere's empty chamber in <a data-e=\"anor-londo\">Anor Londo<\/a>, located above the <a data-e=\"anor-londo\">Aldrich, Devourer of Gods<\/a> bonfire. The player will invade the world of <a data-e=\"rosaria-mother-of-rebirth\">Rosaria<\/a>'s murderer, <a data-e=\"ringfinger-leonhard\">Leonhard<\/a>, and receive the soul upon exacting revenge against him.<\/p>","use":"<ul><li>Use on <a data-e=\"rosaria-mother-of-rebirth\">Rosaria<\/a>'s corpse to resurrect her after she has been slain by <a data-e=\"ringfinger-leonhard\">Leonhard<\/a>.<\/li><li>Consume for 5,000 souls.<\/li><li>Transpose with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth<\/a> to create the <a data-e=\"bountiful-sunlight\">Bountiful Sunlight<\/a> miracle.<\/li><\/ul>","transposes":[{"item":"bountiful-sunlight","cost":null}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_Rosaria"},{"id":"soul-of-sister-friede","kind":"item","name":"Soul of Sister Friede","page":"Soul of Sister Friede","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_Sister_Friede.webp","sub":"Boss soul","usage":"• Consume for 20,000 souls. • Transpose for Friede's Great Scythe. • Transpose for Rose of Ariandel.","buy":null,"sell":20000,"held":99,"desc":"Soul of Sister Friede. One of the twisted souls, steeped in strength.\nUse to acquire numerous souls, or transpose to extract its true strength.\nFriede was the first Ash to enter the painting, but together with the good Father, they chose rot over fire.","avail":"<p>Obtained after defeating <a data-e=\"sister-friede\">Sister Friede<\/a> in the <a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 20,000 souls or transpose with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth<\/a> to create either <a data-e=\"friedes-great-scythe\">Friede's Great Scythe<\/a> or the <a data-e=\"rose-of-ariandel\">Rose of Ariandel<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_Sister_Friede"},{"id":"soul-of-slave-knight-gael","kind":"item","name":"Soul of Slave Knight Gael","page":"Soul of Slave Knight Gael","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_Slave_Knight_Gael.webp","sub":"Boss soul","usage":"• Consume for 20,000 souls. • Transpose for Gael's Greatsword. • Transpose for Repeating Crossbow.","buy":null,"sell":20000,"held":99,"desc":"Soul of Slave Knight Gael.\nOne of the twisted souls, steeped in strength.\nUse to acquire many souls, or transpose to extract its true strength.\nThe red-hooded, wandering slave knight Gael sought the blood of the dark soul as pigment for the Painted World. But Gael knew he was no Champion, that the dark soul would likely ruin him and that he had little hope of a safe return.","avail":"<p>Obtained upon defeating <a data-e=\"slave-knight-gael\">Slave Knight Gael<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 20,000 souls or transpose with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth<\/a> to create either <a data-e=\"gaels-greatsword\">Gael's Greatsword<\/a> or <a data-e=\"repeating-crossbow\">Repeating Crossbow<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_Slave_Knight_Gael"},{"id":"soul-of-yhorm-the-giant","kind":"item","name":"Soul of Yhorm the Giant","page":"Soul of Yhorm the Giant","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_Yhorm_the_Giant.webp","sub":"Boss soul","usage":"• Consume for 20,000 souls. • Transpose for Yhorm's Great Machete. • Transpose for Yhorm's Greatshield.","buy":null,"sell":20000,"held":99,"desc":"Soul of Yhorm the Giant.\nOne of the twisted souls, steeped in strength.\nUse to acquire numerous souls, or transpose to extract its true strength.\nYhorm is the descendant of an ancient conqueror, but was asked by the very people once subjugated to lead them, serving as both a weighty blade and a stone-hard shield.","avail":"<p>Obtained upon defeating <a data-e=\"yhorm-the-giant\">Yhorm the Giant<\/a> in the <a data-e=\"profaned-capital\">Profaned Capital<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 20,000 souls or transpose with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth<\/a> to create either <a data-e=\"yhorms-great-machete\">Yhorm's Great Machete<\/a> or <a data-e=\"yhorms-greatshield\">Yhorm's Greatshield<\/a>.<\/p>","transposes":[{"item":"yhorms-great-machete","cost":null},{"item":"yhorms-greatshield","cost":null}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_Yhorm_the_Giant"},{"id":"soul-of-a-champion","kind":"item","name":"Soul of a Champion","page":"Soul of a Champion","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_a_Champion.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Consume to acquire 25,000 souls.","buy":null,"sell":25000,"held":99,"desc":"Soul found in the corpse of a champion of legend.\nUse to acquire enough souls to sate a lord.\nLet the Fire Keeper transform this sovereignless soul into a source of strength, for to be Unkindled is to be a vessel for souls.","avail":"<p>Can only be obtained in NG+ onward, where it replaces the <a data-e=\"soul-of-a-crestfallen-knight\">Soul of a Crestfallen Knight<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 25,000 souls.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_a_Champion"},{"id":"soul-of-a-crestfallen-knight","kind":"item","name":"Soul of a Crestfallen Knight","page":"Soul of a Crestfallen Knight","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_a_Crestfallen_Knight.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Consume to acquire 10,000 souls.","buy":null,"sell":10000,"held":99,"desc":"Soul found in the corpse of a crestfallen knight.\nUse to acquire a large amount of souls.\nLet the Fire Keeper transform this sovereignless soul into a source of strength, for to be Unkindled is to be a vessel for souls.","avail":"<p>A total of seventeen can be found in each playthrough. Ten can be found in the base game, three can be found in <i>Ashes of Ariandel<\/i> and four can be found in <i><a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a><\/i>:<\/p><ul><li><a data-e=\"smouldering-lake\">Smouldering Lake<\/a><ul><li>Deep within the Demon Ruins, on the bridge above Knight Slayer Tsorig's lava pit, there is an <a data-e=\"black-knight-greatsword\">ultra greatsword<\/a> wielding Black Knight that guards the ladder to the ballista. Next to this Black Knight is a corpse holding the item.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a><ul><li>The Giant Slave sleeping past the initial wing of cell blocks is guarding a Crystal Lizard as well as a corpse holding the soul.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"anor-londo\">Anor Londo<\/a><ul><li>Turning right before the cathedral doors (the path that normally leads to the Batwing Demons and the flying buttress guarded by two <a data-e=\"dragonslayer-greatbow\">Dragonslayer Greatbow<\/a>-wielding Silver Knights), there is a single red-eyed Silver Knight. A nearby corpse holds the item.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"untended-graves\">Untended Graves<\/a><ul><li>Near the broken Lordvessel where the <a data-e=\"ashen-estus-flask\">Ashen Estus Flask<\/a> is looted in the <a data-e=\"cemetery-of-ash\">Cemetery of Ash<\/a>, there is instead a corpse that holds the soul.<\/li><li>At Dark Firelink Shrine, there is a set of stairs in the direction of the <a data-e=\"chaos-blade\">Chaos Blade<\/a> that is guarded by an ultra greatsword wielding Black Knight. Past it, on the level above the shrine entrance, is a corpse holding the item.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a><ul><li>In the first room past the <a data-e=\"dancer-of-the-boreal-valley\">Dancer of the Boreal Valley<\/a>, there is a red-eyed Lothric Knight kneeling before an altar and a Lothric Priest in attendance. Before the altar is a corpse holding the soul.<\/li><li>To the left before the <a data-e=\"dragonslayer-armour\">Dragonslayer Armour<\/a>'s boss fog, there is a broken railing that can be dropped down. This leads to the Pus of Man infecting the white Lothric Wyvern's leg. Perched on another broken railing under the wyvern itself is a corpse holding the item.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a><ul><li>Past the first Crystal Lizard and down the drop-down, a corpse can be seen holding an item. Turning left at the first opportunity down the narrow pathway will lead to an encounter with a Thrall, past which is the corpse holding the soul.<\/li><li>After exiting the domed building that holds the shortcut back to the ground floor of the Archives, turning left will allow the player to climb to the top of the building. On the other side of the dome after the stairs is a corpse holding the item.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"archdragon-peak\">Archdragon Peak<\/a><ul><li>In the Dragon-Kin Mausoleum, go up the stairs and turn towards the left corner at the top. A corpse holds the soul, opposite the path leading to the Man Serpent Summoner.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a><ul><li>At the end of the Corvian Settlement, there is an enclosed chapel with two Corvian Knights guarding <a data-e=\"way-of-white-corona\">Way of White Corona<\/a>. The soul item can be found on a corpse on the rafters above, which can be reached by dropping in from the windows on the roof.<\/li><li>In the second part of the Snowy Mountain Pass, there is a valley patrolled by three Millwood Knights; one wielding the <a data-e=\"millwood-battle-axe\">axe<\/a>, one with a <a data-e=\"quakestone-hammer\">great hammer<\/a> and one carrying a <a data-e=\"earth-seeker\">greataxe<\/a>. A corpse within the valley holds the soul.<\/li><li>Within the same valley, there is a second corpse opposite it that holds another soul.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-dreg-heap\">The Dreg Heap<\/a><ul><li>After the first two dropdowns, two root-infested Lothric Knights, one wielding a <a data-e=\"lothric-war-banner\">banner<\/a>, can be seen praying at an altar. Lying on the altar is a corpse holding the item.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a><ul><li>In the midst of engaging the Judicator Giant at the Mausoleum Outlook, a gazebo outcropping to the right of the graveyard allows the player to temporarily drop down out of the giant's line of sight. Dropping down from the roof and walking back under it, there is a corpse holding the soul.<\/li><li>At the bottom of the great stairway that leads into the Ringed City Streets, turning left will lead into a small alleyway with a ladder and three Hobbled Clerics. Two of the clerics at the far back are guarding a corpse that holds the item.<\/li><li>In the midst of the Ringed City Streets, there is a large abyss crystal near the sunken chapel that holds the <a data-e=\"church-guardian-shiv\">Church Guardian Shiv<\/a>. A corpse lying against the crystal holds the item.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 10,000 souls.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_a_Crestfallen_Knight"},{"id":"soul-of-a-crystal-sage","kind":"item","name":"Soul of a Crystal Sage","page":"Soul of a Crystal Sage","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_a_Crystal_Sage.webp","sub":"Boss soul","usage":"• Consume for 3,000 souls. • Transpose for Crystal Sage's Rapier. • Transpose for Crystal Hail.","buy":null,"sell":3000,"held":99,"desc":"Soul of a Crystal Sage. One of the twisted souls, steeped in strength.\nUse to acquire numerous souls, or transpose to extract its true strength.\nThe twin Crystal Sages once served as spiritual guides to the scholars of the Grand Archives, and one went on to ally with the Undead Legion.","avail":"<p>Obtained after defeating the <a data-e=\"crystal-sage\">Crystal Sage<\/a> in the <a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Road of Sacrifices<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 3,000 souls or transpose with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth<\/a> to create either the <a data-e=\"crystal-sages-rapier\">Crystal Sage's Rapier<\/a> or the <a data-e=\"crystal-hail\">Crystal Hail<\/a> sorcery.<\/p>","transposes":[{"item":"crystal-hail","cost":"1,500 souls"},{"item":"crystal-sages-rapier","cost":null}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_a_Crystal_Sage"},{"id":"soul-of-a-demon","kind":"item","name":"Soul of a Demon","page":"Soul of a Demon","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_a_Demon.webp","sub":"Boss soul","usage":"• Consume for 20,000 souls. • Transpose for Demon's Greataxe. • Transpose for Demon's Fist.","buy":null,"sell":20000,"held":99,"desc":"Soul of a demon.\nOne of the twisted souls, steeped in strength.\nUse to acquire numerous souls, or transpose to extract its true strength.\nDemons were born of the Chaos Flame, but the flame has not survived, and the demons are a dying race.","avail":"<p>Obtained by defeating the Demon in the <a data-e=\"catacombs-of-carthus\">Catacombs of Carthus<\/a>, just before the <a data-e=\"catacombs-of-carthus\">Abandoned Tomb<\/a> bonfire.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 20,000 souls or transpose with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth<\/a> to create either the <a data-e=\"demons-greataxe\">Demon's Greataxe<\/a> or the <a data-e=\"demons-fist\">Demon's Fist<\/a>.<\/p>","transposes":[{"item":"demons-fist","cost":null},{"item":"demons-greataxe","cost":null}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_a_Demon"},{"id":"soul-of-a-deserted-corpse","kind":"item","name":"Soul of a Deserted Corpse","page":"Soul of a Deserted Corpse","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_a_Deserted_Corpse.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Consume to acquire 200 souls.","buy":null,"sell":200,"held":99,"desc":"Soul found in a deserted corpse.\nUse to acquire souls.\nLet the Fire Keeper transform this sovereignless soul into a source of strength, for to be Unkindled is to be a vessel for souls.","avail":"<p>A minimum of nine can be found per playthrough.<\/p><ul><li><a data-e=\"cemetery-of-ash\">Cemetery of Ash<\/a><ul><li>To the right of the <a data-e=\"ashen-estus-flask\">Ashen Estus Flask<\/a>.<\/li><li>On a corpse near the tower behind <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">High Wall of Lothric<\/a><ul><li>Left from first spawn on the bridge.<\/li><li>Dungeon under the Lothric Wyvern.<\/li><li>On a bridge just before the <a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">Tower on the Wall<\/a> bonfire.<\/li><li>After leaving the room under the <a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">Tower on the Wall<\/a> bonfire, take the right exit for the soul item.<\/li><li>In the room with the Lothric Knight after dropping from the rooftop with the Pus of Man and the Praying Hollow Soldiers.<\/li><li>Near the elevator shortcut leading to an area just before the first bonfire.<\/li><li>To the left upon exiting the small courtyard with the Winged Knight.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Hound Rats.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"catacombs-of-carthus\">Catacombs of Carthus<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Hound Rats.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"smouldering-lake\">Smouldering Lake<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Hound Rats.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Hound Rats.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 200 souls.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_a_Deserted_Corpse"},{"id":"soul-of-a-great-champion","kind":"item","name":"Soul of a Great Champion","page":"Soul of a Great Champion","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_a_Great_Champion.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Consume to acquire 50,000 souls.","buy":null,"sell":50000,"held":99,"desc":"Large soul found in the corpse of a champion of legend.\nUse to acquire enough souls to sate a lord.\nLet the Fire Keeper transform this sovereignless soul into a source of strength, for to be Unkindled is to be a vessel for souls.","avail":"<p>Can only be obtained in NG+ onward, where it replaces the <a data-e=\"large-soul-of-a-crestfallen-knight\">Large Soul of a Crestfallen Knight<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 50,000 souls.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_a_Great_Champion"},{"id":"soul-of-a-nameless-soldier","kind":"item","name":"Soul of a Nameless Soldier","page":"Soul of a Nameless Soldier (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_a_Nameless_Soldier__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Soul item","usage":"Consume to acquire 2,000 souls.","buy":null,"sell":2000,"held":99,"desc":"Soul found in the corpse of a nameless soldier.\nUse to acquire souls.\nLet the Fire Keeper transform this sovereignless soul into a source of strength, for to be Unkindled is to be a vessel for souls.","avail":"<p>A maximum of nine are guaranteed to be obtained by the player in each playthrough.<\/p><ul><li>One is granted to the player at the start of the game by choosing the &quot;Sovereignless Soul&quot; burial gift.<\/li><li><a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a><ul><li>At the top of the tower inhabited by the <a data-e=\"giant-archer-of-the-undead-settlement\">Giant Archer of the Undead Settlement<\/a>, there is a corpse holding the item in a small alcove opposite to the lever that controls the elevator.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a><ul><li>Near the white tree patrolled by a Great Crab and which is guarded by the <a data-e=\"giant-archer-of-the-undead-settlement\">Giant Archer of the Undead Settlement<\/a>, a drowned corpse can be looted for the item.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a><ul><li>On the rooftops portion of the exterior of the cathedral, there is a small side structure after navigating the flying buttresses that is patrolled by a large number of Thralls. Inside of the structure is a corpse holding the soul, though additional Thralls lie in ambush.<\/li><li>In the interior of the cathedral, there is a path after the first shortcut back to the Cleansing Chapel that is guarded by a large Giant Slave. One of the corpses along this route holds the item.<\/li><li>On the bottom floor of the cathedral interior, within the sludge at the feet of the first Giant Slave. A corpse beneath the Giant Slave and near to the large double doors holds the consumable.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"catacombs-of-carthus\">Catacombs of Carthus<\/a><ul><li>At the bottom of the ladder in the first section of the tomb, a corpse sitting against a wall holds the item.<\/li><li>A lone pathway to the right after some stairs past the initial bridge is guarded by two headless skeletons. Beyond these two skeletons is a corpse holding the soul consumable.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a><ul><li>Held by a corpse within the dark room after the first wax pool, against some bookshelves against the back wall and protected by Clawed Curses.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"archdragon-peak\">Archdragon Peak<\/a><ul><li>Past the initial gauntlet and ascending the stairs after the first bonfire, a corpse dangling off of a ledge to the right can be looted for the item.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by White-faced Locusts.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 2,000 souls.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_a_Nameless_Soldier_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"soul-of-a-proud-paladin","kind":"item","name":"Soul of a Proud Paladin","page":"Soul of a Proud Paladin","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_a_Proud_Paladin.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Consume to acquire 500 souls.","buy":null,"sell":500,"held":99,"desc":"Soul found in the corpse of a proud paladin.\nUse to acquire many souls.\nLet the Fire Keeper transform this sovereignless soul into a source of strength, for to be Unkindled is to be a vessel for souls.","avail":"<p>Can only be obtained in NG+ onward, where it replaces the <a data-e=\"soul-of-a-deserted-corpse\">Soul of a Deserted Corpse<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 500 souls.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_a_Proud_Paladin"},{"id":"soul-of-a-seasoned-warrior","kind":"item","name":"Soul of a Seasoned Warrior","page":"Soul of a Seasoned Warrior","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_a_Seasoned_Warrior.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Consume to acquire 5,000 souls.","buy":null,"sell":5000,"held":99,"desc":"Soul found in the corpse of a seasoned warrior.\nUse to acquire a great helping of souls.\nLet the Fire Keeper transform this sovereignless soul into a source of strength, for to be Unkindled is to be a vessel for souls.","avail":"<p>Can only be obtained in NG+ onward, where it replaces the <a data-e=\"soul-of-a-nameless-soldier\">Soul of a Nameless Soldier<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 5,000 souls.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_a_Seasoned_Warrior"},{"id":"soul-of-a-stray-demon","kind":"item","name":"Soul of a Stray Demon","page":"Soul of a Stray Demon","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_a_Stray_Demon.webp","sub":"Boss soul","usage":"• Consume for 20,000 souls. • Transpose for Boulder Heave. • Transpose for Havel's Ring.","buy":null,"sell":20000,"held":99,"desc":"Soul of the Stray Demon. One of the twisted souls, steeped in strength.\nUse to acquire numerous souls, or transpose to extract its true strength.\nThe Stray Demon, now lacking even a trace of flame, was once the gatekeeper of Lothric.","avail":"<p>Dropped by the Stray Demon found atop the fortress in <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 20,000 souls or transpose with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth<\/a> to create either the <a data-e=\"boulder-heave\">Boulder Heave<\/a> pyromancy or the <a data-e=\"havels-ring\">Havel's Ring<\/a>.<\/p>","transposes":[{"item":"boulder-heave","cost":null},{"item":"havels-ring","cost":"5,000 souls"}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_a_Stray_Demon"},{"id":"soul-of-a-venerable-old-hand","kind":"item","name":"Soul of a Venerable Old Hand","page":"Soul of a Venerable Old Hand","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_a_Venerable_Old_Hand.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Consume to acquire 20,000 souls.","buy":null,"sell":20000,"held":99,"desc":"Large soul found in the corpse of an old hand at war.\nUse to acquire innumerable souls.\nLet the Fire Keeper transform this sovereignless soul into a source of strength, for to be Unkindled is to be a vessel for souls.","avail":"<p>Can only be obtained in NG+ onward, where it replaces the <a data-e=\"large-soul-of-a-weary-warrior\">Large Soul of a Weary Warrior<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 20,000 souls.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_a_Venerable_Old_Hand"},{"id":"soul-of-a-weary-warrior","kind":"item","name":"Soul of a Weary Warrior","page":"Soul of a Weary Warrior","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_a_Weary_Warrior.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Consume to acquire 5,000 souls.","buy":null,"sell":5000,"held":99,"desc":"Soul found in the corpse of a battle-weary warrior.\nUse to acquire a large amount of souls.\nLet the Fire Keeper transform this sovereignless soul into a source of strength, for to be Unkindled is to be a vessel for souls.","avail":"<p>Seventeen can be found in each playthrough. Twelve are found in the base game, one in <i>Ashes of Ariandel<\/i> and four in <i><a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a><\/i>.<\/p><ul><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a><ul><li>In the plaza at the beginning of Irithyll, there is a corpse on the opposite side of the fountain near the Central Irithyll bonfire holding the item.<\/li><li>Up the first set of stairs from the bonfire towards the first Pontiff Knights, turn left and double back to enter a small alcove where it can be looted from a corpse hanging from a railing.<\/li><li>On the path to the main square below the grand cathedral, there is a path to the left that leads to the Church of Yorshka and which loops around to the side of the square. On a broken railing leading towards the shortcut to the cathedral is a corpse hanging off of a ledge overlooking a Fire Witch. The corpse holds the consumable.<\/li><li>The above Fire Witch is standing watch over a corpse holding another soul consumable.<\/li><li>On the path towards the grand cathedral from the right, shortly after the house filled with Irithyllian Slaves is a stairway leading directly to the cathedral. The item can be found on a corpse to the left of the stairway.<\/li><li>Past <a data-e=\"pontiff-sulyvahn\">Pontiff Sulyvahn<\/a>, at the start of the courtyard with Giant Slaves is a corpse in the open holding the soul item.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a><ul><li>Beyond the initial cell blocks and past the Mimic are a large group of Peasant Hollows. At the end of the hallway they are guarding is a corpse holding the consumable.<\/li><li>Found on a corpse in the sewer tunnel past the large Giant Slave. Several Hound Rats and a Basilisk trap guard the corpse.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"consumed-kings-garden\">Consumed King's Garden<\/a><ul><li>On the beginning path from the <a data-e=\"dancer-of-the-boreal-valley\">Dancer of the Boreal Valley<\/a>'s arena, a corpse before encountering a Consumed King's Knight can be found holding it.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a><ul><li>On a corpse on the roofs section, near where a spear-wielding Gargoyle appears.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"archdragon-peak\">Archdragon Peak<\/a><ul><li>At the very start of the area after arriving from <a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a>, there is a tree to the left of the path that leads to the first Man Serpent encounter of the area. The item can be found on a corpse sitting at the tree's base.<\/li><li>Past the Dragon-kin Mausoleum on the path towards the Great Belfry, it can be found on a corpse hanging from an open window located shortly before reaching the second <a data-e=\"ancient-wyvern\">Ancient Wyvern<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a><ul><li>In the village on the edge of the Snowfield guarded by Millwood Knights, it can be found on a corpse inside the first floor of the tower with the <a data-e=\"millwood-greatbow\">greatbow<\/a> archers.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-dreg-heap\">The Dreg Heap<\/a><ul><li>In the first area where the Murkmen are encountered, there is a corpse hanging from an unstable outcropping. Approaching it will break the outcropping, causing the player and the corpse to fall into the remains of the <a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a> below. The soul item can be looted from the corpse at the bottom.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a><ul><li>In the start of the swamp that comprises the Ringed City Streets, a corpse in the open is guarded by submerged White-faced Locusts. The corpse holes one of the soul consumables.<\/li><li>A corpse directly underneath the Judicator Giant patrolling the swamp holds the item.<\/li><li>Near the Ringed Knight sunken chapel is a sunken spire guarded by two White-faced Locusts, it can be found on a corpse hanging off of the spire.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 5,000 souls.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_a_Weary_Warrior"},{"id":"soul-of-an-intrepid-hero","kind":"item","name":"Soul of an Intrepid Hero","page":"Soul of an Intrepid Hero","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_an_Intrepid_Hero.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Consume to acquire 2,000 souls.","buy":null,"sell":2000,"held":99,"desc":"Soul found in the corpse of an intrepid hero.\nUse to acquire a great helping of souls.\nLet the Fire Keeper transform this sovereignless soul into a source of strength, for to be Unkindled is to be a vessel for souls.","avail":"<p>Can only be obtained in NG+ onward, where it replaces the <a data-e=\"soul-of-an-unknown-traveler\">Soul of an Unknown Traveler<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 2,000 souls.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_an_Intrepid_Hero"},{"id":"soul-of-an-old-hand","kind":"item","name":"Soul of an Old Hand","page":"Soul of an Old Hand","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_an_Old_Hand.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Consume to acquire 12,500 souls.","buy":null,"sell":12500,"held":99,"desc":"Soul found in the corpse of an old hand at war.\nUse to acquire innumerable souls.\nLet the Fire Keeper transform this sovereignless soul into a source of strength, for to be Unkindled is to be a vessel for souls.","avail":"<p>Can only be obtained in NG+ onward, where it replaces the <a data-e=\"soul-of-a-weary-warrior\">Soul of a Weary Warrior<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 12,500 souls.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_an_Old_Hand"},{"id":"soul-of-an-unknown-traveler","kind":"item","name":"Soul of an Unknown Traveler","page":"Soul of an Unknown Traveler","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_an_Unknown_Traveler.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Consume to acquire 800 souls.","buy":null,"sell":800,"held":99,"desc":"Soul found in the corpse of an unknown traveler.\nUse to acquire souls.\nLet the Fire Keeper transform this sovereignless soul into a source of strength, for to be Unkindled is to be a vessel for souls.","avail":"<p>A minimum of eight are guaranteed to the player per playthrough.<\/p><ul><li><a data-e=\"cemetery-of-ash\">Cemetery of Ash<\/a><ul><li>At the far end of the side area guarded by the Ravenous Crystal Lizard.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a><ul><li>To the side of the wide-open area where the Evangelist preaches before the burning tree. To the left are a large number of explosive barrels which hide a corpse that holds the item.<\/li><li>Above the Cliff Underside area, where <a data-e=\"cornyx-of-the-great-swamp\">Cornyx of the Great Swamp<\/a> is encountered. In the wide-open area where Peasant Hollows throw <a data-e=\"firebomb\">Firebombs<\/a> and a Hollow Manservant holding a pot guards the path, there is a corpse pinned under a torture rack that is holding the consumable.<\/li><li>On the path to the Dilapidated Bridge, there is an Evangelist that will cast <a data-e=\"gnaw\">Gnaw<\/a> from very long range down a narrow road. To the right of the road at the start are some destructible barrels and crates that lead to a secret side path to avoid this barrage. Before a drop-down to the lower section of the road is a corpse holding the item.<\/li><li>On a corpse within the underground catacombs area that is accessed with the <a data-e=\"grave-key\">Grave Key<\/a>. The corpse is located deep within the catacombs and is guarded by numerous skeletons.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Road of Sacrifices<\/a><ul><li>Shortly after the Road of Sacrifices bonfire, it can be looted from a corpse next to the overturned carriage at the beginning of the path leading towards the Halfway Fortress area.<\/li><li>In the Crucifixion Woods area, after leaving the Halfway Fortress bonfire there is a series of small drop-downs to the right that can be traversed instead of the sloping path guarded by Lycanthrope Hunters. On the second drop-down there is a corpse that holds the item.<\/li><li>Past the Crucifixion Woods bonfire, instead of entering the ruins that lead to the <a data-e=\"crystal-sage\">Crystal Sage<\/a> take the path to the right. There is a corpse in the open that can be looted for the soul, however it is also guarded by a Lycanthrope.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"catacombs-of-carthus\">Catacombs of Carthus<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Giant Hound Rats.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"smouldering-lake\">Smouldering Lake<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Hound Rats.<\/li><li>Dropped by Giant Hound Rats.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Hound Rats.<\/li><li>Dropped by Giant Hound Rats.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by White-faced Locusts.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 800 souls.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_an_Unknown_Traveler"},{"id":"soul-of-the-blood-of-the-wolf","kind":"item","name":"Soul of the Blood of the Wolf","page":"Soul of the Blood of the Wolf","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_the_Blood_of_the_Wolf.webp","sub":"Boss soul","usage":"• Consume for 20,000 souls. • Transpose for Farron Greatsword. • Transpose for Wolf Knight's Greatsword.","buy":null,"sell":20000,"held":99,"desc":"Soul of the Blood of the Wolf. One of the twisted souls, steeped in strength.\nUse to acquire numerous souls, or transpose to extract its true strength.\nThe blood was spread amongst the Abyss Watchers, and their souls are one with the soul of the wolf blood master.","avail":"<p>Obtained after defeating the <a data-e=\"abyss-watchers\">Abyss Watchers<\/a> in the <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 20,000 souls or transpose with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth<\/a> to create either the <a data-e=\"farron-greatsword\">Farron Greatsword<\/a> or the <a data-e=\"wolf-knights-greatsword\">Wolf Knight's Greatsword<\/a>.<\/p>","transposes":[{"item":"farron-greatsword","cost":null},{"item":"wolf-knights-greatsword","cost":"10,000 souls"}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_the_Blood_of_the_Wolf"},{"id":"soul-of-the-dancer","kind":"item","name":"Soul of the Dancer","page":"Soul of the Dancer","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_the_Dancer.webp","sub":"Boss soul","usage":"• Consume for 10,000 souls. • Transpose for Soothing Sunlight. • Transpose for Dancer's Enchanted Swords.","buy":null,"sell":10000,"held":99,"desc":"Soul of the dancer.\nOne of the twisted souls, steeped in strength.\nUse to acquire many souls, or transpose to extract its true strength.\nThe Pontiff Sulyvahn bestowed a double-slashing sword upon a distant daughter of the formal royal family, ordering her to serve first as a dancer, and then as an outrider knight, the equivalent to exile.","avail":"<p>Obtained upon defeating the <a data-e=\"dancer-of-the-boreal-valley\">Dancer of the Boreal Valley<\/a> in the <a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">High Wall of Lothric<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 10,000 souls or transpose with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth<\/a> to create either the <a data-e=\"soothing-sunlight\">Soothing Sunlight<\/a> miracle or the <a data-e=\"dancers-enchanted-swords\">Dancer's Enchanted Swords<\/a>.<\/p>","transposes":[{"item":"soothing-sunlight","cost":"5,000 souls"},{"item":"dancers-enchanted-swords","cost":null}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_the_Dancer"},{"id":"soul-of-the-deacons-of-the-deep","kind":"item","name":"Soul of the Deacons of the Deep","page":"Soul of the Deacons of the Deep","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_the_Deacons_of_the_Deep.webp","sub":"Boss soul","usage":"• Consume for 20,000 souls. • Transpose for Deep Soul. • Transpose for Cleric's Candlestick.","buy":null,"sell":20000,"held":99,"desc":"Soul of the Deacons of the Deep.\nOne of the twisted souls, steeped in strength.\nUse to acquire numerous souls, or transpose to extract its true strength.\nAfter Aldrich left for the Boreal valley, Archdeacon Royce remained in the cathedral with the high priests, to keep eternal watch over their master's coffin.","avail":"<p>Obtained after defeating the <a data-e=\"deacons-of-the-deep\">Deacons of the Deep<\/a> in the <a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 20,000 souls or transpose with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth<\/a> to create either the <a data-e=\"deep-soul\">Deep Soul<\/a> or the <a data-e=\"clerics-candlestick\">Cleric's Candlestick<\/a>.<\/p>","transposes":[{"item":"deep-soul","cost":null},{"item":"clerics-candlestick","cost":null}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_the_Deacons_of_the_Deep"},{"id":"soul-of-the-demon-prince","kind":"item","name":"Soul of the Demon Prince","page":"Soul of the Demon Prince","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_the_Demon_Prince.webp","sub":"Boss soul","usage":"• Consume for 20,000 souls. • Transpose for Seething Chaos. • Transpose for Demon's Scar.","buy":null,"sell":20000,"held":99,"desc":"Soul of the Demon Prince.\nOne of the twisted souls, steeped in strength.\nUse to acquire many souls, or transpose to extract its true strength.\nThe demons, birthed from a common Chaos, share almost everything between them, even the pride of their prince, and his near-faded flame.\nSo that the last demon standing may rekindle it.","avail":"<p>Obtained upon defeating the <a data-e=\"demon-prince\">Demon Prince<\/a> in <a data-e=\"the-dreg-heap\">The Dreg Heap<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 20,000 souls or transpose with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth<\/a> to create either <a data-e=\"seething-chaos\">Seething Chaos<\/a> or the <a data-e=\"demons-scar\">Demon's Scar<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_the_Demon_Prince"},{"id":"soul-of-the-lords","kind":"item","name":"Soul of the Lords","page":"Soul of the Lords","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_the_Lords.webp","sub":"Boss soul","usage":"• Consume for 20,000 souls. • Transpose for Firelink Greatsword. • Transpose for Sunlight Spear.","buy":null,"sell":20000,"held":99,"desc":"Soul of the Lords.\nOne of the twisted souls, steeped in strength.\nUse to acquire numerous souls, or transpose to extract its true strength.\nSince Lord Gwyn, the first Lord of Cinder, many exalted lords have linked the First Flame, and it is their very souls that have manifested themselves as defender of the flame.","avail":"<p>Obtained after defeating the <a data-e=\"soul-of-cinder\">Soul of Cinder<\/a> in <a data-e=\"kiln-of-the-first-flame\">Kiln of the First Flame<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 20,000 souls or transpose with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth<\/a> to create either the <a data-e=\"firelink-greatsword\">Firelink Greatsword<\/a> or the <a data-e=\"sunlight-spear\">Sunlight Spear<\/a> miracle.<\/p>","transposes":[{"item":"sunlight-spear","cost":null},{"item":"firelink-greatsword","cost":"15,000 souls"}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_the_Lords"},{"id":"soul-of-the-nameless-king","kind":"item","name":"Soul of the Nameless King","page":"Soul of the Nameless King","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_the_Nameless_King.webp","sub":"Boss soul","usage":"• Consume for 16,000 souls. • Transpose for Storm Curved Sword. • Transpose for Dragonslayer Swordspear. • Transpose for Lightning Storm.","buy":null,"sell":16000,"held":99,"desc":"Soul of the Nameless King.\nOne of the twisted souls, steeped in strength.\nUse to acquire many souls, or transpose to extract its true strength.\nThe Nameless King was once a dragon-slaying god of war, before he sacrificed everything to ally himself with the ancient dragons.","avail":"<p>Obtained by defeating the <a data-e=\"the-nameless-king\">Nameless King<\/a> in <a data-e=\"archdragon-peak\">Archdragon Peak<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 16,000 souls or transpose with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth<\/a> to create either the <a data-e=\"storm-curved-sword\">Storm Curved Sword<\/a>, the <a data-e=\"dragonslayer-swordspear\">Dragonslayer Swordspear<\/a> or the <a data-e=\"lightning-storm\">Lightning Storm<\/a> miracle.<\/p>","transposes":[{"item":"lightning-storm","cost":"5,000 souls"},{"item":"dragonslayer-swordspear","cost":"10,000 souls"},{"item":"storm-curved-sword","cost":"5,000 souls"}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_the_Nameless_King"},{"id":"soul-of-the-old-demon-king","kind":"item","name":"Soul of the Old Demon King","page":"Soul of the Old Demon King","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_the_Old_Demon_King.webp","sub":"Boss soul","usage":"• Consume for 10,000 souls. • Transpose for Old King's Great Hammer. • Transpose for Chaos Bed Vestiges.","buy":null,"sell":10000,"held":99,"desc":"Soul of the Old Demon King.\nOne of the twisted souls, steeped in strength.\nUse to acquire many souls, or transpose to extract its true strength.\nThe shriveled Old Demon King is now like a clump of burnt ash, but he is the last living witness of the Chaos of Izalith.","avail":"<p>Obtained after defeating the <a data-e=\"old-demon-king\">Old Demon King<\/a> in the <a data-e=\"smouldering-lake\">Smouldering Lake<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 10,000 souls or transpose with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth<\/a> to create either the <a data-e=\"old-kings-great-hammer\">Old King's Great Hammer<\/a> or the <a data-e=\"chaos-bed-vestiges\">Chaos Bed Vestiges<\/a>.<\/p>","transposes":[{"item":"chaos-bed-vestiges","cost":"5,000 souls"},{"item":"old-kings-great-hammer","cost":null}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_the_Old_Demon_King"},{"id":"soul-of-the-rotted-greatwood","kind":"item","name":"Soul of the Rotted Greatwood","page":"Soul of the Rotted Greatwood","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_the_Rotted_Greatwood.webp","sub":"Boss soul","usage":"• Consume to acquire 3,000 souls. • Transpose to create the Hollowslayer Greatsword. • Transpose to create Arstor's Spear.","buy":null,"sell":3000,"held":99,"desc":"Soul of the Curse-rotted Greatwood.\nOne of the twisted souls, steeped in strength.\nUse to acquire many souls, or transpose to extract its true strength.\nEver since its establishment, all manner of curses have managed to seep into the Undead Settlement. The worst of them were sealed away inside a spirit tree, but eventually the curses took their toll.","avail":"<p>Obtained after defeating the <a data-e=\"curse-rotted-greatwood\">Curse-rotted Greatwood<\/a> in the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 3,000 souls or transpose with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth<\/a> to create either the <a data-e=\"hollowslayer-greatsword\">Hollowslayer Greatsword<\/a> or <a data-e=\"arstors-spear\">Arstor's Spear<\/a>.<\/p>","transposes":[{"item":"arstors-spear","cost":"1,000 souls"},{"item":"hollowslayer-greatsword","cost":"1,000 souls"}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_the_Rotted_Greatwood"},{"id":"soul-of-the-twin-princes","kind":"item","name":"Soul of the Twin Princes","page":"Soul of the Twin Princes","img":"assets/img/Soul_of_the_Twin_Princes.webp","sub":"Boss soul","usage":"• Consume for 20,000 souls. • Transpose for Lothric's Holy Sword. • Transpose for Lorian's Greatsword.","buy":null,"sell":20000,"held":99,"desc":"Soul of the Twin Princes.\nOne of the twisted souls, steeped in strength.\nUse to acquire numerous souls, or transpose to extract its true strength.\nThe two princes rejected their duty to become Lords of Cinder, and settled down far, far away to watch the fire fade from a distance. A curse makes their souls nearly inseparable.","avail":"<p>Obtained after defeating the twin princes, <a data-e=\"lorian-elder-prince-and-lothric-younger-prince\">Lorian and Lothric<\/a>, in <a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Consume to acquire 20,000 souls or transpose with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth<\/a> to create either <a data-e=\"lothrics-holy-sword\">Lothric's Holy Sword<\/a> or <a data-e=\"lorians-greatsword\">Lorian's Greatsword<\/a>.<\/p>","transposes":[{"item":"lorians-greatsword","cost":null},{"item":"lothrics-holy-sword","cost":"5,000 souls"}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_of_the_Twin_Princes"},{"id":"spears-of-the-church-item","kind":"item","name":"Spears of the Church","page":"Spears of the Church (item)","img":"assets/img/Spears_of_the_Church__item.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Equip to join the Spears of the Church covenant.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":null,"desc":"A green-rusted ornament of young grass, the crest of Princess Filianore. Equip to join the Spears of the Church's covenant.\nThe Spears of the Church watch over the Princess' slumber, and when the church is compromised by a trespasser, the Judicator summons them as loyal spirits to eliminate the threat. (Summoned automatically while this is equipped)\nLoyal spirits summoned as Spears of the Church are granted a blessing of protection.","avail":"<p>Obtained after defeating <a data-e=\"darkeater-midir\">Darkeater Midir<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Equip to pledge oneself to the <a data-e=\"spears-of-the-church\">Spears of the Church<\/a> covenant to be summoned to another players world as a boss.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Spears_of_the_Church_(item)"},{"id":"splintering-bolt","kind":"item","name":"Splintering Bolt","page":"Splintering Bolt","img":"assets/img/Splintering_Bolt.webp","sub":"Ammunition","usage":"Deal 20 physical damage and 3 bleed build-up.","buy":280,"sell":5,"held":60,"desc":"Bolts that explode immediately after being shot.\nMakes unusual shots possible, and releases splinters that cause immense bleeding.\nThese are, after all, prototypes created by the weapon craftsman Edmond. You get get what you pay for.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 280 souls once she has been given <a data-e=\"greirats-ashes\">Greirat's Ashes<\/a>, provided that he has pillaged <a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Deals Thrust damage to the target, while also inflicting Bleed buildup. If the target is very close and is hit by the bolt before it splinters, they will take a flat 25 Bleed damage. However, once the bolt splinters, each fragment will inflict 3 Bleed damage.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Splintering_Bolt"},{"id":"stalk-dung-pie","kind":"item","name":"Stalk Dung Pie","page":"Stalk Dung Pie","img":"assets/img/Stalk_Dung_Pie.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Turns enemy toxic, but also affects user","buy":50,"sell":1,"held":5,"desc":"Dried fecal waste material, marked by a long plant stalk that was not properly digested.\nThrow behind at enemies to inflict toxin build-up, but also ups your own toxicity.\nStrictly speaking, this consists of different material than the dung pie, but waste is waste, no sense in splitting hairs.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 50 souls each, once she has been given the <a data-e=\"excrement-covered-ashes\">Excrement-covered Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Giant Slaves.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Drop behind the wielder to inflict 65 Toxic buildup but 0 damage to enemies behind the wielder, while also increasing Toxic buildup on self by 55.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Stalk_Dung_Pie"},{"id":"standard-arrow","kind":"item","name":"Standard Arrow","page":"Standard Arrow (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Standard_Arrow__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Ammunition","usage":"Deals 45 physical damage to target.","buy":10,"sell":1,"held":99,"desc":"Standard arrows used with bows.\nSimultaneously equip up to two types of arrows, and switch between them as needed.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"greirat-of-the-undead-settlement\">Greirat of the Undead Settlement<\/a> for 10 souls.<ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> at the same price once she has been given <a data-e=\"greirats-ashes\">Greirat's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li>Found as loot with a <a data-e=\"longbow\">longbow<\/a> across the bridge from the <a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">High Wall of Lothric<\/a> bonfire.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Shot with a bow, the standard arrow deals 21-45 physical damage dependent on the distance of the enemy.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Standard_Arrow_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"standard-bolt","kind":"item","name":"Standard Bolt","page":"Standard Bolt (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Standard_Bolt__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Ammunition","usage":"Deal 48 physical damage to target.","buy":30,"sell":1,"held":99,"desc":"Standard bolts used with crossbows.\nSimultaneously equip up to two types of bolts, and switch between them as needed.","avail":"<ul><li>Found as common drops from hollow soldiers.<\/li><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"greirat-of-the-undead-settlement\">Greirat of the Undead Settlement<\/a> for 30 souls each.<ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> once she has been given <a data-e=\"greirats-ashes\">Greirat's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Standard_Bolt_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"sunlight-medal","kind":"item","name":"Sunlight Medal","page":"Sunlight Medal (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Sunlight_Medal__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Used to rank up in the Warrior of Sunlight covenant.","buy":null,"sell":15,"held":99,"desc":"A medal received by members of the Warrior of Sunlight covenant for victory over the final fore when summoned. The summoner also gains the same medal.\nThe medal, engraved with the holy symbol of the sun, is slightly warm, and reminds one of the great honor of a shared victory.","avail":"<ul><li>Reward for successfully defeating a boss while in the presence of at least one phantom who is a member of the Warrior of Sunlight covenant.<\/li><li>Reward for destroying a Host of Embers as an invader via the use of the <a data-e=\"red-eye-orb\">Red Eye Orb<\/a>, where at least one invader present is a member of the Warrior of Sunlight covenant.<\/li><li><a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a><ul><li>One can be found before the fog door that leads to the <a data-e=\"dragonslayer-armour\">Dragonslayer Armour<\/a>, on a corpse next to the elevator that leads back down to the first room after <a data-e=\"dancer-of-the-boreal-valley\">Dancer of the Boreal Valley<\/a>.<\/li><li>Dropped by Lothric Knights.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Offer to the Altar of Sunlight in <a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a> to rank up in the <a data-e=\"warrior-of-sunlight\">Warrior of Sunlight<\/a> covenant.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Sunlight_Medal_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"sword-of-avowal","kind":"item","name":"Sword of Avowal","page":"Sword of Avowal","img":"assets/img/Sword_of_Avowal.webp","sub":"Key item","usage":"Ceremonial tool used to conclude Anri's questline.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Ceremonial sword of Londor.\nCannot be equipped as a weapon.\nIt is said that a rite of wedlock will presage a true Hollow lord.\nYour spouse's name is Anri, who patiently awaits a rightful lord, deep within the mausoleum.","avail":"<p>Given to the player by a Londor pilgrim outside of the Darkmoon Tomb in <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a>, just before reaching <a data-e=\"anor-londo\">Anor Londo<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Used to conclude <a data-e=\"anri-of-astora\">Anri of Astora<\/a>'s questline.<\/p><p>Interacting with Anri's body in front of Gwyn's tomb will play a cutscene where the player plunges the sword into his/her body, concluding with this the rite of wedlock that will presage the coming of a true hollow lord.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Sword_of_Avowal"},{"id":"throwing-knife","kind":"item","name":"Throwing Knife","page":"Throwing Knife (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Throwing_Knife__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Throw at enemies to inflict damage.","buy":20,"sell":10,"held":40,"desc":"Small throwing knife.\nThrow at enemies to inflict damage.\nMost items choose their wielder, and only experience can improve their effectiveness.\nTrue strength can be gained in no other way.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><ul><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"greirat-of-the-undead-settlement\">Greirat of the Undead Settlement<\/a> for 20 souls.<\/li><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> once she has been given <a data-e=\"greirats-ashes\">Greirat's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li>Can be farmed from Hollow Assassins or Devout of the Deep enemies.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Throwing_Knife_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"titanite-chunk","kind":"item","name":"Titanite Chunk","page":"Titanite Chunk (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Titanite_Chunk__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Upgrade material","usage":"Reinforces normal weapons from +6 up to +9.","buy":13000,"sell":500,"held":99,"desc":"Titanite chunk for weapon reinforcement.\nReinforces weapons to +9.\nFew records of chunks exist, and once one was discovered in Lothric, the race to locate Legendary Slabs began, but there have been no reports of success.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><ul><li>One can be obtained by trading either a <a data-e=\"black-firebomb\">Black Firebomb<\/a> or a <a data-e=\"rope-black-firebomb\">Rope Black Firebomb<\/a> with Pickle Pee (only once per playthrough).<\/li><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 13,000 souls each, once she has been given the <a data-e=\"dragon-chasers-ashes\">Dragon Chaser's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Large Hollow Soldiers.<\/li><li>Dropped by Lothric Knights.<\/li><li>Dropped by Winged Knights.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"smouldering-lake\">Smoldering Lake<\/a><ul><li>One dropped by Crystal Lizard on the path to the area where you find <a data-e=\"horace-the-hushed\">Horace<\/a><\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"consumed-kings-garden\">Consumed King's Garden<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Praying Hollow Soldiers.<\/li><li>Dropped by Pus of Man.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Gertrude's Knights.<\/li><li>Dropped by Lothric Knights.<\/li><li>Dropped by Thralls.<\/li><li>Two are found on a corpse lying on a balcony on the sixth floor, behind an <a data-e=\"lothric-knight-greatsword\">ultra greatsword<\/a>-wielding, red-eyed Lothric Knight.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"archdragon-peak\">Archdragon Peak<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Man Serpents.<\/li><li>Dropped by Giant Man Serpents.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a> (<i>AoA<\/i>)<ul><li>Dropped by Millwood Knights.<\/li><li>Dropped by Corvian Knights.<\/li><li>2 are found in the Snowy Mountain Pass.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-dreg-heap\">The Dreg Heap<\/a> (<i><a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">TRC<\/a><\/i>)<ul><li>Dropped by Harald Legion Knights.<\/li><li>Dropped by Lothric Knights.<\/li><li>3 are found in the Dreg Heap.<\/li><li>6 are found in Earthen Peak.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a> (<i><a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">TRC<\/a><\/i>)<ul><li>Dropped by Harald Legion Knights.<\/li><li>Dropped by Judicator Giants.<\/li><li>Dropped by Ringed Knights.<\/li><li>2 are found in the Mausoleum Lookout.<\/li><li>2 are found in the Ringed Inner Wall.<\/li><li>6 are found in the Ringed City Streets.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Reinforces standard weapons from +6 up to +9.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Titanite_Chunk_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"titanite-scale","kind":"item","name":"Titanite Scale","page":"Titanite Scale","img":"assets/img/Titanite_Scale.webp","sub":"Upgrade material","usage":"Reinforces soul-transposed weapons up to +4.","buy":"Varies","sell":500,"held":99,"desc":"Titanite altered by a soul.\nReinforces soul-transposed weapons to +4.\nWeapons forged by soul transposition can only be reinforced by titanite of the same kind.\nIn rare cases, crystal lizards devour souls, growing to monstrous proportion and leaving these great scales.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"cemetery-of-ash\">Cemetery of Ash<\/a><ul><li>×1 is dropped by the Ravenous Crystal Lizard found near the beginning of the level.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><ul><li>×3 are sold by <a data-e=\"greirat-of-the-undead-settlement\">Greirat<\/a> for 16,000 souls each if he survives his pillaging journey through <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a>. If he dies by any means after pillaging the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a>, <a data-e=\"greirats-ashes\">his ashes<\/a> can be given to the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a>, which will add the three Scales to her stock of wares.<\/li><li>x1 is sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 20,000 souls once she has been given the <a data-e=\"captains-ashes\">Captain's Ashes<\/a>.<ul><li>The Shrine Handmaid's stock is upgraded to infinite for the same price, once she has been given the <a data-e=\"dragon-chasers-ashes\">Dragon Chaser's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li>×4 can be obtained by trading with the <a data-e=\"nestling\">Nestling<\/a>, one of each trade per game cycle:<ul><li>×1 can be obtained by trading the <a data-e=\"blacksmith-hammer\">Blacksmith Hammer<\/a>.<\/li><li>×3 can be obtained by trading the <a data-e=\"avelyn\">Avelyn<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a><ul><li>×1 is dropped by a Ravenous Crystal Lizard. From the Cleansing Chapel, head toward the cemetery but turn right before reaching the obelisk with four praying Devouts, and follow the narrow path that leads to the chapel's annex. Make way to dry land once more and the lizard can be found sleeping right before reaching a window that leads back into the chapel.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a><ul><li>×2 are dropped by a Ravenous Crystal Lizard. From the Farron Keep Perimeter bonfire, head toward the shortcut that leads back to the swamp in the <a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Road of Sacrifices<\/a>. The lizard can be found sleeping right before it.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"smouldering-lake\">Smouldering Lake<\/a><ul><li>x1 is found on a corpse on the lowermost level, guarded by multiple Basilisks.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a><ul><li>×1 is found on a corpse. From the Pontiff Sulyvahn bonfire, head upstairs of the building past the big courtyard with many dead Giants Slaves; the body is on the back, near a ledge.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a><ul><li>×1 is dropped by the Crystal Lizard found on the lower corridor of the east wing, in front of a couple of cells with Wretches inside.<\/li><li>×2 are dropped by the Mimic found in the second cell block, in the area patrolled by several Jailers.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a><ul><li>x1 is found in a chest after defeating the Boreal Outrider Knight in the room under the left-side Lothric Wyvern.<\/li><li>x3 are dropped by a Mimic on the highest floor of the building under the right-side Lothric Wyvern.<\/li><li>x1 is found on a corpse on the balcony just past the above Mimic, guarded by two Hollow Assassins.<\/li><li>x1 is found by navigating opposite to the Pus of Man which controls the right-side Lothric Wyvern, under the Wyvern's claw.<\/li><li>x3 are found in a chest opposite the <a data-e=\"warrior-of-sunlight\">Sunlight Altar<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a><ul><li>x8 are found on individual corpses throughout the area.<ul><li>One is found on a rolling ladder to the left of the first wax pool on the second floor.<\/li><li>One is guarded by a Grand Archives Scholar inside the dark room after the first wax pool.<\/li><li>One is on top of a bookshelf immediately upon reaching the third floor. It can be reached by navigating up several staircases and dropping down to it.<\/li><li>One is in a corner guarded by a Grand Archives Scholar, on the path to the illusory wall before the Boreal Outrider Knight.<\/li><li>One is to the right of the illusory wall before the Boreal Outrider Knight, next to a ladder which leads down to the third floor.<\/li><li>x3 are found on a corpse on the rooftops, next to where <a data-e=\"greirats-ashes\">Greirat's Ashes<\/a> can be looted from his corpse.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li>x2 are dropped by a Crystal Lizard on the second floor. To reach it, drop down through a broken guardrail on the wooden bridge where the <a data-e=\"crystal-sage\">Crystal Sage<\/a> warps to on the third floor.<\/li><li>x3 are found inside a chest on the fifth floor, near the stairs guarded by Grand Archives Scholars.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"consumed-kings-garden\">Consumed King's Garden<\/a><ul><li>x1 is found in the area with Thralls and Lothric Priests, leading to the shortcut back to the start of the area.<\/li><li>x2 are found inside chests in the area after defeating <a data-e=\"oceiros-the-consumed-king\">Oceiros, the Consumed King<\/a>, and before entering the Untended Graves.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"untended-graves\">Untended Graves<\/a><ul><li>×4 are dropped by a pair of Ravenous Crystal Lizards, two Scales each, in the same area where the first Ravenous Crystal Lizard was encountered in the <a data-e=\"cemetery-of-ash\">Cemetery of Ash<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"archdragon-peak\">Archdragon Peak<\/a><ul><li>x3 are found on corpses in the balcony areas within the Dragon-Kin Mausoleum.<\/li><li>x3 are found in a chest before fighting the second <a data-e=\"ancient-wyvern\">Ancient Wyvern<\/a>.<\/li><li>×3 are dropped by the second Ancient Wyvern.<\/li><li>Dropped by Rock Lizards.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-dreg-heap\">The Dreg Heap<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Harald Legion Knights.<\/li><li>After falling into the remnants of the <a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a>, turn around and one will be on a corpse behind the landing point.<\/li><li>In the Earthen Peak area, there is a collapsed tower above and to the right of the covered path that leads from the second Angel's patrol into the swamp. A Titanite Scale can be found on a corpse inside.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Ringed Knights.<\/li><li>Dropped by Harald Legion Knights.<\/li><li>Upon being transported to the Ringed City after defeating the <a data-e=\"demon-prince\">Demon Prince<\/a>, turn around and loot the nearby corpse.<\/li><li>Dropped by a Crystal Lizard in the ruins to the right of the graveyard archer gauntlet.<\/li><li>Two can be found on corpses in the immediate area where the Iron Dragonslayer is fought in the Ringed City Streets.<\/li><li>Before crossing the bridge into the mountain pass guarded by <a data-e=\"darkeater-midir\">Darkeater Midir<\/a>, turn right to find a path that leads below the stone bridge. A Titanite Scale can be found at the turnaround point, guarded by a Ringed Knight waiting in ambush.<\/li><li>When entering the first cave to take cover from Midir's fire strafe at the mountain pass, two can be found on a corpse at the back of the cave, overlooking the chasm.<\/li><li>After dropping down to the lower level of the mountain pass, two can be found on a nearby corpse.<\/li><li>One is dropped by a Crystal Lizard in the Shared Grave area, on the other side of the collapsing stairs trap.<\/li><li>One is found on a corpse on the stone bridge where Midir attacks the player for the final time.<\/li><li>Two are dropped by another Crystal Lizard that is encountered on the stairs leading up to the statue of Gwyn, Lord of Cinder and the Furtive Pygmy.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Used to reinforce special weapons up to +4. These include all soul-transposed weapons, as well as several otherwise unique weapons.<\/p><p>Reinforcement initially costs only a single Titanite Scale, but doubles in cost for each subsequent level, requiring 8 Titanite Scales to upgrade to +4, and finally a <a data-e=\"titanite-slab\">Titanite Slab<\/a> to upgrade to +5. Fully reinforcing such a weapon requires the use of 15 Titanite Scales and one Titanite Slab. Each level of reinforcement is equal to 2 levels for a weapon upgraded through <a data-e=\"titanite-shard\">regular Titanite<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Titanite_Scale"},{"id":"titanite-shard","kind":"item","name":"Titanite Shard","page":"Titanite Shard (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Titanite_Shard__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Upgrade material","usage":"Reinforces normal weapons up to +3.","buy":null,"sell":100,"held":99,"desc":"Titanite shard for weapon reinforcement.\nReinforces weapons to +3.\nTitanite shards are fragments of\nthe Legendary Slabs. Titanite is\netched into weapons to reinforce.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">High Wall of Lothric<\/a><ul><li>Drops:<ul><li>Hollow Assassins<\/li><li>Hollow Soldiers<\/li><li>Large Hollow Soldiers<\/li><li>Lothric Knights<\/li><li>Praying Hollow Soldiers<\/li><li>Pus of Man (guaranteed drop only the first time it is defeated)<\/li><li>Winged Knight<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li>Loot:<ul><li>On a corner to the left of the Tower on the Wall bonfire.<\/li><li>Behind some barrels in an alcove of the room with three Large Hollow Soldiers and two Starved Hounds.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul><\/li><li>Dropped by Lycanthropes in <a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Road of Sacrifices<\/a>.<\/li><li>Dropped by Skeleton Swordsmen.<\/li><li>Dropped by Hound Rats.<\/li><li>Dropped by Ghrus.<\/li><li>Dropped by Demon Clerics.<\/li><li>An unlimited amount can be purchased from the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 800 souls each once she is given the <a data-e=\"dreamchasers-ashes\">Dreamchaser's Ashes<\/a> or the <a data-e=\"grave-wardens-ashes\">Grave Warden's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Upgrades normal weapons up to +3.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Titanite_Shard_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"titanite-slab","kind":"item","name":"Titanite Slab","page":"Titanite Slab (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Titanite_Slab__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Upgrade material","usage":"Reinforces any weapon to its highest level.","buy":null,"sell":1000,"held":99,"desc":"Titanite slab for weapon reinforcement, said to once belong to the gods.\nReinforces weapons to their highest level.\nTitanite slabs are smithing materials of the gods, and weapons reinforced with slabs will be admired no less than their precious legendary weapons.","avail":"<p>The number of Titanite Slabs that can be obtained in a single playthrough are limited. 8 can be found in the base game, 3 can be found in <i>Ashes of Ariandel<\/i> for a total of 11, and 4 can be found in <i><a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a><\/i> for a maximum of 15.<\/p><h4>Base Game<\/h4><table><tr><th>Slab No.<\/th><th>Directions<\/th><\/tr><tr><th><a data-e=\"profaned-capital\">Profaned Capital<\/a><\/th><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><br>Gifted by <a data-e=\"siegward-of-catarina\">Siegward of Catarina<\/a> after rescuing him from his cell. The <a data-e=\"old-cell-key\">Old Cell Key<\/a> is required to unlock the door.<\/td><\/tr><tr><th><a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a><\/th><\/tr><tr><td>2<\/td><td><br>On the third floor, below the balcony where the <a data-e=\"crystal-sage\">Crystal Sage<\/a> teleports to after engaging him at the beginning of the level and next to a wax pool, there is a lever located between two bookshelves facing the center of the Archives towards the first wax pool. Activating the lever will move a bookshelf in that area. Returning to the first wax pool and exploring the newly opened path will reveal a chest containing the Slab.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>3<\/td><td><br>Reward for defeating the three Gertrude's Knights at the very top of the Archives.<\/td><\/tr><tr><th><a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a><\/th><\/tr><tr><td>4<\/td><td><br>After unlocking the final elevator shortcut of the Grand Archives (at the end of the bridge) which leads back down to Lothric Castle, send the elevator up while standing at the bottom. The elevator will reveal itself to be a tandem elevator, boarding the bottom carriage and going down will lead to a corpse holding the Slab.<\/td><\/tr><tr><th><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><\/th><\/tr><tr><td>5<\/td><td><br>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 30,000 souls once all four <a data-e=\"cinders-of-a-lord\">Cinders of a Lord<\/a> have been placed on their respective thrones.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>6<\/td><td><br>Trade the <a data-e=\"coiled-sword-fragment\">Coiled Sword Fragment<\/a> with Pickle Pee (only once per playthrough).<\/td><\/tr><tr><th><a data-e=\"archdragon-peak\">Archdragon Peak<\/a><\/th><\/tr><tr><td>7<\/td><td><br>Found on the top of the <a data-e=\"archdragon-peak\">Great Belfry<\/a>, next to a dead <a data-e=\"ancient-wyvern\">wyvern<\/a> and guarded by Havel the Rock.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>8<\/td><td>Found on a corpse in the main courtyard after defeating <a data-e=\"the-nameless-king\">the Nameless King<\/a>.<\/td><\/tr><\/table><h4>Ashes of Ariandel<\/h4><table><tr><th>Slab No.<\/th><th>Directions<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><br>From the <a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Depths of the Painting<\/a> bonfire, turn left on the riverbed and proceed past the three Frost Crabs. Past the Birch Women in the riverbed is a unique one guarding the <a data-e=\"snap-freeze\">Snap Freeze<\/a> Sorcery. Defeating her will cause a ladder to materialize on the riverbank. Climb up to the top to claim a Slab from a corpse.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>2<\/td><td><br>Reward for defeating <a data-e=\"sister-friede\">Father Ariandel and Friede<\/a>.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>3<\/td><td>Gifted by the <a data-e=\"forlorn-corvian-settler\">Forlorn Corvian Settler<\/a> in the <a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Corvian Settlement<\/a>, after granting his wish to bring fire to the painted world by defeating Blackflame Friede. If the player has killed him, the Slab can be found at his initial meeting place.<\/td><\/tr><\/table><h4>The Ringed City<\/h4><table><tr><th>Slab No.<\/th><th>Directions<\/th><\/tr><tr><th><a data-e=\"the-dreg-heap\">The Dreg Heap<\/a><\/th><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><br>Within the poison swamp of <a data-e=\"the-dreg-heap\">Earthen Peak Ruins<\/a> guarded by the third Angel, there is a cave on the opposite side with several Poisonhorn Bugs and two Harald Legion Knights, one patrolling the cave and the second guarding the Slab in a corridor at the back. If the player reloads the area several times without retrieving it (either due to leaving or dying and respawning), <a data-e=\"amnesiac-lapp\">Amnesiac Lapp<\/a> will kill the second Harald Legion Knight and gift it to the player at the bonfire.<\/td><\/tr><tr><th><a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a><\/th><\/tr><tr><td>2<\/td><td><br>Reward for defeating Halflight, Spear of the Church for the first time.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>3<\/td><td><br>Gifted by <a data-e=\"shira-knight-of-filianore\">Shira, Knight of Filianore<\/a> after fulfilling her request of defeating <a data-e=\"darkeater-midir\">Darkeater Midir<\/a>. If the player has woken <a data-e=\"filianore\">Filianore<\/a> without obtaining this Slab, it will be dropped by Shira at Pygmy's Throne once she is defeated.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>4<\/td><td>Reward for defeating the <a data-e=\"ringed-knight-paired-greatswords\">paired greatsword<\/a>-wielding Ringed Knight at Pygmy's Throne.<\/td><\/tr><\/table>","use":"<p>Unlike in previous games, Titanite Slabs serve as the final component to upgrade all weapons to their maximum level, normal, unique, and soul-transposed weapons. It is required to upgrade a normal weapon from +9 to +10, and a unique or soul-transposed weapon from +4 to +5.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Titanite_Slab_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"tower-key","kind":"item","name":"Tower Key","page":"Tower Key (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Tower_Key__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Key item","usage":"Unlocks the bell tower behind Firelink Shrine.","buy":20000,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":99,"desc":"Key to the decrepit tower behind Firelink Shrine which leads to the Bell Tower.\nThe Bell Tower is the grave of the Fire Keepers past. When a Fire Keeper has served her purpose, she is led to true darkness, where she enjoys a long-deserved sleep.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> for 20,000 souls.<\/li><li>Dropped by <a data-e=\"irina-of-carim\">Irina of Carim<\/a> after her death.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Unlocks the gate that gives access to the decrepit bell tower behind <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Tower_Key_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"transposing-kiln","kind":"item","name":"Transposing Kiln","page":"Transposing Kiln","img":"assets/img/Transposing_Kiln.webp","sub":"Key item","usage":"Give to Ludleth, Lord of Cinder, to conduct soul transposition.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"An old transposing kiln from Courland, crafted with stitched crystal lizard hide.\nGive to Ludleth, Lord of Cinder, to conduct soul transposition.\nThis kiln can transpose twisted souls to craft special items with their concentrated essence. Deemed forbidden by those unable to make proper use of it.","avail":"<p>Received upon defeating the <a data-e=\"curse-rotted-greatwood\">Curse-rotted Greatwood<\/a> in the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Give the kiln to <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth of Courland<\/a> in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> to conduct transposition of boss souls.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Transposing_Kiln"},{"id":"twinkling-dragon-head-stone","kind":"item","name":"Twinkling Dragon Head Stone","page":"Twinkling Dragon Head Stone","img":"assets/img/Twinkling_Dragon_Head_Stone.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Gain the head of a dragon and emit breath alongside an archdragon mirage.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Stone imbued with the power of the everlasting dragons, the second of its kind, offered to a towering dragon.\nGain the head of a dragon and emit breath alongside an archdragon mirage. The transformation is irreversible until death.\nThe illusion achieved was the first case of a human imitating the form of an ancient dragon, and it revealed the smallness of human existence.\nThe road to the old dragons is long and arduous, and only one can complete the journey.","avail":"<p>Obtained by defeating <a data-e=\"hawkwood\">Hawkwood<\/a> in a duel to the death in the <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron mausoleum<\/a> at the end of his questline.<\/p>","use":"<p>Gain the head of a dragon and emit breath alongside an archdragon mirage. However, the transformation is irreversible until death.<\/p><p>The absorption values for the head piece are as follows:<\/p><ul><li>4% Magic<\/li><li>9% Fire<\/li><li>-4% Lightning<\/li><li>4% Dark<\/li><li>+15 to all status effect resistance<\/li><\/ul><p>Physical absorption remains at 0%, and all flat defenses remain penalized for the empty armor slot.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Twinkling_Dragon_Head_Stone"},{"id":"twinkling-dragon-torso-stone","kind":"item","name":"Twinkling Dragon Torso Stone","page":"Twinkling Dragon Torso Stone","img":"assets/img/Twinkling_Dragon_Torso_Stone.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Gain the torso of a dragon and roar alongside an archdragon mirage.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Stone imbued with the power of the everlasting dragons, offered to a towering dragon. This stone shows signs of a nascent light.\nGain the torso of a dragon and roar alongside an archdragon mirage. The transformation is irreversible until death.\nYet true imitation will require a dragon head, as well.","avail":"<p>Found at the altar erected at the top of the highest cliff in <a data-e=\"archdragon-peak\">Archdragon Peak<\/a>. Pray at the dead archdragon by performing the &quot;Path of the Dragon&quot; gesture in front of the altar to receive the item.<\/p>","use":"<p>Gain the body of a dragon and roar alongside an archdragon mirage. The transformation is irreversible until death.<\/p><p>Additionally, the player's absorption values for the chest, arms and legs pieces become as follows:<\/p><ul><li>13% Magic<\/li><li>26% Fire<\/li><li>-11% Lightning<\/li><li>13% Dark<\/li><li>+45 to all status effect resistance<\/li><\/ul><p>These are compounded with the absorption values of the associated head piece, which is also equipped by default. Physical absorption remains at 0%, and all flat defenses remain penalized for empty armor slots.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Twinkling_Dragon_Torso_Stone"},{"id":"twinkling-titanite","kind":"item","name":"Twinkling Titanite","page":"Twinkling Titanite (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Twinkling_Titanite__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Upgrade material","usage":"Reinforces soulbound weapons up to +4.","buy":"Various","sell":500,"held":99,"desc":"Twinkling titanite for weapon reinforcement. Reinforces soulbound weapons to +4.\nSoulbound weapons cannot be reinforced with ordinary titanite, nor can they be infused.\nUnless one uses this twinkling titanite, which reinforces these weapons without reversing their bolstered strength.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"cemetery-of-ash\">Cemetery of Ash<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by a Crystal Lizard in a secluded area beyond the <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">shrine<\/a>'s rooftop.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><ul><li>Three are sold by <a data-e=\"greirat-of-the-undead-settlement\">Greirat of the Undead Settlement<\/a> for 12,000 souls once he returns from pillaging <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a>. They will instead be sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> if she is given <a data-e=\"greirats-ashes\">his ashes<\/a> provided that Greirat dies after pillaging at least the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a>. (This is not true; giving the Handmaid his ashes after he returns from pillaging the Undead Settlement results in no twinkling titanite in her inventory).<\/li><li>Sold by the Shrine Handmaid for 15,000 souls once she has been given the <a data-e=\"dragon-chasers-ashes\">Dragon Chaser's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><li>Trade with the <a data-e=\"nestling\">Nestling<\/a>, once each per playthrough:<ul><li>One can be obtained by trading a <a data-e=\"large-leather-shield\">Large Leather Shield<\/a>.<\/li><li>One can be obtained by trading a <a data-e=\"prism-stone\">Prism Stone<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"road-of-sacrifices\">Road of Sacrifices<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by a Crystal Lizard found on a ledge below, along the road that leads from the Crystal Sage bonfire to the <a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a>.<\/li><li>Dropped by another Crystal Lizard on another ledge further below from the one mentioned above.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by a Crystal Lizard past a small river with three Corpse Grubs, on a side path located past the Cleansing Chapel.<\/li><li>Dropped by another Crystal Lizard found further from the one mentioned above, next to a Ravenous Crystal Lizard.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by a Crystal Lizard. From the Old Wolf of Farron bonfire, exit and follow the ledge by the right side of the building. The lizard is found near the corner on the backside.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"catacombs-of-carthus\">Catacombs of Carthus<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by a Crystal Lizard located on a ledge on the left side of the large room with the large staircase, just after meeting <a data-e=\"anri-of-astora\">Anri of Astora<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"smouldering-lake\">Smouldering Lake<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by a Crystal Lizard found in the tunnel that leads to <a data-e=\"horace-the-hushed\">Horace the Hushed<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by a Crystal Lizard on a small terrace past the second Fire Witch.<\/li><li>Dropped by a Crystal Lizard hidden behind an illusory wall in the first niche of the quay, just as one reaches the lake that surrounds the city.<\/li><li>Dropped by a Crystal Lizard in the small courtyard past the Pontiff Sulyvahn bonfire.<\/li><li>Dropped by another Crystal Lizard in the same area.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"profaned-capital\">Profaned Capital<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by a Crystal Lizard along the corridors that lead to the toxic swamp.<\/li><li>Dropped by another Crystal Lizard further from the one mentioned above.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a><ul><li>Found on a corpse in the room where the <a data-e=\"winged-knight-twinaxess\">axe<\/a>-wielding Winged Knight ambushes the player.<\/li><li>Two are found on a corpse in the moat before the two Lothric Wyverns, guarded by the left-side Pus of Man.<\/li><li>Two are dropped by a Crystal Lizard in the alleyway where multiple Hollow Assassins ambush the player.<\/li><li>Three are found in various chests guarded by the Boreal Outrider Knight.<\/li><li>Two are dropped by another Crystal Lizard, under the right-side Lothric Wyvern's wing.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a><ul><li>Nine are guaranteed drops from almost all Crystal Lizards found in this area.<\/li><li>Three are found inside a chest after climbing the tower guarded by Gertrude's Knights and navigating the rafters below Gertrude's cage.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"archdragon-peak\">Archdragon Peak<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by Rock Lizards.<\/li><li>Two are found in the <a data-e=\"ancient-wyvern\">Ancient Wyvern<\/a>'s arena, inside the first building cluster and down the short ladder past the second fire hazard area.<\/li><li>Two are found at the end of the Ancient Wyvern's arena, on the wooden scaffolding above the Wyvern that is used to kill it with the plunging attack.<\/li><li>Three are dropped by a Crystal Lizard on the path to the Great Belfry, before encountering the Lesser Ancient Wyvern.<\/li><li>Three are dropped by the Lesser Ancient Wyvern.<\/li><li>Three are found in a chest past the Great Belfry, guarded by a Rock Lizard at the base of the ladder leading to Havel the Rock.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by a Crystal Lizard inside the tower guarded by two Millwood Knights wielding <a data-e=\"millwood-greatbow\">greatbows<\/a> in the abandoned village. It can be found after ascending the staircase, climbing the ladder and then going down the staircase.<\/li><li>Dropped by a Crystal Lizard within the Corvian Settlement. After ascending the tower to the cliffside above the settlement, the lizard can be spotted on the next crossing, guarded by an overhanging Corvian Knight.<\/li><li>Two are dropped by a pair of Crystal Lizards within the Ariandel Chapel basement. After revealing the illusory wall that blocks the path to Crossbreed Priscilla's tower (and Livid Pyromancer Dunnel's arena), the lizards can be found in the very next room.<\/li><li>Dropped by a Crystal Lizard within the Depths of the Painting. After navigating the first set of twisted branches under the rope bridge, it can be found in the crossing that leads to the next set of twisted branches, guarded by two Farron Followers.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-dreg-heap\">The Dreg Heap<\/a><ul><li>After falling through the window into the remnants of the <a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a>, one can be found on a corpse at the other end of the room, guarded by Murkmen.<\/li><li>Two are dropped by each of the Pilgrim Pupas controlling the Angels encountered throughout the area, for a total of six.<\/li><li>After encountering the second Angel shortly after entering Earthen Peak, turn around and head towards the dead end next to the drop-down from the bonfire. Climb onto the tree root and follow it right to find a Twinkling Titanite on a corpse.<\/li><li>When traversing the great tree branches extending above Earthen Peak after defeating Desert Pyromancer Zoey, there is a drop-down to the right that hides a corpse holding a Twinkling Titanite. Following this root will lead back to the original path.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a><ul><li>Dropped by a Crystal Lizard in the Mausoleum Lookout, after jumping to the ruins to the right of the path to the Judicator Giant.<\/li><li>Found on a corpse in the spiral stair building guarded by numerous Hobbled Clerics. It can be accessed by dropping down onto the chandelier in the middle and then jumping to a hidden alcove where a Hobbled Cleric awaits.<\/li><li>Two are dropped by a Crystal Lizard at the top of the long ladder from the swamp, next to the great stairway guarded by Harald Knights. It will attempt to lead the player into an ambush of two Ringed Knights.<\/li><li>One is found in the swamp on the left-hand side, on a corpse guarded by a White-faced Locust.<\/li><li>One is found in the back end of the sunken building guarded by four Ringed Knights, before dropping down to the area leading to <a data-e=\"darkeater-midir\">Darkeater Midir<\/a>'s crossing.<\/li><li>One is dropped by a Crystal Lizard within the Shared Grave area, on the other side of the collapsing stair trap.<\/li><li>Two are found on a corpse in front of the Church of Filianore.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Allows reinforcement of unique weapons up to +4.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Twinkling_Titanite_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"undead-bone-shard","kind":"item","name":"Undead Bone Shard","page":"Undead Bone Shard","img":"assets/img/Undead_Bone_Shard.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Increases the amount of HP recovered from drinking from the Estus Flask.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":99,"desc":"Undead bones that yet burn.\nCast it into the shrine bonfire to boost the recovery provided by the Estus Flask.\nThe bonfire's cinders are bones of Undead, and a bone that still burns is a fresh cinder indeed. Before feeding upon death, one must first pray to it.","avail":"<p>A total of ten Undead Bone Shards can be collected in a single game cycle.<\/p><table><tr><th>Shard No.<\/th><th>Directions<\/th><\/tr><tr><th><a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a><\/th><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td>From the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Dilapidated Bridge<\/a>, head toward the cemetery. The shard can be collected from a corpse lying on a segment of floor separated from the cliff and to the right. It is advisable to befriend the <a data-e=\"giant-archer-of-the-undead-settlement\">giant archer<\/a> before attempting to get it, though, as the blasts produced by his arrows could send the player into the chasm.<\/td><\/tr><tr><th><a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a><\/th><\/tr><tr><td>2<\/td><td>Found on top of a gravestone protruding outside the cliff, in the small graveyard located in front of the cathedral. The area is inhabited by several Infested Corpses. If the player befriended the <a data-e=\"giant-archer-of-the-undead-settlement\">giant archer<\/a> in the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a>, he will lend a hand in clearing this area by shooting arrows.<\/td><\/tr><tr><th><a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a><\/th><\/tr><tr><td>3<\/td><td>Inside a small structure found to the right of both the main gate and the <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Keep Ruins<\/a> bonfire. The building is infested by a large group of Rotten Slugs, so clearing the area with ranged attacks is recommended before even attempting to pick up the shard.<\/td><\/tr><tr><th><a data-e=\"catacombs-of-carthus\">Catacombs of Carthus<\/a><\/th><\/tr><tr><td>4<\/td><td>Found within the first Skeleton Boulder that rolls up and down the big staircase. In order to obtain the shard, the player must first kill the hooded skeleton controlling it; the boulder will keep rolling one last time and release the shard upon crashing onto a wall and breaking apart.<\/td><\/tr><tr><th><a data-e=\"smouldering-lake\">Smouldering Lake<\/a><\/th><\/tr><tr><td>5<\/td><td>Automatically obtained upon defeating the Carthus Sand Worm.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>6<\/td><td>Found in the long hallway inhabited by two Demon Clerics after coming from the <a data-e=\"smouldering-lake\">Demon Ruins<\/a> bonfire. The shard can be obtained from a corpse lying at the far end corner of this hallway. Special care must be taken before looting the corpse, though, as a Writhing Rotten Flesh will attempt to fall from the ceiling and onto the player if not dealt with first.<\/td><\/tr><tr><th><a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a><\/th><\/tr><tr><td>7<\/td><td>Found outside the <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Church of Yorshka<\/a>, behind a large tombstone guarded by a red-eyed Corvian. If the player aided <a data-e=\"sirris-of-the-sunless-realms\">Sirris<\/a> in defeating Creighton at the beginning of the level, he will invade as a dark spirit in this area.<\/td><\/tr><tr><th><a data-e=\"profaned-capital\">Profaned Capital<\/a><\/th><\/tr><tr><td>8<\/td><td>Found on Laddersmith Gilligan's corpse (along with the Stretch Out gesture) next to the <a data-e=\"profaned-capital\">first<\/a> bonfire.<\/td><\/tr><tr><th><a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a><\/th><\/tr><tr><td>9<\/td><td>From the <a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Dragon Barracks<\/a>, head toward the bridge with the two Wyverns and drop just before reaching the other side to land on a ledge with a corpse holding the shard.<\/td><\/tr><tr><th><a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a><\/th><\/tr><tr><td>10<\/td><td>The shard can be looted from a corpse sitting on a chair on a ledge above the area with four Scholars on the sixth floor of the library. This ledge can only be reached by entering through a broken window accessible after coming from the roofs section.<\/td><\/tr><\/table>","use":"<p>Cast into the <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> bonfire to boost the recovery provided by the <a data-e=\"estus-flask\">Estus Flask<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Undead_Bone_Shard"},{"id":"undead-hunter-charm","kind":"item","name":"Undead Hunter Charm","page":"Undead Hunter Charm","img":"assets/img/Undead_Hunter_Charm.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Blocks Estus recovery within a limited area.","buy":500,"sell":100,"held":5,"desc":"Tool used to hunt down the Undead.\nBlocks Estus recovery within a limited area.\nUsed long ago by Lloyd's cleric knights on their Undead hunts. Although Allfather Lloyd is long forgotten by the Way of White, his hunts have lived on, and this charm allows one to challenge Undead without fear of tenacious healing.","avail":"<p><a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">High Wall of Lothric<\/a><\/p><ul><li>Two can be found in a side room after climbing down from the rooftops and before the second Lothric Knight, who wields a <a data-e=\"lothric-knight-long-spear\">spear<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><p><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><\/p><ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 500 souls once she has been given the <a data-e=\"paladins-ashes\">Paladin's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><p><a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a><\/p><ul><li>Dropped by Man-grubs.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Upon use, an Undead Hunter Charm is thrown to the ground, releasing a white cloud that affects anyone that is hit by it. Affected targets will have a debuff applied to them that prevents them from using their <a data-e=\"estus-flask\">Estus Flask<\/a> for 25 seconds. Healing Miracles may still be cast, however.<\/p><p>They may also be thrown at Mimics, forcing them to go into a sleeping state after which they can be looted safely. This effect can be used on Mimics in any state, whether they are waiting for prey or are actively attacking the player, and can be re-applied any number of times, dependent on the number of Undead Hunter Charms being carried.<\/p><p>When thrown at glowing-eyed Skeletons in <a data-e=\"catacombs-of-carthus\">Catacombs of Carthus<\/a>, it will prevent them from reanimating, allowing them to be killed the first time around.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Undead_Hunter_Charm"},{"id":"vertebra-shackle","kind":"item","name":"Vertebra Shackle","page":"Vertebra Shackle","img":"assets/img/Vertebra_Shackle.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Used to rank up in the Mound-makers covenant.","buy":null,"sell":6,"held":99,"desc":"A special bone collected by members of the covenant of Mound-makers, discovered in the corpses of their victims.\nOnly one such bone is found in the vertebrae, and the Mound-makers believe it to be a shackle of the gods. In their minds, each victim is another connection, an addition to the family.","avail":"<p>Single player:<\/p><ul><li>Defeat <a data-e=\"holy-knight-hodrick\">Holy Knight Hodrick<\/a> when he invades near the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Dilapidated Bridge<\/a> bonfire.<\/li><li>Dropped by Skeleton Swordsmen (rare).<\/li><\/ul><p>Online gameplay:<\/p><ul><li>Fulfill duty while invading as a mad dark spirit. This can be done by defeating the Host of Embers, or by defeating enough phantoms of any affiliation.<\/li><li>Defeat an invading mad dark spirit as any affiliation.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Used to rank up in the <a data-e=\"mound-makers\">Mound-makers<\/a> covenant.&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Once per game cycle, one can be traded with the <a data-e=\"nestling\">Nestling<\/a> in exchange for Lucatiel's Mask.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Vertebra_Shackle"},{"id":"warrior-of-sunlight-item","kind":"item","name":"Warrior of Sunlight","page":"Warrior of Sunlight (item)","img":"assets/img/Warrior_of_Sunlight__item.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Equip to join the Warrior of Sunlight covenant.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":null,"desc":"An ancient talisman depicting a holy symbol bestowed upon the Warriors of Sunlight. Equip to pledge oneself to the Warrior of Sunlight covenant.\nWarriors of Sunlight are brilliantly beaming co-operators who place their golden signatures to help those in need, for it is their duty to deliver a great conquest to their summoner.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a>.<\/p><p>From the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a> bonfire, proceed through the level until reaching a big open area with several praying peasants and an Evangelist. Head to the house on the far left and turn right upon entering. Drop through a hole on the floor partially concealed behind some crates to reach a small kitchen with the talisman and a pot with <a data-e=\"estus-flask\">estus soup<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Equip to pledge oneself to the <a data-e=\"warrior-of-sunlight\">Warrior of Sunlight<\/a> covenant.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Warrior_of_Sunlight_(item)"},{"id":"watchdogs-of-farron-item","kind":"item","name":"Watchdogs of Farron","page":"Watchdogs of Farron (item)","img":"assets/img/Watchdogs_of_Farron__item.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Equip to join the Watchdogs of Farron covenant.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":null,"desc":"Ancient medallion depicting the crest of a wolf. Symbolizes the pact with the Old Wolf of Farron. Equip to pledge oneself to the Watchdogs of Farron.\nThe Watchdogs ensure that the warriors sleep in serenity, by taking the form of loyal spirits and hunting down those who would trespass the woods of Farron.\nSummoning takes place automatically while this is equipped.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a>. Obtained by interacting with the Old Wolf of Farron altar in the ruined fortress and accepting to join the <a data-e=\"watchdogs-of-farron\">Watchdogs of Farron<\/a> covenant.<\/p>","use":"<p>Equip to pledge oneself to the <a data-e=\"watchdogs-of-farron\">Watchdogs of Farron<\/a> covenant. Summoning takes place automatically while this item is equipped.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Watchdogs_of_Farron_(item)"},{"id":"way-of-blue-item","kind":"item","name":"Way of Blue","page":"Way of Blue (item)","img":"assets/img/Way_of_Blue__item.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Equip to join the Way of Blue covenant.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":null,"desc":"Pale blue sheepskin parchment featuring an illustration of the moon, symbol of an ancient accord.\nMembers of the Way of Blue are the beneficiaries of an ancient accord. When a dark spirit threatens them, a blue spirit will grant them assistance, and help to root out the invader.\nSummoning takes place automatically while this is equipped.","avail":"<ul><li><a data-e=\"high-wall-of-lothric\">High Wall of Lothric<\/a><ul><li>Gifted by <a data-e=\"emma-high-priestess-of-lothric-castle\">Emma, High Priestess of Lothric Castle<\/a> in the cathedral opposite to <a data-e=\"vordt-of-the-boreal-valley\">Vordt of the Boreal Valley<\/a>'s boss arena, when talking to her after obtaining the <a data-e=\"small-lothric-banner\">Small Lothric Banner<\/a>.<\/li><li>Dropped by Emma if she is killed by the player.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Equip to pledge oneself to the <a data-e=\"way-of-blue\">Way of Blue<\/a> covenant. Summoning takes place automatically while this item is equipped.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Way_of_Blue_(item)"},{"id":"way-of-white-circlet","kind":"item","name":"Way of White Circlet","page":"Way of White Circlet","img":"assets/img/Way_of_White_Circlet.webp","sub":"Online item","usage":"Restores connection to other worlds.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":99,"desc":"Online play item.\nRestore the connection to other worlds.\nThose who engage in unjust deeds when in contact with other worlds will lose their connection to them.\nWay of White Circlets assume such sin as their own, but are found few and far between. Acting without honor will never be without risk.","avail":"<p>A single circlet is included within the player's inventory at the beginning of the game. A new Way of White Circlet can be found in the beginning grave in <a data-e=\"cemetery-of-ash\">Cemetery of Ash<\/a> after an unknown number of gameplay hours, once the previous one has been consumed.<\/p>","use":"<p>If a player disconnects from a PvP session too many times, their online matchmaking will be disabled. Using the Way of White Circlet restores the player's connection to other worlds.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Way_of_White_Circlet"},{"id":"white-sign-soapstone","kind":"item","name":"White Sign Soapstone","page":"White Sign Soapstone (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/White_Sign_Soapstone__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Online item","usage":"Creates a co-op summon sign.","buy":500,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":99,"desc":"Online play item.\nCreate a co-op summon sign.\nBe summoned to another world as a phantom through your sign, and defeat the area boss to gain the strength of flame.\nThe nature of Lothric is murky, unclear.\nThe White Sign Soapstone allows Unkindled to assist one another.","avail":"<p>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> for 500 souls.<\/p>","use":"<p>Lays a white summon sign on the ground. A Host of Embers may interact with this sign to summon the sign's owner into their world.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/White_Sign_Soapstone_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"wolfs-blood-swordgrass","kind":"item","name":"Wolf's Blood Swordgrass","page":"Wolf's Blood Swordgrass","img":"assets/img/Wolf_s_Blood_Swordgrass.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Used to rank up in the Watchdogs of Farron covenant.","buy":null,"sell":10,"held":99,"desc":"A leaf signifying a duty fulfilled by the Watchdogs of Farron, who stand beside the old wolf to ensure the serenity of those at rest. Depicts a swordgrass leaf stained with dried blood.\nLong ago, the swordgrass leaf quietly identified members of the Undead Legion. In the rotted forest rest the spirits of warriors past, their acceptance of and gratitude toward their guardians is expressed eloquently by the humble leaf.","avail":"<ul><li>Dropped by all variants of Ghrus in <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a>.<\/li><li>Rewarded for successfully destroying a Host of Embers when summoned to defend <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a> as a <a data-e=\"watchdogs-of-farron\">Watchdog of Farron<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Offered to the <a data-e=\"old-wolf-of-farron\">Old Wolf of Farron<\/a> in <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a> to rank up in the <a data-e=\"watchdogs-of-farron\">Watchdogs of Farron<\/a> covenant.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Wolf's_Blood_Swordgrass"},{"id":"wood-arrow","kind":"item","name":"Wood Arrow","page":"Wood Arrow (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Wood_Arrow__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Ammunition","usage":"Deals 30 physical damage to target.","buy":5,"sell":1,"held":99,"desc":"Inexpensive wooden arrows.\nWeaker arrows that can be easily purchased in bulk.\nSimultaneously equip up to two types of arrows, and switch between them as needed.","avail":"<p>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 5 souls each.<\/p>","use":"<p>Deals 30 physical damage upon impact to an enemy.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Wood_Arrow_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"wood-bolt","kind":"item","name":"Wood Bolt","page":"Wood Bolt (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Wood_Bolt__Dark_Souls_III.webp","sub":"Ammunition","usage":"Deals 38 physical damage to target.","buy":10,"sell":1,"held":99,"desc":"Inexpensive wooden bolts.\nWeaker bolts that can be easily purchased in bulk.\nSimultaneously equip up to two types of bolts, and switch between them as needed.","avail":"<p>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 10 souls each.<\/p>","use":"<p>Deals 38 physical damage upon impact.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Wood_Bolt_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"xanthous-ashes","kind":"item","name":"Xanthous Ashes","page":"Xanthous Ashes","img":"assets/img/Xanthous_Ashes.webp","sub":"Merchant ashes","usage":"Give to the Shrine Handmaid to increase her inventory.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Umbral ash of a sorcerer who explored the golden sorceries of a long-lost land. With this, the shrine handmaid will prepare new items.\nThey were called xanthous scholars, but some foolishly imitate them by simply dressing in yellow.","avail":"<p>Found within a cell in the <a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a>. The cell is found in the final cell block with the seven Jailers patrolling it, just before the <a data-e=\"profaned-capital\">Profaned Capital<\/a>. They belonged to a Xanthous Scholar, and unlock items connected to the Xanthous and Oolacile.<\/p>","use":"<p>Extends the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a>'s inventory to include the following items:<\/p><table><tr><th>Available<\/th><th>Item<\/th><th>Cost<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"gold-pine-resin\">Gold Pine Resin<\/a><\/td><td>1,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"gold-pine-bundle\">Gold Pine Bundle<\/a><\/td><td>600<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"young-white-branch\">Young White Branch<\/a><\/td><td>1,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td>Xanthous Gloves<\/td><td>7,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td>Xanthous Overcoat<\/td><td>10,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td>Xanthous Trousers<\/td><td>7,000<\/td><\/tr><\/table>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Xanthous_Ashes"},{"id":"yellow-bug-pellet","kind":"item","name":"Yellow Bug Pellet","page":"Yellow Bug Pellet","img":"assets/img/Yellow_Bug_Pellet.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Boosts Lightning damage absorption for 60 seconds.","buy":1500,"sell":200,"held":5,"desc":"Medicinal pellet made from crushed insects. The yellow type temporarily boosts lightning damage absorption.\nThe grave wardens of Carthus used these to repel a great sand worm.\nThe worm tumbled into the catacombs, and proceeded to dominate its new home in the Smoldering Lake.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 1,500 souls each once she is given the <a data-e=\"grave-wardens-ashes\">Grave Warden's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><li>Dropped by Skeletons and Skeleton Swordsmen in the <a data-e=\"catacombs-of-carthus\">Catacombs of Carthus<\/a> and <a data-e=\"smouldering-lake\">Smouldering Lake<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Boosts Lightning damage absorption by 15% for 60 seconds, 10% in PvP.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Yellow_Bug_Pellet"},{"id":"young-grass-dew","kind":"item","name":"Young Grass Dew","page":"Young Grass Dew","img":"assets/img/Young_Grass_Dew.webp","sub":"Key item","usage":"Increases damage absorption and stamina regeneration.","buy":null,"sell":null,"held":null,"desc":"A small, transparent stone that once graced the green young grass crest.\nThis semi-precious gem honors a Spear of Church after a battle well-fought, and is said to slightly enhance their blessing of protection. (while held, this effect is constant)","avail":"<p>Obtained as a reward for reaching Rank 1 in the <a data-e=\"spears-of-the-church\">Spears of the Church<\/a> covenant. To achieve this, the player must offer 10 <a data-e=\"filianores-spear-ornament\">Filianore's Spear Ornaments<\/a> to the Divine Spear Monument in the <a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">Ringed City<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Slightly increases damage absorption and stamina regeneration.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Young_Grass_Dew"},{"id":"young-white-branch","kind":"item","name":"Young White Branch","page":"Young White Branch","img":"assets/img/Young_White_Branch.webp","sub":"Consumable","usage":"Allows the player to transform into an object that suits their current environment and blend with it.","buy":null,"sell":100,"held":10,"desc":"A young white branch.\nUse to transform into something that blends in to the surroundings.\nLittle Dusk's first sorcerer's staff eventually became a seedling, and then three white birch saplings. The young branch is said to still contain echoes of little Dusk's capriciousness.","avail":"<ul><li>×1 can be chosen as a burial gift at the beginning of the game.<\/li><li><a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a><ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 1,000 souls each, once she has been given the <a data-e=\"xanthous-ashes\">Xanthous Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Undead Settlement<\/a><ul><li>×3 can be found around the white birch at the graveyard past the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Dilapidated Bridge<\/a>.<\/li><li>×1 is presented to the player as a &quot;token of friendship&quot; by the <a data-e=\"giant-archer-of-the-undead-settlement\">giant archer<\/a>. If the giant turns hostile once more, he will present another branch each time he is befriended.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a><ul><li>×3 can be found near the white birch at the small graveyard located in front of the cathedral.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a><ul><li>×2 can be found in the poison swamp, near another white birch located to the left of the <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Keep Ruins<\/a> bonfire (if looking toward the main gate). The area is comprised of deep water and is guarded by a Great Crab.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a><ul><li>One is found in the Corvian Settlement, to the right of the building where <a data-e=\"sir-vilhelm\">Sir Vilhelm<\/a> is fought. it is guarded by a lone Birch Woman.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li><a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a><ul><li>Three are found in the Ringed City Streets, at the base of a white birch at the far end of the swamp guarded by numerous Hobbled Clerics.<\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Allows the player to transform into an object that suits their current environment and blend with it, much like the <a data-e=\"chameleon\">Chameleon<\/a> sorcery.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Young_White_Branch"},{"id":"yurias-ashes","kind":"item","name":"Yuria's Ashes","page":"Yuria's Ashes","img":"assets/img/Yuria_s_Ashes.webp","sub":"Merchant ashes","usage":"Give to the Shrine Handmaid to increase her inventory.","buy":null,"sell":"Cannot be sold","held":1,"desc":"Umbral ash of Yuria of Londor. With this, the shrine handmaid will prepare new items.\nHaving three founders of the Black Church ensured Yuria's legacy would survive. Her two sisters could carry the torch, making certain their lord claims the flame, for the sake of all Hollows.","avail":"<p>Dropped by <a data-e=\"yuria-of-londor\">Yuria of Londor<\/a> upon her death.<\/p><p>Completing Yuria's questline by defeating the <a data-e=\"soul-of-cinder\">Soul of Cinder<\/a> with her as a summon, and her surviving to the end of the battle, will only award players with <a data-e=\"darkdrift\">Darkdrift<\/a> and the <a data-e=\"black-set\">Black Set<\/a>, her ashes cannot be obtained after this point.<\/p><p>The easiest way kill Yuria is after performing the marriage ceremony with <a data-e=\"anri-of-astora\">Anri of Astora<\/a>, as Yuria will not retaliate against the Lord of Hollow's attacks.<\/p>","use":"<p>Extends the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a>'s inventory to include items initially sold by <a data-e=\"yuria-of-londor\">Yuria<\/a>, as well as the <a data-e=\"black-set\">Black Set<\/a>.<\/p><table><tr><th>Available<\/th><th>Item<\/th><th>Cost<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"dark-hand\">Dark Hand<\/a><\/td><td>12,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"heavy-soul-arrow\">Heavy Soul Arrow<\/a><\/td><td>2,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"londor-braille-divine-tome\">Londor Braille Divine Tome<\/a><\/td><td>50<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"magic-shield\">Magic Shield<\/a><\/td><td>4,500<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"magic-weapon\">Magic Weapon<\/a><\/td><td>4,500<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"poison-throwing-knife\">Poison Throwing Knife<\/a><\/td><td>100<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>∞<\/td><td><a data-e=\"purging-stone\">Purging Stone<\/a><\/td><td>4,500<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>3<\/td><td><a data-e=\"ring-of-sacrifice\">Ring of Sacrifice<\/a><\/td><td>5,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"soul-arrow\">Soul Arrow<\/a><\/td><td>1,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"soul-greatsword\">Soul Greatsword<\/a><\/td><td>5,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"untrue-dark-ring\">Untrue Dark Ring<\/a><\/td><td>5,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td><a data-e=\"untrue-white-ring\">Untrue White Ring<\/a><\/td><td>5,000<\/td><\/tr><\/table>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Yuria's_Ashes"}]);
